      <data key="v_content">you all</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-c41a061ea67436660e6148138742adb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1223">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-df6b4bb8c5e93db0d296a19b0efc06f2</data>
      <data key="v_content">you can t pretend he s not careless</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-df6b4bb8c5e93db0d296a19b0efc06f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1224">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-60bd8f917e5b3e93965b501eee400d70</data>
      <data key="v_content">you d like one</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-60bd8f917e5b3e93965b501eee400d70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1225">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-be28533b2db0506178ea80ebe0208ffd</data>
      <data key="v_content">you don t forget your name</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-be28533b2db0506178ea80ebe0208ffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1226">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-ed27f23fe712d53b51e11397f51b72aa</data>
      <data key="v_content">you know who</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-ed27f23fe712d53b51e11397f51b72aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1227">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-b82ad381e6494626abd658595e8e0f4b</data>
      <data key="v_content">you ll enjoy yourself with that oaf</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-b82ad381e6494626abd658595e8e0f4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1228">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-d4ed2825d00bef3cc0379262ab428715</data>
      <data key="v_content">you re</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-d4ed2825d00bef3cc0379262ab428715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1229">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-b280e943176398f6d1a060c31ae69a88</data>
      <data key="v_content">you re going out again</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-b280e943176398f6d1a060c31ae69a88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1230">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-9b85ce047a97aadff31d425b52939f25</data>
      <data key="v_content">you re worth twelve of malfoy</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-9b85ce047a97aadff31d425b52939f25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1231">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-c16946b8cba97e8cc9d1ff90a1809406</data>
      <data key="v_content">you went to live with muggles</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-c16946b8cba97e8cc9d1ff90a1809406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1232">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-fe3b08290c0a61922e8ed14099a2152e</data>
      <data key="v_content">you were lucky</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-fe3b08290c0a61922e8ed14099a2152e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1233">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-d5e28e61ae5bf9f3be514984d0b7d392</data>
      <data key="v_content">you were up in the astronomy tower</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-d5e28e61ae5bf9f3be514984d0b7d392</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1234">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-23ea6be0589d5eaedc3bd956d678b7e5</data>
      <data key="v_content">young sirius black</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-23ea6be0589d5eaedc3bd956d678b7e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1235">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-62cc0b4ebb0b57b40778179234246c38</data>
      <data key="v_content">your</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-62cc0b4ebb0b57b40778179234246c38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1236">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-ca579d7ecc639df8004c2763460b64c4</data>
      <data key="v_content">your father</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-ca579d7ecc639df8004c2763460b64c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1237">
      <data key="v_hash_id">entity-a4b1843f4032913c2607e11a1f8d9f25</data>
      <data key="v_content">youwait</data>
      <data key="v_name">entity-a4b1843f4032913c2607e11a1f8d9f25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1238">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-530ab783ee864c857ac92615914d78d7</data>
      <data key="v_content">1
Harry Potter and the Sorcerer&apos;s Stone
CHAPTER ONE
THE BOY WHO LIVED
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-530ab783ee864c857ac92615914d78d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1239">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-47efbd3f8c87e4a0aa5c1997dd13bab4</data>
      <data key="v_content">ofnumberfour,,Dursley, of number four, Privet Drive, were proud to say
that they were perfectly normal, thank you very much.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-47efbd3f8c87e4a0aa5c1997dd13bab4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1240">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7ecfa20b5198b4c63b2c5fe9dbdf7e94</data>
      <data key="v_content">They were the last
people you&apos;d expect to be involved in anything strange or mysterious,
because they just didn&apos;t hold with such nonsense.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7ecfa20b5198b4c63b2c5fe9dbdf7e94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1241">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f00f1c211c17a4938fd7f7c49115d893</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley was the director of a firm called Grunnings, which made
drills.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f00f1c211c17a4938fd7f7c49115d893</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1242">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8cbcc23a4b9ff07fc4c45d21d182fa15</data>
      <data key="v_content">,He was a big, beefy man with hardly any neck, although he did
have a very large mustache.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8cbcc23a4b9ff07fc4c45d21d182fa15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1243">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-01f202542aa1b049bcc9aa18fe18ce2b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley was thin and blonde and had
nearly twice the usual amount of neck, which came in very useful as she
spent so much of her time craning over garden fences, spying on the
neighbors.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-01f202542aa1b049bcc9aa18fe18ce2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1244">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8be4e68729e3c5c6427b58ead65d2b06</data>
      <data key="v_content">The Dursleys had a small son called Dudley and in their
opinion there was no finer boy anywhere.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8be4e68729e3c5c6427b58ead65d2b06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1245">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5187dca16d7d968d99b74d4beda04bc9</data>
      <data key="v_content">The Dursleys had everything they wanted, but they also had a secret, and
their greatest fear was that somebody would discover it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5187dca16d7d968d99b74d4beda04bc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1246">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bbb6c2f187959054570d0eadd54b1201</data>
      <data key="v_content">They didn&apos;t
think they could bear it if anyone found out about the Potters.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bbb6c2f187959054570d0eadd54b1201</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1247">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-324343dc2616e4453a63ca6009eff294</data>
      <data key="v_content">butthey,Dursley&apos;s sister, but they hadn&apos;t met for several years;
in fact, Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-324343dc2616e4453a63ca6009eff294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1248">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-07b4305afdb1335511c993b87142c43d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley pretended she didn&apos;t have a sister, because her
sister and her good-for-nothing husband were as unDursleyish as it was
possible to be.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-07b4305afdb1335511c993b87142c43d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1249">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ab95f7840d0035c25a7cbb2729e41ae2</data>
      <data key="v_content">The Dursleys shuddered to think what the neighbors would
say if the Potters arrived in the street.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ab95f7840d0035c25a7cbb2729e41ae2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1250">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6499f4922c9b7a5e43e1ab7861b08ff2</data>
      <data key="v_content">The Dursleys knew that the
Potters had a small son, too, but they had never even seen him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6499f4922c9b7a5e43e1ab7861b08ff2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1251">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bb90f463287627982b54b12822bea12d</data>
      <data key="v_content">This boy
was another good reason for keeping the Potters away; they didn&apos;t want
Dudley mixing with a child like that.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bb90f463287627982b54b12822bea12d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1252">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fa12ffbe58b3483abdc1370bbcb76e03</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley woke up on the dull, gray Tuesday our story
starts, there was nothing about the cloudy sky outside to suggest that
strange and mysterious things would soon be happening all over the
country.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fa12ffbe58b3483abdc1370bbcb76e03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1253">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4cb807a752070b486ea9076f7c01c2ad</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley hummed as he picked out his most boring tie for
work, and Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4cb807a752070b486ea9076f7c01c2ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1254">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-98281f9a24057d162b25117a02e802a2</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley gossiped away happily as she wrestled a screaming
Dudley into his high chair.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-98281f9a24057d162b25117a02e802a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1255">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9c45055e8d4a1658ac62344e9c79f32e</data>
      <data key="v_content">None of them noticed a large, tawny owl flutter past the window.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9c45055e8d4a1658ac62344e9c79f32e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1256">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-79097dc7223500cf59084cc13c894b28</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley picked up his briefcase, pecked Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-79097dc7223500cf59084cc13c894b28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1257">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3a2d3b124426bd6d60780cc991071fc6</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Dursley on the cheek, and tried to kiss Dudley good-bye but missed,
2
because Dudley was now having a tantrum and throwing his cereal at the
walls.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3a2d3b124426bd6d60780cc991071fc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1258">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a46547848096241ef7a7a70aa7996dfb</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley as he left the house.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a46547848096241ef7a7a70aa7996dfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1259">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d3405eff4f85cc6830d83729c160f0fa</data>
      <data key="v_content">He got
into his car and backed out of number four&apos;s drive.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d3405eff4f85cc6830d83729c160f0fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1260">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-774fb8ae0043a7069e937cb201239c9e</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was on the corner of the street that he noticed the first sign of
something peculiar -- a cat reading a map.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-774fb8ae0043a7069e937cb201239c9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1261">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e3b2b7a60fdfae8944e9e9ef3b37488c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley
didn&apos;t realize what he had seen -- then he jerked his head around to
look again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e3b2b7a60fdfae8944e9e9ef3b37488c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1262">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bd9a5021a311fcb930b3a2130f02c475</data>
      <data key="v_content">There was a tabby cat standing on the corner of Privet
Drive, but there wasn&apos;t a map in sight.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bd9a5021a311fcb930b3a2130f02c475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1263">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-93ff0895ca12fceb5f3ebcd44b463293</data>
      <data key="v_content">What could he have been thinking
of? It must have been a trick of the light.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-93ff0895ca12fceb5f3ebcd44b463293</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1264">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c79512f98b22db857828f242521dc9e8</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley blinked and
stared at the cat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c79512f98b22db857828f242521dc9e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1265">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2b426326c86616f48bea9fb7132276db</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley drove around the
corner and up the road, he watched the cat in his mirror.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2b426326c86616f48bea9fb7132276db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1266">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f9146b1147593cabf4c3570b67e0a2f0</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was now
reading the sign that said Privet Drive -- no, looking at the sign; cats
couldn&apos;t read maps or signs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f9146b1147593cabf4c3570b67e0a2f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1267">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-20c314fcc4d4ba1bf819dbf7748e8f60</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley gave himself a little shake and
put the cat out of his mind.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-20c314fcc4d4ba1bf819dbf7748e8f60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1268">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1834a258201b34bd5fab3d134e1dd792</data>
      <data key="v_content">As he drove toward town he thought of
nothing except a large order of drills he was hoping to get that day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1834a258201b34bd5fab3d134e1dd792</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1269">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b57c821a441e8ce64535aeb4ea35ac4e</data>
      <data key="v_content">But on the edge of town, drills were driven out of his mind by something
else.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b57c821a441e8ce64535aeb4ea35ac4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1270">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2bc655265233fa99fda6c2f658505c05</data>
      <data key="v_content">As he sat in the usual morning traffic jam, he couldn&apos;t help
noticing that there seemed to be a lot of strangely dressed people
about.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2bc655265233fa99fda6c2f658505c05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1271">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c948d3a03591bf1c3049e3f490220e9e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley couldn&apos;t bear people who dressed in
funny clothes -- the getups you saw on young people! He supposed this
was some stupid new fashion.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c948d3a03591bf1c3049e3f490220e9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1272">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-15239dc1aa6a810a6e7cc7cdeee9740c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He drummed his fingers on the steering
wheel and his eyes fell on a huddle of these weirdos standing quite
close by.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-15239dc1aa6a810a6e7cc7cdeee9740c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1273">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8b45257dd470816f0ef3fc66ed995b16</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley was
enraged to see that a couple of them weren&apos;t young at all; why, that man
had to be older than he was, and wearing an emerald-green cloak! The
nerve of him! But then it struck Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8b45257dd470816f0ef3fc66ed995b16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1274">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1cba6d3da6499c2511c0107cd8e40c08</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley that this was probably some
silly stunt -- these people were obviously collecting for something...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1cba6d3da6499c2511c0107cd8e40c08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1275">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-86e41062d382e92a2c1274fdd3faea89</data>
      <data key="v_content">The traffic moved on and a few minutes later, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-86e41062d382e92a2c1274fdd3faea89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1276">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b088b5c073821c9be1bd65e89a831fa9</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley arrived in the Grunnings parking lot, his mind back on drills.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b088b5c073821c9be1bd65e89a831fa9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1277">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5fbd88ff94e7747001995a09b6c1ef6b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley always sat with his back to the window in his office on the
ninth floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5fbd88ff94e7747001995a09b6c1ef6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1278">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fdda1e0201648cba21ffc6d176ee885b</data>
      <data key="v_content">he,If he hadn&apos;t, he might have found it harder to concentrate
on drills that morning.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fdda1e0201648cba21ffc6d176ee885b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1279">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a3f46a72185e36dc88b8a42d93f4b3b7</data>
      <data key="v_content">He didn&apos;t see the owls swoop ing past in broad
daylight, though people down in the street did; they pointed and gazed
open- mouthed as owl after owl sped overhead.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a3f46a72185e36dc88b8a42d93f4b3b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1280">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0383e5ffa420f75442e33ecc297ae3cb</data>
      <data key="v_content">Most of them had never
seen an owl even at nighttime.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0383e5ffa420f75442e33ecc297ae3cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1281">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1968c0cd0bbf7dab9d89ad22134c7c08</data>
      <data key="v_content">however,hada,Dursley, however, had a perfectly
normal, owl-free morning.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1968c0cd0bbf7dab9d89ad22134c7c08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1282">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bdb0f07fc474c41ebd699bab390ca07d</data>
      <data key="v_content">He yelled at five different people.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bdb0f07fc474c41ebd699bab390ca07d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1283">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-10982cd5c976812245670bbe6e2c1f76</data>
      <data key="v_content">He made
several important telephone calls and shouted a bit more.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-10982cd5c976812245670bbe6e2c1f76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1284">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9d8ea3189c22e82b021b36ad715447ac</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was in a
very good mood until lunchtime, when he thought he&apos;d stretch his legs
and walk across the road to buy himself a bun from the bakery.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9d8ea3189c22e82b021b36ad715447ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1285">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1f9311ff2b0b41bfb1718be15ce1ea07</data>
      <data key="v_content">3
He&apos;d forgotten all about the people in cloaks until he passed a group of
them next to the baker&apos;s.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1f9311ff2b0b41bfb1718be15ce1ea07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1286">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-122798c6eb9f444f0999f4db76328976</data>
      <data key="v_content">He eyed them angrily as he passed.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-122798c6eb9f444f0999f4db76328976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1287">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6ad9fee29af81ec03bb11844218df1be</data>
      <data key="v_content">,He didn&apos;t
know why, but they made him uneasy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6ad9fee29af81ec03bb11844218df1be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1288">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-627fe91f1af80b6f0cb91dc128c6751a</data>
      <data key="v_content">This bunch were whispering
excitedly, too, and he couldn&apos;t see a single collecting tin.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-627fe91f1af80b6f0cb91dc128c6751a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1289">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2093f3d79f8265396aeec4c2aa1d01d5</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was on
his way back past them, clutching a large doughnut in a bag, that he
caught a few words of what they were saying.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2093f3d79f8265396aeec4c2aa1d01d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1290">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-405d647b1c04bc1bcb80b819d6b72952</data>
      <data key="v_content">that&apos;sright,,&quot;The Potters, that&apos;s right, that&apos;s what I heard yes, their son, Harry&quot;
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-405d647b1c04bc1bcb80b819d6b72952</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1291">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-34bb87c496cda80f8739e947b0005154</data>
      <data key="v_content">He looked back at the
whisperers as if he wanted to say something to them, but thought better
of it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-34bb87c496cda80f8739e947b0005154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1292">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eea998c97dee21af0705a82ff8c2396e</data>
      <data key="v_content">He dashed back across the road, hurried up to his office, snapped at his
secretary not to disturb him, seized his telephone, and had almost
finished dialing his home number when he changed his mind.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eea998c97dee21af0705a82ff8c2396e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1293">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-09741928145b03c9f3ead3d9031067e9</data>
      <data key="v_content">He put the
receiver back down and stroked his mustache, thinking...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-09741928145b03c9f3ead3d9031067e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1294">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c45147d665f4a535e4334f7c705f0b76</data>
      <data key="v_content">Potter wasn&apos;t such an unusual name.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c45147d665f4a535e4334f7c705f0b76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1295">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e47981cce38aef55597be780be256340</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was sure there were
lots of people called Potter who had a son called Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e47981cce38aef55597be780be256340</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1296">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1aeacce70eb48f65858a4a25613a06a0</data>
      <data key="v_content">Come to think
of it, he wasn&apos;t even sure his nephew was called Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1aeacce70eb48f65858a4a25613a06a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1297">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b1654dcf425312375cdea1a2ff39ff30</data>
      <data key="v_content">He&apos;d never even
seen the boy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b1654dcf425312375cdea1a2ff39ff30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1298">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-711d7e3e6fe7cbd17e8df1bce0754d28</data>
      <data key="v_content">There was no point
in worrying Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-711d7e3e6fe7cbd17e8df1bce0754d28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1299">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-196b245fd018d50495d0be06aafd170b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley; she always got so upset at any mention of her
sister.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-196b245fd018d50495d0be06aafd170b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1300">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8292df1a778f75fd5b1db00c599086eb</data>
      <data key="v_content">He didn&apos;t blame her -- if he&apos;d had a sister like that...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8292df1a778f75fd5b1db00c599086eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1301">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e57bf8181e295071d69d9acc93d77624</data>
      <data key="v_content">,but all
the same, those people in cloaks...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e57bf8181e295071d69d9acc93d77624</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1302">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ee68846d38ec3318cc9df841c0922bce</data>
      <data key="v_content">He found it a lot harder to concentrate on drills that afternoon and
when he left the building at five o&apos;clock, he was still so worried that
he walked straight into someone just outside the door.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ee68846d38ec3318cc9df841c0922bce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1303">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-316a8a69e6fec16c757134e94dad4acf</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;hegrunted,as,&quot;Sorry,&quot; he grunted, as the tiny old man stumbled and almost fell.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-316a8a69e6fec16c757134e94dad4acf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1304">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-da87b40957143834d850b32e7a2b00a0</data>
      <data key="v_content">It
was a few seconds before Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-da87b40957143834d850b32e7a2b00a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1305">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1948575404f3c192f3b5ec29cb80bb18</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley realized that the man was wearing a
violet cloak.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1948575404f3c192f3b5ec29cb80bb18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1306">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-73de333296809eb923dc852827ece86c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He didn&apos;t seem at all upset at being almost knocked to the
ground.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-73de333296809eb923dc852827ece86c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1307">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c0ed653f394f7225e99b1a30967b0090</data>
      <data key="v_content">his,On the contrary, his face split into a wide smile and he said in
a squeaky voice that made passersby stare, &quot;Don&apos;t be sorry, my dear sir,
for nothing could upset me today! Rejoice, for You-Know-Who has gone at
last! Even Muggles like yourself should be celebrating, this happy,
happy day!&quot;
And the old man hugged Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c0ed653f394f7225e99b1a30967b0090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1308">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2c3598af72779109c30e65a1a423f138</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley around the middle and walked off.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2c3598af72779109c30e65a1a423f138</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1309">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3b45a3a223e2a0700ffd76a17b7b59dc</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley stood rooted to the spot.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3b45a3a223e2a0700ffd76a17b7b59dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1310">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1d4647bed50af55e7fc1884c1444be84</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had been hugged by a complete
stranger.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1d4647bed50af55e7fc1884c1444be84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1311">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-075ab121b1eabfcf4de50ea0ecb803da</data>
      <data key="v_content">He also thought he had been called a Muggle, whatever that
was.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-075ab121b1eabfcf4de50ea0ecb803da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1312">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0ca8232c9572023248a4236756a88490</data>
      <data key="v_content">He hurried to his car and set off for home, hoping
4
he was imagining things, which he had never hoped before, because he
didn&apos;t approve of imagination.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0ca8232c9572023248a4236756a88490</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1313">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bb6a3e1341491227e82b71f6499bfabb</data>
      <data key="v_content">As he pulled into the driveway of number four, the first thing he saw --
and it didn&apos;t improve his mood -- was the tabby cat he&apos;d spotted that
morning.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bb6a3e1341491227e82b71f6499bfabb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1314">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5e7642396696bbf90fa70d4ec773b299</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was now sitting on his garden wall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5e7642396696bbf90fa70d4ec773b299</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1315">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c842a5e9ce018984d00f04ba3c4d98dd</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was sure it was the
same one; it had the same markings around its eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c842a5e9ce018984d00f04ba3c4d98dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1316">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6a8f60021d1112426f399bbd07fbff82</data>
      <data key="v_content">It just gave him a
stern look.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6a8f60021d1112426f399bbd07fbff82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1317">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8b5d416b2429011b7fba1c80f7cbf60f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Was this normal cat behavior? Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8b5d416b2429011b7fba1c80f7cbf60f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1318">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9df239fccf8c57256b8af6185c0ab970</data>
      <data key="v_content">Trying
to pull himself together, he let himself into the house.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9df239fccf8c57256b8af6185c0ab970</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1319">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d3d3319f347a2dd781634b1ab47eee94</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was still
determined not to mention anything to his wife.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d3d3319f347a2dd781634b1ab47eee94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1320">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-290ff5ee130d8e3540b0a4e69f707636</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley had had a nice, normal day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-290ff5ee130d8e3540b0a4e69f707636</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1321">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f9e627c6080a39bfdea72c7bbd8bbeb8</data>
      <data key="v_content">She told him over dinner all
about Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f9e627c6080a39bfdea72c7bbd8bbeb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1322">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-38a226064bb20912ee8b3ac4c3eb7919</data>
      <data key="v_content">Next Door&apos;s problems with her daughter and how Dudley had
learned a new word (&quot;Won&apos;t!&quot;).</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-38a226064bb20912ee8b3ac4c3eb7919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1323">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2c480895048a2a134a94bb92729123ec</data>
      <data key="v_content">When
Dudley had been put to bed, he went into the living room in time to
catch the last report on the evening news:
&quot;And finally, bird-watchers everywhere have reported that the nation&apos;s
owls have been behaving very unusually today.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2c480895048a2a134a94bb92729123ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1324">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4e29ae5cb8e43b31bc5189520ac56b62</data>
      <data key="v_content">Although owls normally
hunt at night and are hardly ever seen in daylight, there have been
hundreds of sightings of these birds flying in every direction since
sunrise.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4e29ae5cb8e43b31bc5189520ac56b62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1325">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-79dcae965ae79eeee58d5db6bc11a4ee</data>
      <data key="v_content">Experts are unable to explain why the owls have suddenly
changed their sleeping pattern.&quot; The newscaster allowed himself a grin.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-79dcae965ae79eeee58d5db6bc11a4ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1326">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-73401b880be6f292abf39f2e3394ea63</data>
      <data key="v_content">overto,And now, over to Jim McGuffin with the weather.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-73401b880be6f292abf39f2e3394ea63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1327">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d5989175a88886f3536971012292f89f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Going
to be any more showers of owls tonight, Jim?&quot;
&quot;Well, Ted,&quot; said the weatherman, &quot;I don&apos;t know about that, but it&apos;s not
only the owls that have been acting oddly today.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d5989175a88886f3536971012292f89f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1328">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4fbcfe8ae55fdfcac7f0b2e05172d116</data>
      <data key="v_content">Viewers as far apart as
Kent, Yorkshire, and Dundee have been phoning in to tell me that instead
of the rain I promised yesterday, they&apos;ve had a downpour of shooting
stars! Perhaps people have been celebrating Bonfire Night early -- it&apos;s
not until next week, folks! But I can promise a wet night tonight.&quot;
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4fbcfe8ae55fdfcac7f0b2e05172d116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1329">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8b8940323b0550f05640effb9f6ccae8</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley sat frozen in his armchair.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8b8940323b0550f05640effb9f6ccae8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1330">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4cb43bf94798d36ff2c3d9b2e3013bac</data>
      <data key="v_content">Shooting stars all over Britain?
Owls flying by daylight? Mysterious people in cloaks all over the place?
And a whisper, a whisper about the Potters...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4cb43bf94798d36ff2c3d9b2e3013bac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1331">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2922fe5c26065365179972d13c6b0dda</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley came into the living room carrying two cups of tea.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2922fe5c26065365179972d13c6b0dda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1332">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-27dfa576759f8250f1d6c8a01a6f321c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He&apos;d have to say something to her.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-27dfa576759f8250f1d6c8a01a6f321c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1333">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-67b09f2eca995460a362d63c5ac0c798</data>
      <data key="v_content">dear,&quot;Er -- Petunia, dear -- you haven&apos;t heard from your sister
lately, have you?&quot;
5
As he had expected, Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-67b09f2eca995460a362d63c5ac0c798</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1334">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-78b6ef9238689486c5f0e2a7f1656982</data>
      <data key="v_content">theynormally,After all,
they normally pretended she didn&apos;t have a sister.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-78b6ef9238689486c5f0e2a7f1656982</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1335">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4243f075c5122ac7908bf9c93f03087d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Why?&quot;
&quot;Funny stuff on the news,&quot; Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4243f075c5122ac7908bf9c93f03087d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1336">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-72670774ffab8f1f46b9132b2f491fbc</data>
      <data key="v_content">and there were a lot of funny-looking people in town today...&quot;
&quot;So?&quot; snapped Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-72670774ffab8f1f46b9132b2f491fbc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1337">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-57d98858d0290cb9ee755c785065a762</data>
      <data key="v_content">it was something to do with...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-57d98858d0290cb9ee755c785065a762</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1338">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-70d75551a120c670ddeeddaf6bb3dee1</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley sipped her tea through pursed lips.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-70d75551a120c670ddeeddaf6bb3dee1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1339">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6badc3f0043e0f50b0a192e98225c465</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley wondered
whether he dared tell her he&apos;d heard the name &quot;Potter.&quot; He decided he
didn&apos;t dare.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6badc3f0043e0f50b0a192e98225c465</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1340">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1b2ed9daef3405a64617fde64485ac51</data>
      <data key="v_content">as,Instead he said, as casually as he could, &quot;Their son --
he&apos;d be about Dudley&apos;s age now, wouldn&apos;t he?&quot;
&quot;I suppose so,&quot; said Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1b2ed9daef3405a64617fde64485ac51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1341">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e3964411b2a2efa091ba6ae0b3468537</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;What&apos;s his name again? Howard, isn&apos;t it?&quot;
&quot;Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e3964411b2a2efa091ba6ae0b3468537</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1342">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3e80362c71a4005c0e9428f7e871dffb</data>
      <data key="v_content">commonname,if,Nasty, common name, if you ask me.&quot;
&quot;Oh, yes,&quot; said Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3e80362c71a4005c0e9428f7e871dffb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1343">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f5ee328dfd81166cd238f6586a788d36</data>
      <data key="v_content">Iquiteagree.&quot;,&quot;Yes, I quite
agree.&quot;
He didn&apos;t say another word on the subject as they went upstairs to bed.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f5ee328dfd81166cd238f6586a788d36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1344">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c46fdaf030f88a89635e6477169f307e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley was in the bathroom, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c46fdaf030f88a89635e6477169f307e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1345">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-de3123a5f7f6c92b2f30764a2676fc89</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley crept to the bedroom
window and peered down into the front garden.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-de3123a5f7f6c92b2f30764a2676fc89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1346">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7a2d80911786a127ba83082f5b4b6c40</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was staring down Privet Drive as though it were waiting for
something.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7a2d80911786a127ba83082f5b4b6c40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1347">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6a698b583e6e7ac400fb173c22a292f2</data>
      <data key="v_content">Was he imagining things? Could all this have anything to do with the
Potters? If it did...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6a698b583e6e7ac400fb173c22a292f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1348">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-95044bc464fc6bcfc741e040e1e64be1</data>
      <data key="v_content">if it got out that they were related to a pair of
-- well, he didn&apos;t think he could bear it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-95044bc464fc6bcfc741e040e1e64be1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1349">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e4fb6124fd1597c2c0314dc6f8a02f6a</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley fell asleep quickly but Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e4fb6124fd1597c2c0314dc6f8a02f6a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1350">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6d6c78b7808c831c58fea553f495c857</data>
      <data key="v_content">turning,Dursley lay awake, turning it all over in his mind.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6d6c78b7808c831c58fea553f495c857</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1351">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bd89fbcaccb2d92cedec0d86ff6d64ad</data>
      <data key="v_content">comfortingthought,His last, comforting
thought before he fell asleep was that even if the Potters were
involved, there was no reason for them to come near him and Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bd89fbcaccb2d92cedec0d86ff6d64ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1352">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-752a5503d125d577e603afe754548315</data>
      <data key="v_content">The Potters knew very well what he and Petunia thought about
6
them and their kind....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-752a5503d125d577e603afe754548315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1353">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2dc7866208b22cd3bbf7a02543e45b08</data>
      <data key="v_content">He couldn&apos;t see how he and Petunia could get
mixed up in anything that might be going on -- he yawned and turned over
-- it couldn&apos;t affect them....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2dc7866208b22cd3bbf7a02543e45b08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1354">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e701ebfb7017f20c54553f204e7196b6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley might have been drifting into an uneasy sleep, but the cat
on the wall outside was showing no sign of sleepiness.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e701ebfb7017f20c54553f204e7196b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1355">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4aba7460ef1838098894f6ff648d5710</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was sitting as
still as a statue, its eyes fixed unblinkingly on the far corner of
Privet Drive.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4aba7460ef1838098894f6ff648d5710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1356">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bbd6ca02ae0f7cd39553306c59791596</data>
      <data key="v_content">It didn&apos;t so much as quiver when a car door slammed on the
next street, nor when two owls swooped overhead.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bbd6ca02ae0f7cd39553306c59791596</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1357">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2df25ee65d5724de29f0639df933a42e</data>
      <data key="v_content">itwas,In fact, it was nearly
midnight before the cat moved at all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2df25ee65d5724de29f0639df933a42e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1358">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5528842d9f3a36874296cb75478a55ba</data>
      <data key="v_content">A man appeared on the corner the cat had been watching, appeared so
suddenly and silently you&apos;d have thought he&apos;d just popped out of the
ground.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5528842d9f3a36874296cb75478a55ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1359">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3cd8f78096abe83cac016155b250d293</data>
      <data key="v_content">The cat&apos;s tail twitched and its eyes narrowed.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3cd8f78096abe83cac016155b250d293</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1360">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-759dbc481577e403c2ba2f857c6b0d03</data>
      <data key="v_content">Nothing like this man had ever been seen on Privet Drive.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-759dbc481577e403c2ba2f857c6b0d03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1361">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b5b15b53f5c2079c31c4c7ccf4e3b26e</data>
      <data key="v_content">thin,,He was tall,
thin, and very old, judging by the silver of his hair and beard, which
were both long enough to tuck into his belt.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b5b15b53f5c2079c31c4c7ccf4e3b26e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1362">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-05b510852b9ebc87a50ed49f33353a4d</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was wearing long robes,
a purple cloak that swept the ground, and high-heeled, buckled boots.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-05b510852b9ebc87a50ed49f33353a4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1363">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ceb97afbff911ed987b76c665b1a8545</data>
      <data key="v_content">His blue eyes were light, bright, and sparkling behind half-moon
spectacles and his nose was very long and crooked, as though it had been
broken at least twice.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ceb97afbff911ed987b76c665b1a8545</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1364">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f84db9c36194a8735fd4f96aea970e77</data>
      <data key="v_content">This man&apos;s name was Albus Dumbledore.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f84db9c36194a8735fd4f96aea970e77</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1365">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8a1b1da7544615960a48f34adefe09f5</data>
      <data key="v_content">Albus Dumbledore didn&apos;t seem to realize that he had just arrived in a
street where everything from his name to his boots was unwelcome.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8a1b1da7544615960a48f34adefe09f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1366">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-849ce4f3c42d68b4e633a7aeb9e7abb9</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was
busy rummaging in his cloak, looking for something.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-849ce4f3c42d68b4e633a7aeb9e7abb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1367">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0c8d430da53c44540a88147a1cb20da6</data>
      <data key="v_content">But he did seem to
realize he was being watched, because he looked up suddenly at the cat,
which was still staring at him from the other end of the street.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0c8d430da53c44540a88147a1cb20da6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1368">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-62c279c060fc4484b730a0b12734b513</data>
      <data key="v_content">the,For
some reason, the sight of the cat seemed to amuse him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-62c279c060fc4484b730a0b12734b513</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1369">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1fd524f2c3c62ccbc23a8545d1f886bc</data>
      <data key="v_content">,He chuckled and
muttered, &quot;I should have known.&quot;
He found what he was looking for in his inside pocket.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1fd524f2c3c62ccbc23a8545d1f886bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1370">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-54975f66e2686266aff055d18479dba6</data>
      <data key="v_content">It seemed to be a
silver cigarette lighter.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-54975f66e2686266aff055d18479dba6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1371">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-06c7774a45f3e03640c17e7aefb14417</data>
      <data key="v_content">,He flicked it open, held it up in the air, and
clicked it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-06c7774a45f3e03640c17e7aefb14417</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1372">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8c1f5c0f8447db76ae70cbcf3c91a31e</data>
      <data key="v_content">The nearest street lamp went out with a little pop.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8c1f5c0f8447db76ae70cbcf3c91a31e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1373">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b5f952c07dbcdd3d68a020b3e5cdbd8b</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
clicked it again -- the next lamp flickered into darkness.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b5f952c07dbcdd3d68a020b3e5cdbd8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1374">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-89ecab51e1591f57aea9b387785123ef</data>
      <data key="v_content">Twelve times
he clicked the Put-Outer, until the only lights left on the whole street
were two tiny pinpricks in the distance, which were the eyes of the cat
watching him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-89ecab51e1591f57aea9b387785123ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1375">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c1ca7ea268ace5960fa37bb1d225c15f</data>
      <data key="v_content">If anyone looked out of their window now, even beady-eyed
Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c1ca7ea268ace5960fa37bb1d225c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1376">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-676dc219a95437026d8393da576a2db0</data>
      <data key="v_content">theywouldn&apos;tbe,Dursley, they wouldn&apos;t be able to see anything that was happening
down on the pavement.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-676dc219a95437026d8393da576a2db0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1377">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c54398c05f4cf6049308ee494366d80f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dumbledore slipped the Put-Outer back inside his
cloak and set off down the street toward number four, where he sat down
7
on the wall next to the cat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c54398c05f4cf6049308ee494366d80f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1378">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-73927398f3615891ff5ef0eec9a54951</data>
      <data key="v_content">He didn&apos;t look at it, but after a moment he
spoke to it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-73927398f3615891ff5ef0eec9a54951</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1379">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0346490c834c6613cd461493f5d3224e</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Fancy seeing you here, Professor McGonagall.&quot;
He turned to smile at the tabby, but it had gone.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0346490c834c6613cd461493f5d3224e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1380">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b9bddb2d995830ba5b09a33723aa6389</data>
      <data key="v_content">Instead he was smiling
at a rather severe-looking woman who was wearing square glasses exactly
the shape of the markings the cat had had around its eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b9bddb2d995830ba5b09a33723aa6389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1381">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-19e8e4766695a9904e65f695c60f85af</data>
      <data key="v_content">too,waswearing,She, too, was
wearing a cloak, an emerald one.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-19e8e4766695a9904e65f695c60f85af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1382">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f5d5fc988d3993cad4a7f00bf5c48450</data>
      <data key="v_content">Her black hair was drawn into a tight
bun.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f5d5fc988d3993cad4a7f00bf5c48450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1383">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7882ecb1a89226827fd03658c81e07e2</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;How did you know it was me?&quot; she asked.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7882ecb1a89226827fd03658c81e07e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1384">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-531e8fea42fb8260d85853d553dd1ec3</data>
      <data key="v_content">I,&quot;My dear Professor, I &apos;ve never seen a cat sit so stiffly.&quot;
&quot;You&apos;d be stiff if you&apos;d been sitting on a brick wall all day,&quot; said
Professor McGonagall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-531e8fea42fb8260d85853d553dd1ec3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1385">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9f605fdaf4c7444afaf53f2d1fecfc0f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;All day? When you could have been celebrating? I must have passed a
dozen feasts and parties on my way here.&quot;
Professor McGonagall sniffed angrily.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9f605fdaf4c7444afaf53f2d1fecfc0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1386">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-184f07b6e17a04f607adcabaabd7b030</data>
      <data key="v_content">everyone&apos;scelebrating,,&quot;Oh yes, everyone&apos;s celebrating, all right,&quot; she said impatiently.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-184f07b6e17a04f607adcabaabd7b030</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1387">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7c8dd3e30c0c6aa8bd04cf2296d63cfc</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You&apos;d think they&apos;d be a bit more careful, but no -- even the Muggles
have noticed something&apos;s going on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7c8dd3e30c0c6aa8bd04cf2296d63cfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1388">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a382aa586c8461e649e04befae508a63</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was on their news.&quot; She jerked her
head back at the Dursleys&apos; dark living-room window.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a382aa586c8461e649e04befae508a63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1389">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-520215ddc268430cfe1bfd9ff65fc4dc</data>
      <data key="v_content">They
were bound to notice something.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-520215ddc268430cfe1bfd9ff65fc4dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1390">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-14e8bedcd3d4c0a8432e60d2de94e6cc</data>
      <data key="v_content">Shooting stars down in Kent -- I&apos;ll bet
that was Dedalus Diggle.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-14e8bedcd3d4c0a8432e60d2de94e6cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1391">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-13b5a2965396438c4348eff8639fa800</data>
      <data key="v_content">He never had much sense.&quot;
&quot;You can&apos;t blame them,&quot; said Dumbledore gently.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-13b5a2965396438c4348eff8639fa800</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1392">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b9ad4a75dd9b7d804af8e5702adf6187</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;We&apos;ve had precious
little to celebrate for eleven years.&quot;
&quot;I know that,&quot; said Professor McGonagall irritably.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b9ad4a75dd9b7d804af8e5702adf6187</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1393">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7673188e6aea042f05fc593cd9ac1ee8</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But that&apos;s no
reason to lose our heads.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7673188e6aea042f05fc593cd9ac1ee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1394">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-00b730413e15449ead5a33f89cae575d</data>
      <data key="v_content">People are being downright careless, out on
the streets in broad daylight, not even dressed in Muggle clothes,
swapping rumors.&quot;
She threw a sharp, sideways glance at Dumbledore here, as though hoping
he was going to tell her something, but he didn&apos;t, so she went on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-00b730413e15449ead5a33f89cae575d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1395">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-feb9d2ace75e7bdf94ebde2a007eef0f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;A
fine thing it would be if, on the very day YouKnow-Who seems to have
disappeared at last, the Muggles found out about us all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-feb9d2ace75e7bdf94ebde2a007eef0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1396">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a9713abffe3191086c2d7fcb566470a2</data>
      <data key="v_content">I suppose he
8
really has gone, Dumbledore?&quot;
&quot;It certainly seems so,&quot; said Dumbledore.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a9713abffe3191086c2d7fcb566470a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1397">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c67aafff7ee02b409b5b58b3bc6e8929</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;We have much to be thankful
for.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c67aafff7ee02b409b5b58b3bc6e8929</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1398">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-db72d80d0b85d3a3747886710c02c326</data>
      <data key="v_content">Would you care for a lemon drop?&quot;
&quot;A what?&quot;
&quot;A lemon drop.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-db72d80d0b85d3a3747886710c02c326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1399">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-67f4ff7a8d53e14bbbb1cc68a9b7ee47</data>
      <data key="v_content">They&apos;re a kind of Muggle sweet I&apos;m rather fond of&quot;
&quot;No, thank you,&quot; said Professor McGonagall coldly, as though she didn&apos;t
think this was the moment for lemon drops.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-67f4ff7a8d53e14bbbb1cc68a9b7ee47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1400">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2404cf455e03d700086bde1e2a39bfa7</data>
      <data key="v_content">even,&quot;As I say, even if
You-Know-Who has gone -&quot;
&quot;My dear Professor, surely a sensible person like yourself can call him
by his name? All this &apos;You- Know-Who&apos; nonsense -- for eleven years I
have been trying to persuade people to call him by his proper name:
Voldemort.&quot; Professor McGonagall flinched, but Dumbledore, who was
unsticking two lemon drops, seemed not to notice.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2404cf455e03d700086bde1e2a39bfa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1401">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9ef3e689806c3de56a9522a97d036d06</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;It all gets so
confusing if we keep saying &apos;You-Know-Who.&apos; I have never seen any reason
to be frightened of saying Voldemort&apos;s name.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9ef3e689806c3de56a9522a97d036d06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1402">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-34725d891ae5bbef35be92c76d2329e0</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I know you haven &apos;t, said Professor McGonagall, sounding half
exasperated, half admiring.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-34725d891ae5bbef35be92c76d2329e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1403">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-be0a84110dc9fcd0d52b663da882137d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Everyone knows you&apos;re
the only one You-Know- oh, all right, Voldemort, was frightened of.&quot;
&quot;You flatter me,&quot; said Dumbledore calmly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-be0a84110dc9fcd0d52b663da882137d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1404">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2082da7e47cdd76c348b36ed889a9a6b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Voldemort had powers I will
never have.&quot;
&quot;Only because you&apos;re too -- well -- noble to use them.&quot;
&quot;It&apos;s lucky it&apos;s dark.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2082da7e47cdd76c348b36ed889a9a6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1405">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6536d9105309941b5e2f18f1a8ef137d</data>
      <data key="v_content">I haven&apos;t blushed so much since Madam Pomfrey
told me she liked my new earmuffs.&quot;
Professor McGonagall shot a sharp look at Dumbledore and said, &quot;The owls
are nothing next to the rumors that are flying around.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6536d9105309941b5e2f18f1a8ef137d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1406">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-32dd6b36b411877ad40408eb417aad4c</data>
      <data key="v_content">You know what
everyone&apos;s saying? About why he&apos;s disappeared? About what finally
stopped him?&quot;
It seemed that Professor McGonagall had reached the point she was most
anxious to discuss, the real reason she had been waiting on a cold, hard
wall all day, for neither as a cat nor as a woman had she fixed
Dumbledore with such a piercing stare as she did now.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-32dd6b36b411877ad40408eb417aad4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1407">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-354a1060c9352a17edb64524615c81e5</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was plain that
whatever &quot;everyone&quot; was saying, she was not going to believe it until
9
Dumbledore told her it was true.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-354a1060c9352a17edb64524615c81e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1408">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a2ed11b98db75febf0206da842247ad3</data>
      <data key="v_content">however,waschoosing,Dumbledore, however, was choosing
another lemon drop and did not answer.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a2ed11b98db75febf0206da842247ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1409">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-39041ca63f56392e663ecff2dbc9fce4</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;she,&quot;What they&apos;re saying,&quot; she pressed on, &quot;is that last night Voldemort
turned up in Godric&apos;s Hollow.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-39041ca63f56392e663ecff2dbc9fce4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1410">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-270def1b0c33f40dd40bb51e04f0b89e</data>
      <data key="v_content">He went to find the Potters.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-270def1b0c33f40dd40bb51e04f0b89e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1411">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-35bf03d9aa948d0478335d0978bd3b3a</data>
      <data key="v_content">The rumor is
that Lily and James Potter are -- are -- that they&apos;re -- dead.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-35bf03d9aa948d0478335d0978bd3b3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1412">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a45468825bce34215362c6caef9ac646</data>
      <data key="v_content">I didn&apos;t want to believe it...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a45468825bce34215362c6caef9ac646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1413">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f20c6d86a66e003ada2662a73da06059</data>
      <data key="v_content">Albus...&quot;Dumbledorereached,Oh, Albus...&quot;
Dumbledore reached out and patted her on the shoulder.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f20c6d86a66e003ada2662a73da06059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1414">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c5e0c0e66b1953295871369d389de38e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Professor McGonagall&apos;s voice trembled as she went on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c5e0c0e66b1953295871369d389de38e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1415">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a24329d246c3fcfc4bc8ae1587489beb</data>
      <data key="v_content">They&apos;re saying he tried to kill the Potter&apos;s son, Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a24329d246c3fcfc4bc8ae1587489beb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1416">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6cce08317a4e778bccfbfb882e391e50</data>
      <data key="v_content">He couldn&apos;t kill that little boy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6cce08317a4e778bccfbfb882e391e50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1417">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b794f3fe7d18f1e3e21fd91dade6dc95</data>
      <data key="v_content">,No one knows why, or how,
but they&apos;re saying that when he couldn&apos;t kill Harry Potter, Voldemort&apos;s
power somehow broke -- and that&apos;s why he&apos;s gone.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b794f3fe7d18f1e3e21fd91dade6dc95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1418">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-994b96b63c1b5c368c49f042a7b05f16</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;It&apos;s -- it&apos;s true?&quot; faltered Professor McGonagall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-994b96b63c1b5c368c49f042a7b05f16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1419">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ab4c5a10b1f44723db43ed976a871d5f</data>
      <data key="v_content">he couldn&apos;t kill a little boy?
It&apos;s just astounding...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ab4c5a10b1f44723db43ed976a871d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1420">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6accaa376b88151a7d5d7d19e4c8f5d3</data>
      <data key="v_content">of all the things to stop him...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6accaa376b88151a7d5d7d19e4c8f5d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1421">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f558dd23bbcfb5a8cdfc066f6e77e38d</data>
      <data key="v_content">but how in the
name of heaven did Harry survive?&quot;
&quot;We can only guess,&quot; said Dumbledore.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f558dd23bbcfb5a8cdfc066f6e77e38d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1422">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9fb03f59a833f6158094c7f3811d4ebf</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;We may never know.&quot;
Professor McGonagall pulled out a lace handkerchief and dabbed at her
eyes beneath her spectacles.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9fb03f59a833f6158094c7f3811d4ebf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1423">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d7f1aceab1b853ee26de4cc486497327</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dumbledore gave a great sniff as he took a
golden watch from his pocket and examined it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d7f1aceab1b853ee26de4cc486497327</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1424">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dd7aac5a73cad065d4506f884f139c03</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was a very odd watch.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dd7aac5a73cad065d4506f884f139c03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1425">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ab7e9d13ebe0004c6d5d282755a70359</data>
      <data key="v_content">It had twelve hands but no numbers; instead, little planets were moving
around the edge.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ab7e9d13ebe0004c6d5d282755a70359</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1426">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cca3f4090d7607950b437192f3218dff</data>
      <data key="v_content">It must have made sense to Dumbledore, though, because
he put it back in his pocket and said, &quot;Hagrid&apos;s late.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cca3f4090d7607950b437192f3218dff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1427">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eeb76c67a9ca0859ef183b96017d39a3</data>
      <data key="v_content">I suppose it was
he who told you I&apos;d be here, by the way?&quot;
&quot;Yes,&quot; said Professor McGonagall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eeb76c67a9ca0859ef183b96017d39a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1428">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2ec437db2c631547adabe53a7514206e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;And I don&apos;t suppose you&apos;re going to
tell me why you&apos;re here, of all places?&quot;
&quot;I&apos;ve come to bring Harry to his aunt and uncle.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2ec437db2c631547adabe53a7514206e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1429">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-478207f3124c4e3aa2c4568cd6755e27</data>
      <data key="v_content">They&apos;re the only family
he has left now.&quot;
10
&quot;You don&apos;t mean -- you can&apos;t mean the people who live here?&quot; cried
Professor McGonagall, jumping to her feet and pointing at number four.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-478207f3124c4e3aa2c4568cd6755e27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1430">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c34d482ede7f90168c5d0e4745ce6113</data>
      <data key="v_content">I&apos;ve been watching them all day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c34d482ede7f90168c5d0e4745ce6113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1431">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2ca9b5e1c0e36f51e234f785b4c38fce</data>
      <data key="v_content">You couldn&apos;t
find two people who are less like us.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2ca9b5e1c0e36f51e234f785b4c38fce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1432">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-20bd49a1cde25d0a84f7aeb6fb06be16</data>
      <data key="v_content">And they&apos;ve got this son -- I saw
him kicking his mother all the way up the street, screaming for sweets.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-20bd49a1cde25d0a84f7aeb6fb06be16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1433">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eebfd02586d811d0f9f7f5cbb5f1f791</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry Potter come and live here!&quot;
&quot;It&apos;s the best place for him,&quot; said Dumbledore firmly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eebfd02586d811d0f9f7f5cbb5f1f791</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1434">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-595438dff3689795325237c5ad19e8f0</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;His aunt and
uncle will be able to explain everything to him when he&apos;s older.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-595438dff3689795325237c5ad19e8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1435">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-651336c65a99c2ae953d9c34789b96d1</data>
      <data key="v_content">I&apos;ve
written them a letter.&quot;
&quot;A letter?&quot; repeated Professor McGonagall faintly, sitting back down on
the wall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-651336c65a99c2ae953d9c34789b96d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1436">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-310658b56d71c00be31ca7c8037362a2</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dumbledore,youthink,&quot;Really, Dumbledore, you think you can explain all this in a
letter? These people will never understand him! He&apos;ll be famous -- a
legend -- I wouldn&apos;t be surprised if today was known as Harry Potter day
in the future -- there will be books written about Harry -- every child
in our world will know his name!&quot;
&quot;Exactly,&quot; said Dumbledore, looking very seriously over the top of his
half-moon glasses.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-310658b56d71c00be31ca7c8037362a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1437">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b695365d31bebf35490c7c81d38461a5</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;It would be enough to turn any boy&apos;s head.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b695365d31bebf35490c7c81d38461a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1438">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-826f272b00a7a4094d97d78de3745b9d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Famous
before he can walk and talk! Famous for something he won&apos;t even
remember! CarA you see how much better off he&apos;ll be, growing up away
from all that until he&apos;s ready to take it?&quot;
Professor McGonagall opened her mouth, changed her mind, swallowed, and
then said, &quot;Yes -- yes, you&apos;re right, of course.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-826f272b00a7a4094d97d78de3745b9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1439">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e8ea2c56830e515ba2bd46b0699914e9</data>
      <data key="v_content">But how is the boy
getting here, Dumbledore?&quot; She eyed his cloak suddenly as though she
thought he might be hiding Harry underneath it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e8ea2c56830e515ba2bd46b0699914e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1440">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dbbfabbfc26c8309a77d5bdc7ab2b61a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Hagrid&apos;s bringing him.&quot;
&quot;You think it -- wise -- to trust Hagrid with something as important as
this?&quot;
I would trust Hagrid with my life,&quot; said Dumbledore.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dbbfabbfc26c8309a77d5bdc7ab2b61a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1441">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ee00b79f9f7e7eb919d289f9af4f1e94</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I&apos;m not saying his heart isn&apos;t in the right place,&quot; said Professor
McGonagall grudgingly, &quot;but you can&apos;t pretend he&apos;s not careless.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ee00b79f9f7e7eb919d289f9af4f1e94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1442">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bd918e81df66b261bdf16e870e62fde5</data>
      <data key="v_content">He does
tend to -- what was that?&quot;
A low rumbling sound had broken the silence around them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bd918e81df66b261bdf16e870e62fde5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1443">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f8c74f48f0f258ab320ee9b99eb5b714</data>
      <data key="v_content">It grew
steadily louder as they looked up and down the street for some sign of a
11
headlight; it swelled to a roar as they both looked up at the sky -- and
a huge motorcycle fell out of the air and landed on the road in front of
them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f8c74f48f0f258ab320ee9b99eb5b714</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1444">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-335af44d61f7794807f01bec32c1a78b</data>
      <data key="v_content">If the motorcycle was huge, it was nothing to the man sitting astride
it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-335af44d61f7794807f01bec32c1a78b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1445">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-78a1473e43a240671330a04d77588ffa</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was almost twice as tall as a normal man and at least five times
as wide.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-78a1473e43a240671330a04d77588ffa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1446">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8fea999ecd19b1987d45b8b9d950aff9</data>
      <data key="v_content">He looked simply too big to be allowed, and so wild - long
tangles of bushy black hair and beard hid most of his face, he had hands
the size of trash can lids, and his feet in their leather boots were
like baby dolphins.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8fea999ecd19b1987d45b8b9d950aff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1447">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-80666b45df5b4a3d4313188478ebd5a8</data>
      <data key="v_content">muscular,In his vast, muscular arms he was holding a bundle
of blankets.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-80666b45df5b4a3d4313188478ebd5a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1448">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e580e6c7da9975d5ed90b2d3f9807ec4</data>
      <data key="v_content">And where did
you get that motorcycle?&quot;
&quot;Borrowed it, Professor Dumbledore, sit,&quot; said the giant, climbing
carefully off the motorcycle as he spoke.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e580e6c7da9975d5ed90b2d3f9807ec4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1449">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ba0d5c2dbf7405a751e616b8989c2f03</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Young Sirius Black lent it to
me.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ba0d5c2dbf7405a751e616b8989c2f03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1450">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b7175e0e0730c0c20416dd6c3c61487c</data>
      <data key="v_content">sir.&quot;,I&apos;ve got him, sir.&quot;
&quot;No problems, were there?&quot;
&quot;No, sir -- house was almost destroyed, but I got him out all right
before the Muggles started swarmin&apos; around.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b7175e0e0730c0c20416dd6c3c61487c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1451">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9cccb8ff0a0f807bcca4ebfa43a27ca7</data>
      <data key="v_content">He fell asleep as we was
flyin&apos; over Bristol.&quot;
Dumbledore and Professor McGonagall bent forward over the bundle of
blankets.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9cccb8ff0a0f807bcca4ebfa43a27ca7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1452">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-16acb797bdb53e6793284347fd5fc21c</data>
      <data key="v_content">justvisible,was,Inside, just visible, was a baby boy, fast asleep.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-16acb797bdb53e6793284347fd5fc21c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1453">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-96078960bb9cea629ef794d54b816860</data>
      <data key="v_content">Under a
tuft of jet-black hair over his forehead they could see a curiously
shaped cut, like a bolt of lightning.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-96078960bb9cea629ef794d54b816860</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1454">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2a2ac5a135d68e54a7baf6c4fea0e58e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Is that where -?&quot; whispered Professor McGonagall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2a2ac5a135d68e54a7baf6c4fea0e58e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1455">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-262ba9e9b267cdbcc8a835dac0f2fa23</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;He&apos;ll have that scar forever.&quot;
&quot;Couldn&apos;t you do something about it, Dumbledore?&quot;
&quot;Even if I could, I wouldn&apos;t.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-262ba9e9b267cdbcc8a835dac0f2fa23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1456">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b66a0642289d1f6c3f32dd1683aaab17</data>
      <data key="v_content">I have one myself
above my left knee that is a perfect map of the London Underground.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b66a0642289d1f6c3f32dd1683aaab17</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1457">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8bad9f7cd5ef6f4fe54ce3597e3907d5</data>
      <data key="v_content">Well
-- give him here, Hagrid -- we&apos;d better get this over with.&quot;
Dumbledore took Harry in his arms and turned toward the Dursleys&apos; house.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8bad9f7cd5ef6f4fe54ce3597e3907d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1458">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-90571a471bb6dfba722e7d0074b62d11</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Could I -- could I say good-bye to him, sir?&quot; asked Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-90571a471bb6dfba722e7d0074b62d11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1459">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-36528e09b872c96e30019e1c236776d7</data>
      <data key="v_content">He bent his
12
great, shaggy head over Harry and gave him what must have been a very
scratchy, whiskery kiss.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-36528e09b872c96e30019e1c236776d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1460">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b485b2f576e47e84b584d66978e1b799</data>
      <data key="v_content">suddenly,Hagridlet,Then, suddenly, Hagrid let out a howl like a
wounded dog.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b485b2f576e47e84b584d66978e1b799</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1461">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e71f35a501deeb184fb44e1008c05268</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Shhh!&quot; hissed Professor McGonagall, &quot;you&apos;ll wake the Muggles!&quot;
&quot;S-s-sorry,&quot; sobbed Hagrid, taking out a large, spotted handkerchief and
burying his face in it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e71f35a501deeb184fb44e1008c05268</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1462">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-47f25c17f49736ff423773a9b14c0cb7</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But I c-c-can&apos;t stand it -- Lily an&apos; James dead
-- an&apos; poor little Harry off ter live with Muggles -&quot;
&quot;Yes, yes, it&apos;s all very sad, but get a grip on yourself, Hagrid, or
we&apos;ll be found,&quot; Professor McGonagall whispered, patting Hagrid gingerly
on the arm as Dumbledore stepped over the low garden wall and walked to
the front door.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-47f25c17f49736ff423773a9b14c0cb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1463">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e263d5a5431517f0282a71714207a568</data>
      <data key="v_content">He laid Harry gently on the doorstep, took a letter out
of his cloak, tucked it inside Harry&apos;s blankets, and then came back to
the other two.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e263d5a5431517f0282a71714207a568</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1464">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cdd27806629a8fd8544749092e29ec35</data>
      <data key="v_content">For a full minute the three of them stood and looked at
the little bundle; Hagrid&apos;s shoulders shook, Professor McGonagall
blinked furiously, and the twinkling light that usually shone from
Dumbledore&apos;s eyes seemed to have gone out.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cdd27806629a8fd8544749092e29ec35</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1465">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-41d18e2b0bbe4f8e95857405c5858b77</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidDumbledorefinally,,&quot;Well,&quot; said Dumbledore finally, &quot;that&apos;s that.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-41d18e2b0bbe4f8e95857405c5858b77</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1466">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cb427ba41a5d7414c58d8729fa851dae</data>
      <data key="v_content">We may as well go and join the celebrations.&quot;
&quot;Yeah,&quot; said Hagrid in a very muffled voice, &quot;I&apos;ll be takin&apos; Sirius his
bike back.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cb427ba41a5d7414c58d8729fa851dae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1467">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5981547623789ea4e2b953ba8546e2b0</data>
      <data key="v_content">ProfessorMcGonagall--,G&apos;night, Professor McGonagall -- Professor Dumbledore, sir.&quot;
Wiping his streaming eyes on his jacket sleeve, Hagrid swung himself
onto the motorcycle and kicked the engine into life; with a roar it rose
into the air and off into the night.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5981547623789ea4e2b953ba8546e2b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1468">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-33148fa23718dbe3be29db2db431ee53</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I shall see you soon, I expect, Professor McGonagall,&quot; said Dumbledore,
nodding to her.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-33148fa23718dbe3be29db2db431ee53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1469">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b76c9f49b0a7f307f1943fd66ff2d183</data>
      <data key="v_content">Professor McGonagall blew her nose in reply.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b76c9f49b0a7f307f1943fd66ff2d183</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1470">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-70dcf08268d9dd74405265498edd7d21</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dumbledore turned and walked back down the street.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-70dcf08268d9dd74405265498edd7d21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1471">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a67b2def1b8bf83902695d1020f13138</data>
      <data key="v_content">On the corner he
stopped and took out the silver Put-Outer.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a67b2def1b8bf83902695d1020f13138</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1472">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-75f5126878cfe487e78c3043181ee8d8</data>
      <data key="v_content">,He clicked it once, and
twelve balls of light sped back to their street lamps so that Privet
Drive glowed suddenly orange and he could make out a tabby cat slinking
around the corner at the other end of the street.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-75f5126878cfe487e78c3043181ee8d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1473">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3a71094ccc786325c530b68d9fe586e9</data>
      <data key="v_content">He could just see the
bundle of blankets on the step of number four.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3a71094ccc786325c530b68d9fe586e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1474">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dfb86f29ec8282d9c56975ef22c6ae45</data>
      <data key="v_content">He turned on his heel and with a swish
of his cloak, he was gone.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dfb86f29ec8282d9c56975ef22c6ae45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1475">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1cf08971198c5d87917d6a8df9a9d865</data>
      <data key="v_content">13
A breeze ruffled the neat hedges of Privet Drive, which lay silent and
tidy under the inky sky, the very last place you would expect
astonishing things to happen.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1cf08971198c5d87917d6a8df9a9d865</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1476">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-23e5329f1924145c18128033cf6a186a</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry Potter rolled over inside his
blankets without waking up.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-23e5329f1924145c18128033cf6a186a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1477">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7b170fe39b70facd91ac58fbede3cd5f</data>
      <data key="v_content">One small hand closed on the letter beside
him and he slept on, not knowing he was special, not knowing he was
famous, not knowing he would be woken in a few hours&apos; time by Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7b170fe39b70facd91ac58fbede3cd5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1478">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bfa59bf4ba6d4188dfbb2aee87adeb5a</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley&apos;s scream as she opened the front door to put out the milk
bottles, nor that he would spend the next few weeks being prodded and
pinched by his cousin Dudley...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bfa59bf4ba6d4188dfbb2aee87adeb5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1479">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b3a553a2ed37448c833ed34f7ca9d704</data>
      <data key="v_content">He couldn&apos;t know that at this very
moment, people meeting in secret all over the country were holding up
their glasses and saying in hushed voices: &quot;To Harry Potter -- the boy
who lived!&quot;
CHAPTER TWO
THE VANISHING GLASS
Nearly ten years had passed since the Dursleys had woken up to find
their nephew on the front step, but Privet Drive had hardly changed at
all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b3a553a2ed37448c833ed34f7ca9d704</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1480">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-15002d8150ae4c5619dbf3d3993ef9b5</data>
      <data key="v_content">The sun rose on the same tidy front gardens and lit up the brass
number four on the Dursleys&apos; front door; it crept into their living
room, which was almost exactly the same as it had been on the night when
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-15002d8150ae4c5619dbf3d3993ef9b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1481">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-78b2d531f3026e3f988709efcc8c80d8</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dursley had seen that fateful news report about the owls.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-78b2d531f3026e3f988709efcc8c80d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1482">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ce7cf357dcf78a1f0c424f4e94d06805</data>
      <data key="v_content">Only the
photographs on the mantelpiece really showed how much time had passed.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ce7cf357dcf78a1f0c424f4e94d06805</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1483">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b27c39159e82803bf99ffb3ccd7b7162</data>
      <data key="v_content">there,Ten years ago, there had been lots of pictures of what looked like a
large pink beach ball wearing different-colored bonnets -- but Dudley
Dursley was no longer a baby, and now the photographs showed a large
blond boy riding his first bicycle, on a carousel at the fair, playing a
computer game with his father, being hugged and kissed by his mother.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b27c39159e82803bf99ffb3ccd7b7162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1484">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8533ec7f92b15e9b50ce5ea887b4dcdc</data>
      <data key="v_content">The room held no sign at all that another boy lived in the house, too.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8533ec7f92b15e9b50ce5ea887b4dcdc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1485">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-de6b42b75170ec9a1639329a6f04a885</data>
      <data key="v_content">Yet Harry Potter was still there, asleep at the moment, but not for
long.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-de6b42b75170ec9a1639329a6f04a885</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1486">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c6800fa3dea70448ed64deba58a13d99</data>
      <data key="v_content">His Aunt Petunia was awake and it was her shrill voice that made
the first noise of the day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c6800fa3dea70448ed64deba58a13d99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1487">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-63df3d87af03c474db20d20a5a21cf39</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Up! Get up! Now!&quot;
Harry woke with a start.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-63df3d87af03c474db20d20a5a21cf39</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1488">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e11b843e11592c5bab10a7ee1b966d57</data>
      <data key="v_content">His aunt rapped on the door again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e11b843e11592c5bab10a7ee1b966d57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1489">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7489a7da545e949a404eb7975f66ad39</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry heard her walking toward the kitchen and then
the sound of the frying pan being put on the stove.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7489a7da545e949a404eb7975f66ad39</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1490">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7b527bec8b3f285eef9b131532d73836</data>
      <data key="v_content">He rolled onto his
back and tried to remember the dream he had been having.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7b527bec8b3f285eef9b131532d73836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1491">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-770e095d1b711fc5859bee502e69ffd2</data>
      <data key="v_content">It had been a
14
good one.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-770e095d1b711fc5859bee502e69ffd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1492">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7e2d70c18588b8e09de4b3f05642e462</data>
      <data key="v_content">There had been a flying motorcycle in it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7e2d70c18588b8e09de4b3f05642e462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1493">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6a61df08782b4e0573a7812b9ce8e111</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had a funny
feeling he&apos;d had the same dream before.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6a61df08782b4e0573a7812b9ce8e111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1494">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b476598ceee62396d29f8ae9a02672fb</data>
      <data key="v_content">His aunt was back outside the door.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b476598ceee62396d29f8ae9a02672fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1495">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4699014a5beb8211a113d2b4f69e12e8</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Are you up yet?&quot; she demanded.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4699014a5beb8211a113d2b4f69e12e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1496">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-646b58a8cbd967e916cb22c500be5bda</data>
      <data key="v_content">getamove,&quot;Well, get a move on, I want you to look after the bacon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-646b58a8cbd967e916cb22c500be5bda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1497">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8fc7d43916f7ddb762df2606f3b3a0b5</data>
      <data key="v_content">And don&apos;t you
dare let it burn, I want everything perfect on Duddy&apos;s birthday.&quot;
Harry groaned.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8fc7d43916f7ddb762df2606f3b3a0b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1498">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-acb7f953ea902d8745e01a12d3578e7b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;What did you say?&quot; his aunt snapped through the door.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-acb7f953ea902d8745e01a12d3578e7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1499">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0ba7d52882ce3bc37f0f0e9ed2a17f49</data>
      <data key="v_content">nothing...&quot;Dudley&apos;sbirthday,&quot;Nothing, nothing...&quot;
Dudley&apos;s birthday -- how could he have forgotten? Harry got slowly out
of bed and started looking for socks.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0ba7d52882ce3bc37f0f0e9ed2a17f49</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1500">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-45113f17dc1b9851bc66e5e3a6061824</data>
      <data key="v_content">He found a pair under his bed and,
after pulling a spider off one of them, put them on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-45113f17dc1b9851bc66e5e3a6061824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1501">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e4bf344017cfcbeedfe1dafbd3167b95</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry was used to
spiders, because the cupboard under the stairs was full of them, and
that was where he slept.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e4bf344017cfcbeedfe1dafbd3167b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1502">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ec86fbd5b520a5f4a3b1a793ab9a200f</data>
      <data key="v_content">When he was dressed he went down the hall into the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ec86fbd5b520a5f4a3b1a793ab9a200f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1503">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b092c3f0bd3943a18aefed6f15adb22a</data>
      <data key="v_content">The table
was almost hidden beneath all Dudley&apos;s birthday presents.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b092c3f0bd3943a18aefed6f15adb22a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1504">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4eede16f13c40494ff72051dde1f8792</data>
      <data key="v_content">It looked as
though Dudley had gotten the new computer he wanted, not to mention the
second television and the racing bike.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4eede16f13c40494ff72051dde1f8792</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1505">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-582d97ba375c8a025bb1d1386f1200dd</data>
      <data key="v_content">Exactly why Dudley wanted a
racing bike was a mystery to Harry, as Dudley was very fat and hated
exercise -- unless of course it involved punching somebody.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-582d97ba375c8a025bb1d1386f1200dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1506">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-44103132177a0b5d3e20a26746076b43</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley&apos;s
favorite punching bag was Harry, but he couldn&apos;t often catch him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-44103132177a0b5d3e20a26746076b43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1507">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-df58787eb741406875aea674fa970f43</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Harry
didn&apos;t look it, but he was very fast.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-df58787eb741406875aea674fa970f43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1508">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-36e86c43d64d5609d410411f9505e7df</data>
      <data key="v_content">Perhaps it had something to do with living in a dark cupboard, but Harry
had always been small and skinny for his age.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-36e86c43d64d5609d410411f9505e7df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1509">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c1a29ffc0641f38687597acd3aa1bf06</data>
      <data key="v_content">He looked even smaller and
skinnier than he really was because all he had to wear were old clothes
of Dudley&apos;s, and Dudley was about four times bigger than he was.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c1a29ffc0641f38687597acd3aa1bf06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1510">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9e9a2841a8890ec466e55545df9d8e20</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry
had a thin face, knobbly knees, black hair, and bright green eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9e9a2841a8890ec466e55545df9d8e20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1511">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ca6e965e5adaa1da8945435bf5d67b8e</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
wore round glasses held together with a lot of Scotch tape because of
all the times Dudley had punched him on the nose.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ca6e965e5adaa1da8945435bf5d67b8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1512">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bc27496038ed7c6ebb6105ddf7642413</data>
      <data key="v_content">The only thing Harry
liked about his own appearance was a very thin scar on his forehead that
was shaped like a bolt of lightning.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bc27496038ed7c6ebb6105ddf7642413</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1513">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-33b8ffff28c57cd7784c74589d62f90b</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had had it as long as he could
remember, and the first question he could ever remember asking his Aunt
15
Petunia was how he had gotten it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-33b8ffff28c57cd7784c74589d62f90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1514">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0f81f79afdf3ee6c1657adbbf00d4e96</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;In the car crash when your parents died,&quot; she had said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0f81f79afdf3ee6c1657adbbf00d4e96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1515">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c4be1478b881d028e05c2b6c7360557f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;And don&apos;t ask
questions.&quot;
Don&apos;t ask questions -- that was the first rule for a quiet life with the
Dursleys.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c4be1478b881d028e05c2b6c7360557f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1516">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4b8de56d76e2efb6ca18aa7ac8e525ef</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon entered the kitchen as Harry was turning over the bacon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4b8de56d76e2efb6ca18aa7ac8e525ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1517">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0b1cb968c20047ee14ca6ba15faac838</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Comb your hair!&quot; he barked, by way of a morning greeting.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0b1cb968c20047ee14ca6ba15faac838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1518">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fd77eafe9389cf776685eb4e26b2c445</data>
      <data key="v_content">,About once a week, Uncle Vernon looked over the top of his newspaper and
shouted that Harry needed a haircut.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fd77eafe9389cf776685eb4e26b2c445</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1519">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5f8b58840675453329e004666f83f994</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry must have had more haircuts
than the rest of the boys in his class put
together, but it made no difference, his hair simply grew that way --
all over the place.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5f8b58840675453329e004666f83f994</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1520">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a459d751ba9b6e27633bc53b4d94e839</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry was frying eggs by the time Dudley arrived in the kitchen with his
mother.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a459d751ba9b6e27633bc53b4d94e839</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1521">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cde95f50f687509a37c2ed696b67a35f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley looked a lot like Uncle Vernon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cde95f50f687509a37c2ed696b67a35f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1522">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-336cc6467a62b91bba8be1a2ecedbb4f</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had a large pink face,
not much neck, small, watery blue eyes, and thick blond hair that lay
smoothly on his thick, fat head.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-336cc6467a62b91bba8be1a2ecedbb4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1523">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f82c44e156a882c43eff531b27a093de</data>
      <data key="v_content">Aunt Petunia often said that Dudley
looked like a baby angel -- Harry often said that Dudley looked like a
pig in a wig.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f82c44e156a882c43eff531b27a093de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1524">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f8ececd84fb811a2a6fab78e668592bf</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry put the plates of egg and bacon on the table, which was difficult
as there wasn&apos;t much room.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f8ececd84fb811a2a6fab78e668592bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1525">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-647f63e102db15023bb3e2704e5b4942</data>
      <data key="v_content">meanwhile,wascounting,Dudley, meanwhile, was counting his presents.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-647f63e102db15023bb3e2704e5b4942</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1526">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3975b17dfaffef5401bd80f0b02c9e1e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;hesaid,looking,&quot;Thirty-six,&quot; he said, looking up at his mother and father.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3975b17dfaffef5401bd80f0b02c9e1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1527">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f42322f61a83d5b56c284bfad212fb21</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;That&apos;s two
less than last year.&quot;
&quot;Darling, you haven&apos;t counted Auntie Marge&apos;s present, see, it&apos;s here
under this big one from Mommy and Daddy.&quot;
&quot;All right, thirty-seven then,&quot; said Dudley, going red in the face.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f42322f61a83d5b56c284bfad212fb21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1528">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e39e829cd2891cdb2ed0e44d2dae54d3</data>
      <data key="v_content">whocouldsee,Harry, who could see a huge Dudley tantrum coming on, began wolfing down
his bacon as fast as possible in case Dudley turned the table over.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e39e829cd2891cdb2ed0e44d2dae54d3</data>
    </node>
