      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8c509c6ed419fd341b3f9893fe94e747</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harrywas,Every
year, Harry was left behind with Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8c509c6ed419fd341b3f9893fe94e747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1544">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c27722dbb4b53e6735deee1b8a34e4f2</data>
      <data key="v_content">amadold,Figg, a mad old lady who lived two
streets away.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c27722dbb4b53e6735deee1b8a34e4f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1545">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-673a1027839afb26b0f89279632c9753</data>
      <data key="v_content">The whole house smelled of cabbage
and Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-673a1027839afb26b0f89279632c9753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1546">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eff72621e8343b8277549826ba999802</data>
      <data key="v_content">Figg made him look at photographs of all the cats she&apos;d ever
owned.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eff72621e8343b8277549826ba999802</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1547">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5f5da606272d99d9e3eaca5558811085</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Now what?&quot; said Aunt Petunia, looking furiously at Harry as though he&apos;d
planned this.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5f5da606272d99d9e3eaca5558811085</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1548">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a69f7e446c0184cc0c361bbd412f9b20</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry knew he ought to feel sorry that Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a69f7e446c0184cc0c361bbd412f9b20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1549">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-443429744c4926a1e2d58a019e2fcd6b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Figg had
broken her leg, but it wasn&apos;t easy when he reminded himself it would be
a whole year before he had to look at Tibbles, Snowy, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-443429744c4926a1e2d58a019e2fcd6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1550">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dfe423e02ea6d2d046246c9fd8f9972e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;We could phone Marge,&quot; Uncle Vernon suggested.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dfe423e02ea6d2d046246c9fd8f9972e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1551">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c9b6496bcb67a204da8bc1d836cd773e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Vernon,,&quot;Don&apos;t be silly, Vernon, she hates the boy.&quot;
The Dursleys often spoke about Harry like this, as though he wasn&apos;t
there -- or rather, as though he was something very nasty that couldn&apos;t
understand them, like a slug.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c9b6496bcb67a204da8bc1d836cd773e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1552">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5f6641a3d8147bddf9825822ae069b61</data>
      <data key="v_content">,17
&quot;What about what&apos;s-her-name, your friend -- Yvonne?&quot;
&quot;On vacation in Majorca,&quot; snapped Aunt Petunia.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5f6641a3d8147bddf9825822ae069b61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1553">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a1d25196bbcb72add7e06a77bfcdc69f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You could just leave me here,&quot; Harry put in hopefully (he&apos;d be able to
watch what he wanted on television for a change and maybe even have a go
on Dudley&apos;s computer).</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a1d25196bbcb72add7e06a77bfcdc69f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1554">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2d28da4496e21b7164753de18c0a46be</data>
      <data key="v_content">Aunt Petunia looked as though she&apos;d just swallowed a lemon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2d28da4496e21b7164753de18c0a46be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1555">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9b3c58d3f2780fe08cbe6b43521d820c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;And come back and find the house in ruins?&quot; she snarled.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9b3c58d3f2780fe08cbe6b43521d820c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1556">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1c29b967deb47220c71f5c151760f113</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I won&apos;t blow up the house,&quot; said Harry, but they weren&apos;t listening.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1c29b967deb47220c71f5c151760f113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1557">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f16c6e30654b09a7da1eb45894512b56</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I suppose we could take him to the zoo,&quot; said Aunt Petunia slowly, &quot;...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f16c6e30654b09a7da1eb45894512b56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1558">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-70bac2a11fd0e9e283d027e4f569bbb6</data>
      <data key="v_content">and leave him in the car....&quot;
&quot;That car&apos;s new, he&apos;s not sitting in it alone....&quot;
Dudley began to cry loudly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-70bac2a11fd0e9e283d027e4f569bbb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1559">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-118f41c409ae72e0b4921ff476fa9316</data>
      <data key="v_content">hewasn&apos;t,In fact, he wasn&apos;t really crying -- it had
been years since he&apos;d really cried -- but he knew that if he screwed up
his face and wailed, his mother would give him anything he wanted.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-118f41c409ae72e0b4921ff476fa9316</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1560">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1b5cfc4d643f75ca1f18338814b7c9d8</data>
      <data key="v_content">don&apos;tcry,,&quot;Dinky Duddydums, don&apos;t cry, Mummy won&apos;t let him spoil your special
day!&quot; she cried, flinging her arms around him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1b5cfc4d643f75ca1f18338814b7c9d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1561">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cdb922f3f50e526a706ddf8bc7b35407</data>
      <data key="v_content">t-t-to come!&quot; Dudley yelled between huge,
pretend sobs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cdb922f3f50e526a706ddf8bc7b35407</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1562">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9fc1555deeb3f924b80f78cecd6626b7</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;He always sp- spoils everything!&quot; He shot Harry a nasty
grin through the gap in his mother&apos;s arms.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9fc1555deeb3f924b80f78cecd6626b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1563">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-61ce166a26cf6ded8cc6a560a6e6aedd</data>
      <data key="v_content">thedoorbell,Just then, the doorbell rang -- &quot;Oh, good Lord, they&apos;re here!&quot; said Aunt
Petunia frantically -- and a moment later, Dudley&apos;s best friend, Piers
Polkiss, walked in with his mother.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-61ce166a26cf6ded8cc6a560a6e6aedd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1564">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a15b478bab03caab4bb8a1506e4f8bad</data>
      <data key="v_content">Piers was a scrawny boy with a face
like a rat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a15b478bab03caab4bb8a1506e4f8bad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1565">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3777bdc747313777abc6bceef40c914a</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was usually the one who held people&apos;s arms behind their
backs while Dudley hit them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3777bdc747313777abc6bceef40c914a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1566">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-28c8ebb723b4870d5d179872657156b4</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley stopped pretending to cry at once.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-28c8ebb723b4870d5d179872657156b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1567">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a4a97e38b31548a7089412cfd37fdb68</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Half an hour later, Harry, who couldn&apos;t believe his luck, was sitting in
the back of the Dursleys&apos; car with Piers and Dudley, on the way to the
zoo for the first time in his life.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a4a97e38b31548a7089412cfd37fdb68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1568">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5805d4f9dabc5ebfeb229356763d82d0</data>
      <data key="v_content">His aunt and uncle hadn&apos;t been able
to think of anything else to do with him, but before they&apos;d left, Uncle
Vernon had taken Harry aside.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5805d4f9dabc5ebfeb229356763d82d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1569">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b4aedd2e3ac68cffb813edffb52a8193</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;he,&quot;I&apos;m warning you,&quot; he had said, putting his large purple face right up
18
close to Harry&apos;s, &quot;I&apos;m warning you now, boy -- any funny business,
anything at all -- and you&apos;ll be in that cupboard from now until
Christmas.&quot;
&quot;I&apos;m not going to do anything,&quot; said Harry, &quot;honestly..</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b4aedd2e3ac68cffb813edffb52a8193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1570">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f20dd0654ce2adbd992adb4de13e8e9b</data>
      <data key="v_content">But Uncle Vernon didn&apos;t believe him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f20dd0654ce2adbd992adb4de13e8e9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1571">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3ad85f95c90e016ee6615be9a7d271bc</data>
      <data key="v_content">strange,The problem was, strange things often happened around Harry and it was
just no good telling the Dursleys he didn&apos;t make them happen.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3ad85f95c90e016ee6615be9a7d271bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1572">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1befaeedd0e36c36d2dc33a60258a527</data>
      <data key="v_content">AuntPetunia,tired,Once, Aunt Petunia, tired of Harry coming back from the barbers looking
as though he hadn&apos;t been at all, had taken a pair of kitchen scissors
and cut his hair so short he was almost bald except for his bangs, which
she left &quot;to hide that horrible scar.&quot; Dudley had laughed himself silly
at Harry, who spent a sleepless night imagining school the next day,
where he was already laughed at for his baggy clothes and taped glasses.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1befaeedd0e36c36d2dc33a60258a527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1573">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9c8b50e09118bd256b8ee47f6cd30838</data>
      <data key="v_content">however,he,Next morning, however, he had gotten up to find his hair exactly as it
had been before Aunt Petunia had sheared it off He had been given a week
in his cupboard for this, even though he had tried to explain that he
couldn&apos;t explain how it had grown back so quickly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9c8b50e09118bd256b8ee47f6cd30838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1574">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3e9931a51a4c8c7d15c94bfffaa36717</data>
      <data key="v_content">AuntPetunia,Another time, Aunt Petunia had been trying to force him into a revolting
old sweater of Dudley&apos;s (brown with orange puff balls) -- The harder she
tried to pull it over his head, the smaller it seemed to become, until
finally it might have fitted a hand puppet, but certainly wouldn&apos;t fit
Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3e9931a51a4c8c7d15c94bfffaa36717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1575">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e6faec8e7a95c971cf1b027c62de56c0</data>
      <data key="v_content">Aunt Petunia had decided it must have shrunk in the wash and, to
his great relief, Harry wasn&apos;t punished.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e6faec8e7a95c971cf1b027c62de56c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1576">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1b836589ddfbff791a1f61229cf12c24</data>
      <data key="v_content">,On the other hand, he&apos;d gotten into terrible trouble for being found on
the roof of the school kitchens.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1b836589ddfbff791a1f61229cf12c24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1577">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dbde53fbb10b2f38018553d75f904c4b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley&apos;s gang had been chasing him as
usual when, as much to Harry&apos;s surprise as anyone else&apos;s, there he was
sitting on the chimney.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dbde53fbb10b2f38018553d75f904c4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1578">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4c716a226a99ff5d22ff809b4194e044</data>
      <data key="v_content">The Dursleys had received a very angry letter
from Harry&apos;s headmistress telling them Harry had been climbing school
buildings.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4c716a226a99ff5d22ff809b4194e044</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1579">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d50ee495d240d85f0fab63df0568904a</data>
      <data key="v_content">But all he&apos;d tried to do (as he shouted at Uncle Vernon
through the locked door of his cupboard) was jump behind the big trash
cans outside the kitchen doors.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d50ee495d240d85f0fab63df0568904a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1580">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-21882eb2fdabd337505c3ce69f9ed2cf</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry supposed that the wind must have
caught him in mid- jump.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-21882eb2fdabd337505c3ce69f9ed2cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1581">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-39d34594f4601c4e52238adb69d67739</data>
      <data key="v_content">nothingwas,But today, nothing was going to go wrong.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-39d34594f4601c4e52238adb69d67739</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1582">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e8415ad12e4c6cab9f0b38d569a33381</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was even worth being with
Dudley and Piers to be spending the day somewhere that wasn&apos;t school,
his cupboard, or Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e8415ad12e4c6cab9f0b38d569a33381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1583">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c77eb8266ec3b346a296b76e1da573f0</data>
      <data key="v_content">,19
While he drove, Uncle Vernon complained to Aunt Petunia.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c77eb8266ec3b346a296b76e1da573f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1584">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-77a6fea12a470b46c8a6e2d3d514d189</data>
      <data key="v_content">He liked to
complain about things: people at work, Harry, the council, Harry, the
bank, and Harry were just a few of his favorite subjects.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-77a6fea12a470b46c8a6e2d3d514d189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1585">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6b859044a40338afaa83a2e51cc9b65d</data>
      <data key="v_content">,roaring along like maniacs, the young hoodlums,&quot; he said, as a
motorcycle overtook them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6b859044a40338afaa83a2e51cc9b65d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1586">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-952dee41a73fdae288ead771de3df7ac</data>
      <data key="v_content">I had a dream about a motorcycle,&quot; said Harry, remembering suddenly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-952dee41a73fdae288ead771de3df7ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1587">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-835fd0070054112329051c2b46b9c3a6</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;It
was flying.&quot;
Uncle Vernon nearly crashed into the car in front.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-835fd0070054112329051c2b46b9c3a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1588">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cb6026a7877042f8ac9e82791a8551e0</data>
      <data key="v_content">He turned right
around in his seat and yelled at Harry, his face like a gigantic beet
with a mustache: &quot;MOTORCYCLES DON&apos;T FLY!&quot;
Dudley and Piers sniggered.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cb6026a7877042f8ac9e82791a8551e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1589">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-30e3ce935c6609fc4c7af8d3224a53dd</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,I know they don&apos;t,&quot; said Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-30e3ce935c6609fc4c7af8d3224a53dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1590">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5cc60ee92150ce772fa2ae2a153ab71d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;It was only a dream.&quot;
But he wished he hadn&apos;t said anything.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5cc60ee92150ce772fa2ae2a153ab71d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1591">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e5682e0dd53b546bd5855bcc3fb40e79</data>
      <data key="v_content">If there was one thing the
Dursleys hated even more than his asking questions, it was his talking
about anything acting in a way it shouldn&apos;t, no matter if it was in a
dream or even a cartoon -- they seemed to think he might get dangerous
ideas.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e5682e0dd53b546bd5855bcc3fb40e79</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1592">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-083f6e94ba27c0edcb8a875b5bc7b383</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was a very sunny Saturday and the zoo was crowded with families.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-083f6e94ba27c0edcb8a875b5bc7b383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1593">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8d8b9d4f6e936193b07b23226bdcac14</data>
      <data key="v_content">The
Dursleys bought Dudley and Piers large chocolate ice creams at the
entrance and then, because the smiling lady in the van had asked Harry
what he wanted before they could hurry him away, they bought him a cheap
lemon ice pop.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8d8b9d4f6e936193b07b23226bdcac14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1594">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b68ed02cb1f6f1fbd41ec4da9c37639c</data>
      <data key="v_content">either,,It wasn&apos;t bad, either, Harry thought, licking it as they
watched a gorilla scratching its head who looked remarkably like Dudley,
except that it wasn&apos;t blond.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b68ed02cb1f6f1fbd41ec4da9c37639c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1595">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-87be45662596ef9c883a7531e0ce3d62</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry had the best morning he&apos;d had in a long time.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-87be45662596ef9c883a7531e0ce3d62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1596">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d6161a713594c50e0aba417e2a90614e</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was careful to
walk a little way apart from the Dursleys so that Dudley and Piers, who
were starting to get bored with the animals by lunchtime, wouldn&apos;t fall
back on their favorite hobby of hitting him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d6161a713594c50e0aba417e2a90614e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1597">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2d7135051a6b05ea51f1ea99351cd2a8</data>
      <data key="v_content">They ate in the zoo
restaurant, and when Dudley had a tantrum because his knickerbocker
glory didn&apos;t have enough ice cream on top, Uncle Vernon bought him
another one and Harry was allowed to finish the first.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2d7135051a6b05ea51f1ea99351cd2a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1598">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-121ffab4d6f5d716bfc5fe384048f4a5</data>
      <data key="v_content">afterward,that,Harry felt, afterward, that he should have known it was all too good to
last.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-121ffab4d6f5d716bfc5fe384048f4a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1599">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-230d3957798c487748fadfb15211229f</data>
      <data key="v_content">20
After lunch they went to the reptile house.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-230d3957798c487748fadfb15211229f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1600">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4fd767d09ecbb8bea40fe068d6ebb236</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was cool and dark in
there, with lit windows all along the walls.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4fd767d09ecbb8bea40fe068d6ebb236</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1601">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1701f38a12eda2a41fc389cf36f3d629</data>
      <data key="v_content">all,Behind the glass, all sorts
of lizards and snakes were crawling and slithering over bits of wood and
stone.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1701f38a12eda2a41fc389cf36f3d629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1602">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1ae022421109cb8aa77f5947228a1bf5</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley and Piers wanted to see huge, poisonous cobras and thick,
man-crushing pythons.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1ae022421109cb8aa77f5947228a1bf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1603">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4a1c4634f552c2fd0100a28c6838fad0</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley quickly found the largest snake in the
place.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4a1c4634f552c2fd0100a28c6838fad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1604">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-66861f5b47ba8cd741d9f3f0854d128c</data>
      <data key="v_content">It could have wrapped its body twice around Uncle Vernon&apos;s car
and crushed it into a trash can -- but at the moment it didn&apos;t look in
the mood.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-66861f5b47ba8cd741d9f3f0854d128c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1605">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fbc0d01fbeb1bd3a6c2975f5c3b38978</data>
      <data key="v_content">itwas,In fact, it was fast asleep.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fbc0d01fbeb1bd3a6c2975f5c3b38978</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1606">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6f26ec27ddb4380709bd84881b65e29c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley stood with his nose pressed against the glass, staring at the
glistening brown coils.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6f26ec27ddb4380709bd84881b65e29c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1607">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3d6378dd8640bc3e2795b88fc9ab6111</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;he,&quot;Make it move,&quot; he whined at his father.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3d6378dd8640bc3e2795b88fc9ab6111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1608">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-618ca97cfb16f353b47a78d3309a1896</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon tapped on the
glass, but the snake didn&apos;t budge.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-618ca97cfb16f353b47a78d3309a1896</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1609">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9174e5559cd111da9f6ee96f1b4308d3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon rapped the glass smartly
with his knuckles, but the snake just snoozed on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9174e5559cd111da9f6ee96f1b4308d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1610">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eb97d0eb41d7f029c282f03447fc8850</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry moved in front of the tank and looked intently at the snake.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eb97d0eb41d7f029c282f03447fc8850</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1611">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f0fd51a6a752e613c0b268e1943236e0</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
wouldn&apos;t have been surprised if it had died of boredom itself -- no
company except stupid people drumming their fingers on the glass trying
to disturb it all day long.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f0fd51a6a752e613c0b268e1943236e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1612">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-28c94d8c884a3f10cd362632b3c60f7e</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was worse than having a cupboard as a
bedroom, where the only visitor was Aunt Petunia hammering on the door
to wake you up; at least he got to visit the rest of the house.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-28c94d8c884a3f10cd362632b3c60f7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1613">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-27009f89e03dce094cdb8d8b273df74d</data>
      <data key="v_content">The snake suddenly opened its beady eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-27009f89e03dce094cdb8d8b273df74d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1614">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-14c404e075a5578c2763d0d1bda67500</data>
      <data key="v_content">veryslowly,it,Slowly, very slowly, it raised
its head until its eyes were on a level with Harry&apos;s.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-14c404e075a5578c2763d0d1bda67500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1615">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ca56b2c4b32685668de9c1437a49e11d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Then he looked quickly around to see if anyone was
watching.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ca56b2c4b32685668de9c1437a49e11d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1616">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b5fa3f485663311c5976c5515d62d87c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He looked back at the snake and winked, too.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b5fa3f485663311c5976c5515d62d87c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1617">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9e27ef9259b1921c0918bae1973e708e</data>
      <data key="v_content">The snake jerked its head toward Uncle Vernon and Dudley, then raised
its eyes to the ceiling.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9e27ef9259b1921c0918bae1973e708e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1618">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8a2299a9e4c4aca5387625273e47438e</data>
      <data key="v_content">It gave Harry a look that said quite plainly:
&quot;I get that all the time.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8a2299a9e4c4aca5387625273e47438e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1619">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4cefb7c0ea3e46391e4c4fcb3f1128be</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Harrymurmured,&quot;I know,&quot; Harry murmured through the glass, though he wasn&apos;t sure the
snake could hear him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4cefb7c0ea3e46391e4c4fcb3f1128be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1620">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6cb1924b7a910b308c943ec0b63d967a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;It must be really annoying.&quot;
21
The snake nodded vigorously.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6cb1924b7a910b308c943ec0b63d967a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1621">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b8082a658b47bcef4ac2f6cb60ce73d7</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Where do you come from, anyway?&quot; Harry asked.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b8082a658b47bcef4ac2f6cb60ce73d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1622">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0091247987811e0533d88215b92ca44a</data>
      <data key="v_content">The snake jabbed its tail at a little sign next to the glass.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0091247987811e0533d88215b92ca44a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1623">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eaa4ab6c513de0e5c3c782b550aaf06d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Was it nice there?&quot;
The boa constrictor jabbed its tail at the sign again and Harry read on:
This specimen was bred in the zoo.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eaa4ab6c513de0e5c3c782b550aaf06d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1624">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9ee68b6744446464327792a9a842ebc1</data>
      <data key="v_content">Isee--,&quot;Oh, I see -- so you&apos;ve never been to
Brazil?&quot;
As the snake shook its head, a deafening shout behind Harry made both of
them jump.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9ee68b6744446464327792a9a842ebc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1625">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ad08803da7d0f00fbb5c09c794546e42</data>
      <data key="v_content">DURSLEY! COME AND LOOK AT THIS SNAKE! YOU
WON&apos;T BELIEVE
WHAT IT&apos;S DOING!&quot;
Dudley came waddling toward them as fast as he could.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ad08803da7d0f00fbb5c09c794546e42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1626">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fbe11e850b3bad288cfdce363094daef</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Out of the way, you,&quot; he said, punching Harry in the ribs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fbe11e850b3bad288cfdce363094daef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1627">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2ef26edab0fa54caa993c9f65e0b2af7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry,Caught by
surprise, Harry fell hard on the concrete floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2ef26edab0fa54caa993c9f65e0b2af7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1628">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b4db9ea9a0f606e6608f91d57044aca1</data>
      <data key="v_content">What came next happened
so fast no one saw how it happened -- one second, Piers and Dudley were
leaning right up close to the glass, the next, they had leapt back with
howls of horror.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b4db9ea9a0f606e6608f91d57044aca1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1629">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-14b85c108805b2f2bbb76ca73a6b8b8d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry sat up and gasped; the glass front of the boa constrictor&apos;s tank
had vanished.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-14b85c108805b2f2bbb76ca73a6b8b8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1630">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7b352927f220d6eb305b58f69ed73c2a</data>
      <data key="v_content">The great snake was uncoiling itself rapidly, slithering
out onto the floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7b352927f220d6eb305b58f69ed73c2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1631">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d593a1df1aad462b525ba3fa1107a8b3</data>
      <data key="v_content">People throughout the reptile house screamed and
started running for the exits.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d593a1df1aad462b525ba3fa1107a8b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1632">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ee2e23663fb9411e1c9931649ddea96c</data>
      <data key="v_content">As the snake slid swiftly past him, Harry could have sworn a low,
hissing voice said, &quot;Brazil, here I come....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ee2e23663fb9411e1c9931649ddea96c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1633">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d00bcac889f2f1aeed0332fc7879348c</data>
      <data key="v_content">amigo.&quot;Thekeeper,Thanksss, amigo.&quot;
The keeper of the reptile house was in shock.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d00bcac889f2f1aeed0332fc7879348c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1634">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b63c2fc0f2b80d832232c4d18dda5650</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;he,&quot;But the glass,&quot; he kept saying, &quot;where did the glass go?&quot;
22
The zoo director himself made Aunt Petunia a cup of strong, sweet tea
while he apologized over and over again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b63c2fc0f2b80d832232c4d18dda5650</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1635">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cb037ca8e9bf5ae74e31f10428658d7c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Piers and Dudley could only
gibber.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cb037ca8e9bf5ae74e31f10428658d7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1636">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bb7162917b43ba6461c2a54afdd0b62d</data>
      <data key="v_content">As far as Harry had seen, the snake hadn&apos;t done anything except
snap playfully at their heels as it passed, but by the time they were
all back in Uncle Vernon&apos;s car, Dudley was telling them how it had
nearly bitten off his leg, while Piers was swearing it had tried to
squeeze him to death.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bb7162917b43ba6461c2a54afdd0b62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1637">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fbe391136c537c9455d4e14f145418c2</data>
      <data key="v_content">,But worst of all, for Harry at least, was Piers
calming down enough to say, &quot;Harry was talking to it, weren&apos;t you,
Harry?&quot;
Uncle Vernon waited until Piers was safely out of the house before
starting on Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fbe391136c537c9455d4e14f145418c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1638">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1ac46f94514fc1c00f2c18eae82cf73f</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was so angry he could hardly speak.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1ac46f94514fc1c00f2c18eae82cf73f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1639">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-af9d0a28ba2eef989a0d05172717b786</data>
      <data key="v_content">,He managed to
say, &quot;Go -- cupboard -- stay -- no meals,&quot; before he collapsed into a
chair, and Aunt Petunia had to run and get him a large brandy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-af9d0a28ba2eef989a0d05172717b786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1640">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4bd43263dcb63439d74725196acf5121</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry lay in his dark cupboard much later, wishing he had a watch.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4bd43263dcb63439d74725196acf5121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1641">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a259097c07e9f8087a7c3b0584dab75e</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
didn&apos;t know what time it was and he couldn&apos;t be sure the Dursleys were
asleep yet.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a259097c07e9f8087a7c3b0584dab75e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1642">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-82c2b6ea6dcafb686680e02500d93ec6</data>
      <data key="v_content">he,Until they were, he couldn&apos;t risk sneaking to the kitchen
for some food.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-82c2b6ea6dcafb686680e02500d93ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1643">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9d1b28456c42ccbe48e5224bd5ca4a4b</data>
      <data key="v_content">He&apos;d lived with the Dursleys almost ten years, ten miserable years, as
long as he could remember, ever since he&apos;d been a baby and his parents
had died in that car crash.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9d1b28456c42ccbe48e5224bd5ca4a4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1644">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6e9bf9939230723a1160b3008873add9</data>
      <data key="v_content">He couldn&apos;t remember being in the car when
his parents had died.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6e9bf9939230723a1160b3008873add9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1645">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7e5e31a52212928920853e49ed6a5e1e</data>
      <data key="v_content">whenhestrained,Sometimes, when he strained his memory during long
hours in his cupboard, he came up with a strange vision: a blinding
flash of green light and a burn- ing pain on his forehead.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7e5e31a52212928920853e49ed6a5e1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1646">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c4e40a0e602e3d81b1ae83c5e9d32085</data>
      <data key="v_content">hesupposed,was,This, he
supposed, was the crash, though he couldn&apos;t imagine where all the green
light came from.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c4e40a0e602e3d81b1ae83c5e9d32085</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1647">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-478b405f19bf62259d24fe17cd947c61</data>
      <data key="v_content">He couldn&apos;t remember his parents at all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-478b405f19bf62259d24fe17cd947c61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1648">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-48038cf0c2ed7fa5f44dbac9aa683369</data>
      <data key="v_content">His aunt and
uncle never spoke about them, and of course he was forbidden to ask
questions.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-48038cf0c2ed7fa5f44dbac9aa683369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1649">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c21278837c13d18daba6899ec02acbb7</data>
      <data key="v_content">There were no photographs of them in the house.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c21278837c13d18daba6899ec02acbb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1650">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e71e52c42665abc0192798ad718c3660</data>
      <data key="v_content">When he had been younger, Harry had dreamed and dreamed of some unknown
relation coming to take him away, but it had never happened; the
Dursleys were his only family.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e71e52c42665abc0192798ad718c3660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1651">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-474a69575d0ddfcab0187775b2746f5b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Yet sometimes he thought (or maybe hoped)
that strangers in the street seemed to know him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-474a69575d0ddfcab0187775b2746f5b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1652">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1822091492afa291c0167a09e1317345</data>
      <data key="v_content">Very strange strangers
they were, too.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1822091492afa291c0167a09e1317345</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1653">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-429675e41f83f5fdd1907e6db5dfc4b2</data>
      <data key="v_content">A tiny man in a violet top hat had bowed to him once
while out shopping with Aunt Petunia and Dudley.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-429675e41f83f5fdd1907e6db5dfc4b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1654">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1847dae2665d3c275f3caa2efcbf78e7</data>
      <data key="v_content">After asking Harry
furiously if he knew the man, Aunt Petunia had rushed them out of the
shop without buying anything.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1847dae2665d3c275f3caa2efcbf78e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1655">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ffc220f371127ee9ce9db304d81eb639</data>
      <data key="v_content">A wild-looking old woman dressed all in
green had waved merrily at him once on a bus.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ffc220f371127ee9ce9db304d81eb639</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1656">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4e32c3d0d59df25c6bc3e7b9659cc192</data>
      <data key="v_content">A bald man in a very long
purple coat had actually shaken his hand in the street the other day and
then walked away without a word.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4e32c3d0d59df25c6bc3e7b9659cc192</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1657">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e3076337f41b26e68c0280ee16f35777</data>
      <data key="v_content">The weirdest thing about all these
people was the way they seemed to vanish the second Harry tried to get a
23
closer look.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e3076337f41b26e68c0280ee16f35777</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1658">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6ce2e3896856c433c7757a00a188be21</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harryhad,At school, Harry had no one.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6ce2e3896856c433c7757a00a188be21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1659">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a3daeb3e09151ef186fb54171a1a40f1</data>
      <data key="v_content">Everybody knew that Dudley&apos;s gang hated
that odd Harry Potter in his baggy old clothes and broken glasses, and
nobody liked to disagree with Dudley&apos;s gang.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a3daeb3e09151ef186fb54171a1a40f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1660">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-97bc978a65cc62bb8f64bc611636da48</data>
      <data key="v_content">CHAPTER THREE
THE LETTERS FROM NO ONE
The escape of the Brazilian boa constrictor earned Harry his
longest-ever punishment.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-97bc978a65cc62bb8f64bc611636da48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1661">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9a65afeab4013f61c5762c5b379a402a</data>
      <data key="v_content">By the time he was allowed out of his cupboard
again, the summer holidays had started and Dudley had already broken his
new video camera, crashed his remote control airplane, and, first time
out on his racing bike, knocked down old Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9a65afeab4013f61c5762c5b379a402a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1662">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c72e8616313243913444723bcda620e6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Figg as she crossed Privet
Drive on her crutches.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c72e8616313243913444723bcda620e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1663">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-abc9353d92deb35378051e4f9fd91cc0</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry was glad school was over, but there was no escaping Dudley&apos;s gang,
who visited the house every single day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-abc9353d92deb35378051e4f9fd91cc0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1664">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-41362ea3dfc648c79c8d13bbacd011e0</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dennis,Malcolm,and,Piers, Dennis, Malcolm, and
Gordon were all big and stupid, but as Dudley was the biggest and
stupidest of the lot, he was the leader.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-41362ea3dfc648c79c8d13bbacd011e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1665">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-08c2b0994b454e6d570448fa1e5b8a97</data>
      <data key="v_content">The rest of them were all quite
happy to join in Dudley&apos;s favorite sport: Harry Hunting.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-08c2b0994b454e6d570448fa1e5b8a97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1666">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-526418acd5a566e38ff474ec053f12e1</data>
      <data key="v_content">This was why Harry spent as much time as possible out of the house,
wandering around and thinking about the end of the holidays, where he
could see a tiny ray of hope.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-526418acd5a566e38ff474ec053f12e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1667">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3b6f3df390725f4fc2d8d358735abfcf</data>
      <data key="v_content">When September came he would be going off
to secondary school and, for the first time in his life, he wouldn&apos;t be
with Dudley.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3b6f3df390725f4fc2d8d358735abfcf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1668">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-79088a70d818c0d3cfcb2300b436f46f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley had been accepted at Uncle Vernon&apos;s old private
school, Smeltings.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-79088a70d818c0d3cfcb2300b436f46f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1669">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cd6551a9c4cf75b24042a264e1838e89</data>
      <data key="v_content">Piers Polkiss was going there too.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cd6551a9c4cf75b24042a264e1838e89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1670">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c40412bb3fbb6b4b12ff392a02562e9a</data>
      <data key="v_content">ontheother,Harry, on the
other hand, was going to Stonewall High, the local public school.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c40412bb3fbb6b4b12ff392a02562e9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1671">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4f78ebe798c07b2a5d4b768036db1eac</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley
thought this was very funny.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4f78ebe798c07b2a5d4b768036db1eac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1672">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f24705cead5ce4a3e68139b7ff792cf5</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;They stuff people&apos;s heads down the toilet the first day at Stonewall,&quot;
he told Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f24705cead5ce4a3e68139b7ff792cf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1673">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4225b524689c1612cdb3261303dc8b36</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Want to come upstairs and practice?&quot;
&quot;No, thanks,&quot; said Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4225b524689c1612cdb3261303dc8b36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1674">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f467f221150878c1ac3f407401f76b90</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;The poor toilet&apos;s never had anything as
horrible as your head down it -- it might be sick.&quot; Then he ran, before
Dudley could work out what he&apos;d said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f467f221150878c1ac3f407401f76b90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1675">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0c365dc5e13ce173a65fbaf1dd138584</data>
      <data key="v_content">,One day in July, Aunt Petunia took Dudley to London to buy his Smeltings
uniform, leaving Harry at Mrs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0c365dc5e13ce173a65fbaf1dd138584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1676">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d84c011ae8bc5929fd729cb949b42b95</data>
      <data key="v_content">Figg wasn &apos;t as bad as
usual.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d84c011ae8bc5929fd729cb949b42b95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1677">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-408426748b6aca4f68bd75b1488b25a9</data>
      <data key="v_content">It turned out she&apos;d broken her leg tripping over one of her cats,
24
and she didn&apos;t seem quite as fond of them as before.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-408426748b6aca4f68bd75b1488b25a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1678">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-193365419708102e9491345e42746604</data>
      <data key="v_content">She let Harry watch
television and gave him a bit of chocolate cake that tasted as though
she&apos;d had it for several years.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-193365419708102e9491345e42746604</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1679">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ffde28ac0c91ed376f4e3f7faccc0da6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudleyparaded,That evening, Dudley paraded around the living room for the family in
his brand-new uniform.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ffde28ac0c91ed376f4e3f7faccc0da6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1680">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-10785af6d7850dae379641b0fa41449d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Smeltings&apos; boys wore maroon tailcoats, orange
knickerbockers, and flat straw hats called boaters.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-10785af6d7850dae379641b0fa41449d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1681">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-27b73c6856a2d7511dc20001223d8254</data>
      <data key="v_content">They also carried
knobbly sticks, used for hitting each other while the teachers weren&apos;t
looking.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-27b73c6856a2d7511dc20001223d8254</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1682">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4c2ca7bdca20c5d84bae17412bd066d0</data>
      <data key="v_content">This was supposed to be good training for later life.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4c2ca7bdca20c5d84bae17412bd066d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1683">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-991b7bd5400038d43ce9e693a3f84737</data>
      <data key="v_content">As he looked at Dudley in his new knickerbockers, Uncle Vernon said
gruffly that it was the proudest moment of his life.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-991b7bd5400038d43ce9e693a3f84737</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1684">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4b18c105fff5068d3a57c305d8c4568a</data>
      <data key="v_content">Aunt Petunia burst
into tears and said she couldn&apos;t believe it was her Ickle Dudleykins, he
looked so handsome and grown-up.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4b18c105fff5068d3a57c305d8c4568a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1685">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f583946f2270273a03c2cc5df785eb02</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry didn&apos;t trust himself to speak.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f583946f2270273a03c2cc5df785eb02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1686">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d0b0385057634ba9c7915ca0cc2efb5f</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
thought two of his ribs might already have cracked from trying not to
laugh.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d0b0385057634ba9c7915ca0cc2efb5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1687">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4085252dd57486f7c4eb745151fa9c7f</data>
      <data key="v_content">There was a horrible smell in the kitchen the next morning when Harry
went in for breakfast.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4085252dd57486f7c4eb745151fa9c7f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1688">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0071dc22c97a02a86ba27e444e373cb1</data>
      <data key="v_content">It seemed to be coming from a large metal tub in
the sink.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0071dc22c97a02a86ba27e444e373cb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1689">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-feb26f86624e4b1ab5f0bf2bd2cab0ec</data>
      <data key="v_content">He went to have a look.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-feb26f86624e4b1ab5f0bf2bd2cab0ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1690">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-092c51739f3d4cf09bd9006022256e48</data>
      <data key="v_content">The tub was full of what looked like
dirty rags swimming in gray water.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-092c51739f3d4cf09bd9006022256e48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1691">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6cf9fc3e387448a69f77b8ea23e40580</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;What&apos;s this?&quot; he asked Aunt Petunia.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6cf9fc3e387448a69f77b8ea23e40580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1692">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-41468ff778b12ff7070ff6e17b95fa75</data>
      <data key="v_content">Her lips tightened as they always
did if he dared to ask a question.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-41468ff778b12ff7070ff6e17b95fa75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1693">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1a7707cdacf15f43876d4c422b0460ce</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;Your new school uniform,&quot; she said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1a7707cdacf15f43876d4c422b0460ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1694">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-de1cb1170c0cc3dc8e942e1bbdb5bcd5</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry looked in the bowl again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-de1cb1170c0cc3dc8e942e1bbdb5bcd5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1695">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7570b1b88be26e6ab5183aee5a93ec76</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;hesaid,&quot;I,&quot;Oh,&quot; he said, &quot;I didn&apos;t realize it had to be so wet.&quot;
&quot;DotA be stupid,&quot; snapped Aunt Petunia.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7570b1b88be26e6ab5183aee5a93ec76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1696">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-31ec8905745c4da1de57bb97f0382102</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I&apos;m dyeing some of Dudley&apos;s old
things gray for you.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-31ec8905745c4da1de57bb97f0382102</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1697">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-744df510fa2b6289d89befd075277816</data>
      <data key="v_content">It&apos;ll look just like everyone else&apos;s when I&apos;ve
finished.&quot;
Harry seriously doubted this, but thought it best not to argue.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-744df510fa2b6289d89befd075277816</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1698">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2e53a758ed668619b24f6677737d9807</data>
      <data key="v_content">He sat
down at the table and tried not to think about how he was going to look
on his first day at Stonewall High -- like he was wearing bits of old
elephant skin, probably.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2e53a758ed668619b24f6677737d9807</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1699">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-da3d3ab0ef82c71de2c9c638052ccbb4</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley and Uncle Vernon came in, both with wrinkled noses because of the
smell from Harry&apos;s new uniform.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-da3d3ab0ef82c71de2c9c638052ccbb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1700">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-63133846d5038b1ccafdc76fa69135c5</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon opened his newspaper as
usual and Dudley banged his Smelting stick, which he carried everywhere,
25
on the table.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-63133846d5038b1ccafdc76fa69135c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1701">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-66bc97e9ffe9b96d0d6cdf2832c8679a</data>
      <data key="v_content">They heard the click of the mail slot and flop of letters on the
doormat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-66bc97e9ffe9b96d0d6cdf2832c8679a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1702">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b96377a6d3bc6b69306049838954c8ba</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley,&quot;,&quot;Get the mail, Dudley,&quot; said Uncle Vernon from behind his paper.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b96377a6d3bc6b69306049838954c8ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1703">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c9199fe19c3b13714340162a50ce3760</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Make Harry get it.&quot;
&quot;Get the mail, Harry.&quot;
&quot;Make Dudley get it.&quot;
&quot;Poke him with your Smelting stick, Dudley.&quot;
Harry dodged the Smelting stick and went to get the mail.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c9199fe19c3b13714340162a50ce3760</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1704">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-737a78d4a79b1957736643d03887ef5a</data>
      <data key="v_content">Three things
lay on the doormat: a postcard from Uncle Vernon&apos;s sister Marge, who was
vacationing on the Isle of Wight, a brown envelope that looked like a
bill, and -- a letter for Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-737a78d4a79b1957736643d03887ef5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1705">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8bc10b51bccb9f60f2813611089703dc</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry picked it up and stared at it, his heart twanging like a giant
elastic band.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8bc10b51bccb9f60f2813611089703dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1706">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3515df8ccd6150ee2b63ef18ec22532e</data>
      <data key="v_content">ever,in,No one, ever, in his whole life, had written to him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3515df8ccd6150ee2b63ef18ec22532e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1707">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dc576d1544745052b9cbe22ad1354c76</data>
      <data key="v_content">Who
would? He had no friends, no other relatives -- he didn&apos;t belong to the
library, so he&apos;d never even got rude notes asking for books back.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dc576d1544745052b9cbe22ad1354c76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1708">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-33212c18e120f38dd107dd302b2618f5</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Yet
here it was, a letter, addressed so plainly there could be no mistake:
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-33212c18e120f38dd107dd302b2618f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1709">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-572ddf2ef900636da2d0bb4ea9da631b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Potter
The Cupboard under the Stairs
4 Privet Drive
Little Whinging
Surrey
The envelope was thick and heavy, made of yellowish parchment, and the
address was written in emerald-green ink.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-572ddf2ef900636da2d0bb4ea9da631b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1710">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b907b67331b83207d6e8a9415efd4441</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Turning the envelope over, his hand trembling, Harry saw a purple wax
seal bearing a coat of arms; a lion, an eagle, a badger, and a snake
surrounding a large letter H.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b907b67331b83207d6e8a9415efd4441</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1711">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-870ae1353a6cd3ff092c7f12731af713</data>
      <data key="v_content">boy!&quot;,26
&quot;Hurry up, boy!&quot; shouted Uncle Vernon from the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-870ae1353a6cd3ff092c7f12731af713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1712">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c00958f3ac664775ac74bbfaaae5c48d</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;What are you
doing, checking for letter bombs?&quot; He chuckled at his own joke.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c00958f3ac664775ac74bbfaaae5c48d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1713">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f2d6045a495a2d86c5dba8fc05f40695</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry went back to the kitchen, still staring at his letter.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f2d6045a495a2d86c5dba8fc05f40695</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1714">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1966fa781974487454b5adf8b8abd7c9</data>
      <data key="v_content">He handed
Uncle Vernon the bill and the postcard, sat down, and slowly began to
open the yellow envelope.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1966fa781974487454b5adf8b8abd7c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1715">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-163c8ebe4fb1bbb6a1c041a0ec49ed61</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon ripped open the bill, snorted in disgust, and flipped over
the postcard.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-163c8ebe4fb1bbb6a1c041a0ec49ed61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1716">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-191e831454afbb00b5c314b2312f3f4e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;heinformed,&quot;Marge&apos;s ill,&quot; he informed Aunt Petunia.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-191e831454afbb00b5c314b2312f3f4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1717">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f368b40ce1ba5c56357131bc7fc973af</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry&apos;sgotsomething!&quot;,&quot;Dad, Harry&apos;s got something!&quot;
Harry was on the point of unfolding his letter, which was written on the
same heavy parchment as the envelope, when it was jerked sharply out of
his hand by Uncle Vernon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f368b40ce1ba5c56357131bc7fc973af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1718">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0f0d1916f2f51b701ec7090a183a76d6</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;That&apos;s mine!&quot; said Harry, trying to snatch it back.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0f0d1916f2f51b701ec7090a183a76d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1719">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-57f2f4afa92283bdbe5c93255b421822</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Who&apos;d be writing to you?&quot; sneered Uncle Vernon, shaking the letter open
with one hand and glancing at it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-57f2f4afa92283bdbe5c93255b421822</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1720">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4b019f894de90954dde8235389fb83cf</data>
      <data key="v_content">His face went from red to green faster
than a set of traffic lights.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4b019f894de90954dde8235389fb83cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1721">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-876ab3681b46292cd6b260c1067c6cb7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Within seconds
it was the grayish white of old porridge.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-876ab3681b46292cd6b260c1067c6cb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1722">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9791cc4625b66679c28a0ff11504f99f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley tried to grab the letter to read it, but Uncle Vernon held it
high out of his reach.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9791cc4625b66679c28a0ff11504f99f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1723">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2b3c1723f6a7d335fd23706f63b1af9e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Aunt Petunia took it curiously and read the first
line.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2b3c1723f6a7d335fd23706f63b1af9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1724">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b7163525cff9da7f9612eb8ec6f710dd</data>
      <data key="v_content">For a moment it looked as though she might faint.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b7163525cff9da7f9612eb8ec6f710dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1725">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c22bcdca6a20a97b4368ebab02a04cc6</data>
      <data key="v_content">She clutched her
throat and made a choking noise.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c22bcdca6a20a97b4368ebab02a04cc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1726">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2440aa215320bc87e9b6bad9461d5a5e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Vernon! Oh my goodness -- Vernon!&quot;
They stared at each other, seeming to have forgotten that Harry and
Dudley were still in the room.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2440aa215320bc87e9b6bad9461d5a5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1727">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-27a8e304ecb383cab19ebe74242ae09c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley wasn&apos;t used to being ignored.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-27a8e304ecb383cab19ebe74242ae09c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1728">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7392ef6f5992899e2e37d2a548a8907b</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
gave his father a sharp tap on the head with his Smelting stick.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7392ef6f5992899e2e37d2a548a8907b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1729">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-79d034f1f6aa54150a6ef75f06979bc0</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I want to read that letter,&quot; he said loudly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-79d034f1f6aa54150a6ef75f06979bc0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1730">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e9e2dadc52e4f68bb87f4b3c4313937c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,want to read it,&quot; said
Harry furiously, &quot;as it&apos;s mine.&quot;
&quot;Get out, both of you,&quot; croaked Uncle Vernon, stuffing the letter back
inside its envelope.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e9e2dadc52e4f68bb87f4b3c4313937c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1731">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b140652464c58337823293963d669ea4</data>
      <data key="v_content">I WANT MY LETTER!&quot; he shouted.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b140652464c58337823293963d669ea4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1732">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eff77988bd473c58d0d6321313ac3135</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Let me see it!&quot; demanded Dudley.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eff77988bd473c58d0d6321313ac3135</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1733">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b56bb0e1fa53450a5ad96cd347ff18c3</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;OUT!&quot; roared Uncle Vernon, and he took both Harry and Dudley by the
scruffs of their necks and threw them into the hall, slamming the
kitchen door behind them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b56bb0e1fa53450a5ad96cd347ff18c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1734">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dea04fd130febb96e8f0c8c03b8a915f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry and Dudley promptly had a furious but
silent fight over who would listen at the keyhole; Dudley won, so Harry,
his glasses dangling from one ear, lay flat on his stomach to listen at
the crack between door and floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dea04fd130febb96e8f0c8c03b8a915f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1735">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-63e77337a5b00784f7f9a2a7dcd409fb</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;AuntPetuniawas,&quot;Vernon,&quot; Aunt Petunia was saying in a quivering voice, &quot;look at the
address -- how could they possibly know where he sleeps? You don&apos;t think
they&apos;re watching the house?&quot;
&quot;Watching -- spying -- might be following us,&quot; muttered Uncle Vernon
wildly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-63e77337a5b00784f7f9a2a7dcd409fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1736">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8b50ee8a16a9b44897e9f7c0f0cdbaf1</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But what should we do, Vernon? Should we write back? Tell them we don&apos;t
want --&quot;
Harry could see Uncle Vernon&apos;s shiny black shoes pacing up and down the
kitchen.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8b50ee8a16a9b44897e9f7c0f0cdbaf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1737">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3f3aa4cb040948775c1e7938b749a923</data>
      <data key="v_content">If they don&apos;t get an
answer...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3f3aa4cb040948775c1e7938b749a923</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1738">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f850b0291b3705752615ccea706eb257</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But --&quot;
&quot;I&apos;m not having one in the house, Petunia! Didn&apos;t we swear when we took
him in we&apos;d stamp out that dangerous nonsense?&quot;
That evening when he got back from work, Uncle Vernon did something he&apos;d
never done before; he visited Harry in his cupboard.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f850b0291b3705752615ccea706eb257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1739">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-06212dec18514c37af63c8c8c7fa2940</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Where&apos;s my letter?&quot; said Harry, the moment Uncle Vernon had squeezed
through the door.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-06212dec18514c37af63c8c8c7fa2940</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1740">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5e054f804ba17cc424c7c3355fc77568</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Who&apos;s writing to me?&quot;
&quot;No one.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5e054f804ba17cc424c7c3355fc77568</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1741">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9f67252bd9838fd47870aba5ab2ebe36</data>
      <data key="v_content">it was addressed to you by mistake,&quot; said Uncle Vernon shortly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9f67252bd9838fd47870aba5ab2ebe36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1742">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9c25d3e8702ed341cbaa68eb47aab039</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I have burned it.&quot;
28
&quot;It was not a mistake,&quot; said Harry angrily, &quot;it had my cupboard on it.&quot;
&quot;SILENCE!&quot; yelled Uncle Vernon, and a couple of spiders fell from the
ceiling.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9c25d3e8702ed341cbaa68eb47aab039</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1743">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1ac31bfdf105312ac2734f4b0a5a3a87</data>
      <data key="v_content">He took a few deep breaths and then forced his face into a
smile, which looked quite painful.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1ac31bfdf105312ac2734f4b0a5a3a87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1744">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-408a5db431c10cdea9f23b8ed8869086</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry,&quot;Er -- yes, Harry -- about this cupboard.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-408a5db431c10cdea9f23b8ed8869086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1745">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0d9c8e037e763f90b249aa07ccf8f8bf</data>
      <data key="v_content">Your aunt and I have been
thinking...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0d9c8e037e763f90b249aa07ccf8f8bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1746">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c988f106c3767e6f1749336e64b53386</data>
      <data key="v_content">you&apos;re really getting a bit big for it...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c988f106c3767e6f1749336e64b53386</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1747">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e24b932eef941f4d9d625beb7e4162d1</data>
      <data key="v_content">we think it might
be nice if you moved into Dudley&apos;s second bedroom.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e24b932eef941f4d9d625beb7e4162d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1748">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-936259671a83c5d8b4cdecc996698ab7</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Don&apos;t ask questions!&quot; snapped his uncle.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-936259671a83c5d8b4cdecc996698ab7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1749">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-035e4906f94015cf32250bffc5635ff5</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Take this stuff upstairs,
now.&quot;
The Dursleys&apos; house had four bedrooms: one for Uncle Vernon and Aunt
Petunia, one for visitors (usually Uncle Vernon&apos;s sister, Marge), one
where Dudley slept, and one where Dudley kept all the toys and things
that wouldn&apos;t fit into his first bedroom.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-035e4906f94015cf32250bffc5635ff5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1750">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2443b4df1e8ab1610b61ae7ef3787038</data>
      <data key="v_content">It only took Harry one trip
upstairs to move everything he owned from the cupboard to this room.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2443b4df1e8ab1610b61ae7ef3787038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1751">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b50a1691c04b1ae395e6b710a2d072d9</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
sat down on the bed and stared around him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b50a1691c04b1ae395e6b710a2d072d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1752">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5d9118b980c2e116b0e8018bb2490422</data>
      <data key="v_content">Nearly everything in here was
broken.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5d9118b980c2e116b0e8018bb2490422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1753">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cbbecb0a8fc37b5aa4185889404c766f</data>
      <data key="v_content">The month-old video camera was lying on top of a small, working
tank Dudley had once driven over the next door neighbor&apos;s dog; in the
corner was Dudley&apos;s first-ever television set, which he&apos;d put his foot
through when his favorite program had been canceled; there was a large
birdcage, which had once held a parrot that Dudley had swapped at school
for a real air rifle, which was up on a shelf with the end all bent
because Dudley had sat on it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cbbecb0a8fc37b5aa4185889404c766f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1754">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dd745d5c8c77abafca181c0fc110ba83</data>
      <data key="v_content">Other shelves were full of books.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dd745d5c8c77abafca181c0fc110ba83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1755">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dea73568138b282c5597355cbdb286d2</data>
      <data key="v_content">They
were the only things in the room that looked as though they&apos;d never been
touched.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dea73568138b282c5597355cbdb286d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1756">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-20c96c8d3e3526a59b1e82257a4c50b7</data>
      <data key="v_content">From downstairs came the sound of Dudley bawling at his mother, I don&apos;t
want him in there...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-20c96c8d3e3526a59b1e82257a4c50b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1757">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1cf23b897f0a5b4e28ff5f7270d42b42</data>
      <data key="v_content">make him get out....&quot;
Harry sighed and stretched out on the bed.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1cf23b897f0a5b4e28ff5f7270d42b42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1758">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6ecdd6fac658fa4d7d3aa6ad99d40460</data>
      <data key="v_content">Yesterday he&apos;d have given
anything to be up here.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6ecdd6fac658fa4d7d3aa6ad99d40460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1759">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-37ed4a1949d628d0df39595c34d15764</data>
      <data key="v_content">Today he&apos;d rather be back in his cupboard with
that letter than up here without it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-37ed4a1949d628d0df39595c34d15764</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1760">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a4e945d78d36b16996f33185d3c7503b</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Next morning at breakfast, everyone was rather quiet.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a4e945d78d36b16996f33185d3c7503b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1761">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a39f78c20c003fbfb401cbe86676e153</data>
      <data key="v_content">whackedhis,He&apos;d screamed, whacked his father with his Smelting stick, been
sick on purpose, kicked his mother, and thrown his tortoise through the
greenhouse roof, and he still didn&apos;t have his room back.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a39f78c20c003fbfb401cbe86676e153</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1762">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b6bf7cf9f75845ac9dedd9d50b83cad2</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry was
29
thinking about this time yesterday and bitterly wishing he&apos;d opened the
letter in the hall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b6bf7cf9f75845ac9dedd9d50b83cad2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1763">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-604af747fbe4daf4f558720761b1633b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon and Aunt Petunia kept looking at each
other darkly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-604af747fbe4daf4f558720761b1633b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1764">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fa132ec095b5391593e88e7ab342c92a</data>
      <data key="v_content">,When the mail arrived, Uncle Vernon, who seemed to be trying to be nice
to Harry, made Dudley go and get it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fa132ec095b5391593e88e7ab342c92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1765">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6a9666da32160cc2f47d9135ff670a52</data>
      <data key="v_content">They heard him banging things with
his Smelting stick all the way down the hall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6a9666da32160cc2f47d9135ff670a52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1766">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6d5b9539763aea484fc22d247444343d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;There&apos;s,Then he shouted, &quot;There&apos;s
another one! &apos;Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6d5b9539763aea484fc22d247444343d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1767">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c9f3d40e4c87ca83652b8fe0e1ee9e33</data>
      <data key="v_content">TheSmallestBedroom,,Potter, The Smallest Bedroom, 4 Privet Drive --&apos;&quot;
With a strangled cry, Uncle Vernon leapt from his seat and ran down the
hall, Harry right behind him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c9f3d40e4c87ca83652b8fe0e1ee9e33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1768">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ae84055e3e1c009e4a26f6ae956223e2</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon had to wrestle Dudley to the
ground to get the letter from him, which was made difficult by the fact
that Harry had grabbed Uncle Vernon around the neck from behind.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ae84055e3e1c009e4a26f6ae956223e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1769">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-472819e2801a918517d8d4790950871b</data>
      <data key="v_content">After a
minute of confused fighting, in which everyone got hit a lot by the
Smelting stick, Uncle Vernon straightened up, gasping for breath, with
Harry&apos;s letter clutched in his hand.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-472819e2801a918517d8d4790950871b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1770">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3d96a88940212b023ae58bfa91774020</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Go to your cupboard -- I mean, your bedroom,&quot; he wheezed at Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3d96a88940212b023ae58bfa91774020</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1771">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a2593bd430201e8d8f062b5e4a7c0a1d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Dudley -- go -- just go.&quot;
Harry walked round and round his new room.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a2593bd430201e8d8f062b5e4a7c0a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1772">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b6fedb73cf47daf31121b8eb96c3731a</data>
      <data key="v_content">Someone knew he had moved out
of his cupboard and they seemed to know he hadn&apos;t received his first
letter.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b6fedb73cf47daf31121b8eb96c3731a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1773">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-16918fb596d96f7419a13244d848334b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Surely that meant they&apos;d try again? And this time he&apos;d make sure
they didn&apos;t fail.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-16918fb596d96f7419a13244d848334b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1774">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c77213ffc48687bfad7f7eabe0fcefe8</data>
      <data key="v_content">The repaired alarm clock rang at six o&apos;clock the next morning.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c77213ffc48687bfad7f7eabe0fcefe8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1775">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0becead4587a6353a733c1a950a0fc4d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry
turned it off quickly and dressed silently.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0becead4587a6353a733c1a950a0fc4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1776">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f16e00a1ba8ab8aee4ba968863e1a675</data>
      <data key="v_content">He stole downstairs without turning on any of the lights.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f16e00a1ba8ab8aee4ba968863e1a675</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1777">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0580c92795e3990618b83d420974d11c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was going to wait for the postman on the corner of Privet Drive and
get the letters for number four first.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0580c92795e3990618b83d420974d11c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1778">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cda2d5fd6e20b5169c76c78b1dab90aa</data>
      <data key="v_content">His heart hammered as he crept
across the dark hall toward the front door --
Harry leapt into the air; he&apos;d trodden on something big and squashy on
the doormat -- something alive!
Lights clicked on upstairs and to his horror Harry realized that the
big, squashy something had been his uncle&apos;s face.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cda2d5fd6e20b5169c76c78b1dab90aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1779">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-052524cedbffc3ec31030dd4de4d0fd7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon had been
lying at the foot of the front door in a sleeping bag, clearly making
sure that Harry didn&apos;t do exactly what he&apos;d been trying to do.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-052524cedbffc3ec31030dd4de4d0fd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1780">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-866c9926bd651b294e4f1f6ec08f2a9e</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
shouted at Harry for about half an hour and then told him to go and make
a cup of tea.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-866c9926bd651b294e4f1f6ec08f2a9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1781">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1d939909ed48264d9f76725e972a3821</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry shuffled miserably off into the kitchen and by the
time he got back, the mail had arrived, right into Uncle Vernon&apos;s lap.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1d939909ed48264d9f76725e972a3821</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1782">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c19ee3cf5f2920015336f668f782aef1</data>
      <data key="v_content">30
Harry could see three letters addressed in green ink.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c19ee3cf5f2920015336f668f782aef1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1783">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-852d6d807efe16d00aa19d7c933eb032</data>
      <data key="v_content">I want --&quot; he began, but Uncle Vernon was tearing the letters into
pieces before his eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-852d6d807efe16d00aa19d7c933eb032</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1784">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b54f1013207b5b7b72ab781481d767d8</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon didnt go to work that day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b54f1013207b5b7b72ab781481d767d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1785">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-61e4f96f24321dddf64084a9c0a55861</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
stayed at home and nailed up the mail slot.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-61e4f96f24321dddf64084a9c0a55861</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1786">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fc5793a65fd55c0c791d614062e99b8a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;heexplainedto,&quot;See,&quot; he explained to Aunt Petunia through a mouthful of nails, &quot;if
they can&apos;t deliver them they&apos;ll just give up.&quot;
&quot;I&apos;m not sure that&apos;ll work, Vernon.&quot;
&quot;Oh, these people&apos;s minds work in strange ways, Petunia, they&apos;re not
like you and me,&quot; said Uncle Vernon, trying to knock in a nail with the
piece of fruitcake Aunt Petunia had just brought him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fc5793a65fd55c0c791d614062e99b8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1787">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4b8b9a39d34c1e69bf4955c61e5352f8</data>
      <data key="v_content">noless,On Friday, no less than twelve letters arrived for Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4b8b9a39d34c1e69bf4955c61e5352f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1788">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-729161fe3312d2b0baad0621f728ba85</data>
      <data key="v_content">As they
couldn&apos;t go through the mail slot they had been pushed under the door,
slotted through the sides, and a few even forced through the small
window in the downstairs bathroom.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-729161fe3312d2b0baad0621f728ba85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1789">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-33b1afc14e96304462e9dd3076d7300f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon stayed at home again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-33b1afc14e96304462e9dd3076d7300f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1790">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4a62d864ab18bd9a2f4508b62f1c6d68</data>
      <data key="v_content">After burning all the letters, he got
out a hammer and nails and boarded up the cracks around the front and
back doors so no one could go out.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4a62d864ab18bd9a2f4508b62f1c6d68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1791">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2817fbda380e2b586bfa503989fdbbc4</data>
      <data key="v_content">He hummed &quot;Tiptoe Through the Tulips&quot;
as he worked, and jumped at small noises.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2817fbda380e2b586bfa503989fdbbc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1792">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2677ad8748115ae0b217ac3b50bce18b</data>
      <data key="v_content">thingsbegan,On Saturday, things began to get out of hand.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2677ad8748115ae0b217ac3b50bce18b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1793">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-09a62e0274a74f00d7fcc57aa9700217</data>
      <data key="v_content">Twenty-four letters to
Harry found their way into the house, rolled up and hidden inside each
of the two dozen eggs that their very confused milkman had handed Aunt
Petunia through the living room window.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-09a62e0274a74f00d7fcc57aa9700217</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1794">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0a6d4afc8f2ee695a1279c8c3777b35f</data>
      <data key="v_content">While Uncle Vernon made furious
telephone calls to the post office and the dairy trying to find someone
to complain to, Aunt Petunia shredded the letters in her food processor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0a6d4afc8f2ee695a1279c8c3777b35f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1795">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b8ba36c9bcf46dfd215b5a972e417553</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Who on earth wants to talk to you this badly?&quot; Dudley asked Harry in
amazement.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b8ba36c9bcf46dfd215b5a972e417553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1796">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-67870dd4288a6a161422bfcbb4f48abd</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle,On Sunday morning, Uncle Vernon sat down at the breakfast table looking
tired and rather ill, but happy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-67870dd4288a6a161422bfcbb4f48abd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1797">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-263c0e9fde247cf506e3bb39f9616c00</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;No post on Sundays,&quot; he reminded them cheerfully as he spread marmalade
on his newspapers, &quot;no damn letters today --&quot;
Something came whizzing down the kitchen chimney as he spoke and caught
him sharply on the back of the head.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-263c0e9fde247cf506e3bb39f9616c00</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1798">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-606c62cd4d6173cdfea4bbf8e89f53f4</data>
      <data key="v_content">thirtyor,Next moment, thirty or forty
31
letters came pelting out of the fireplace like bullets.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-606c62cd4d6173cdfea4bbf8e89f53f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1799">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f41024dc56faa3a10dcf46343db8f5e2</data>
      <data key="v_content">but,The Dursleys
ducked, but Harry leapt into the air trying to catch one.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f41024dc56faa3a10dcf46343db8f5e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1800">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6beceedac1511892ae59511f140f1123</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Out! OUT!&quot;
Uncle Vernon seized Harry around the waist and threw him into the hall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6beceedac1511892ae59511f140f1123</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1801">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e15b833514efae1915fc0dbafa719ee8</data>
      <data key="v_content">When Aunt Petunia and Dudley had run out with their arms over their
faces, Uncle Vernon slammed the door shut.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e15b833514efae1915fc0dbafa719ee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1802">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f35704bdea633cbf4bdc09a506c48418</data>
      <data key="v_content">They could hear the letters
still streaming into the room, bouncing off the walls and floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f35704bdea633cbf4bdc09a506c48418</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1803">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-036a0db78cc067df3b05b43dadfd683a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;said,&quot;That does it,&quot; said Uncle Vernon, trying to speak calmly but pulling
great tufts out of his mustache at the same time.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-036a0db78cc067df3b05b43dadfd683a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1804">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6fa2225c55fb024b6204142668fc01e5</data>
      <data key="v_content">I want you all back
here in five minutes ready to leave.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6fa2225c55fb024b6204142668fc01e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1805">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-94d41fbeab0465958ebf7bd3dd24e44f</data>
      <data key="v_content">No arguments!&quot;
He looked so dangerous with half his mustache missing that no one dared
argue.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-94d41fbeab0465958ebf7bd3dd24e44f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1806">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-47030430617e7bbe131e540271ec49bd</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ten minutes later they had wrenched their way through the
boarded-up doors and were in the car, speeding toward the highway.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-47030430617e7bbe131e540271ec49bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1807">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3588fb02dea77d8a79ec417e86ae54eb</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley was sniffling in the back seat; his father had hit him round the
head for holding them up while he tried to pack his television, VCR, and
computer in his sports bag.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3588fb02dea77d8a79ec417e86ae54eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1808">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2d979b54ead128be4b3b92e6a1f4da19</data>
      <data key="v_content">Even Aunt Petunia didn&apos;t dare ask where they
were going.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2d979b54ead128be4b3b92e6a1f4da19</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1809">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eb3987d59636cf3a6cd81616b023840c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Every now and then Uncle Vernon would take a sharp turn and
drive in the opposite direction for a while.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eb3987d59636cf3a6cd81616b023840c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1810">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d24f818488e5805d1f196cde4ab072a3</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;he,shake &apos;em
off,&quot; he would mutter whenever he did this.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d24f818488e5805d1f196cde4ab072a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1811">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f120bdebb57028f5628c3d56f425fc12</data>
      <data key="v_content">They didn&apos;t stop to eat or drink all day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f120bdebb57028f5628c3d56f425fc12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1812">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c75c2e7d694ccd0596b9baefe39a733f</data>
      <data key="v_content">He&apos;d never had such a bad day in his life.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c75c2e7d694ccd0596b9baefe39a733f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1813">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bfe9f7a98cca4f323993fb7a2f557fb1</data>
      <data key="v_content">he&apos;d,He was hungry, he&apos;d
missed five television programs he&apos;d wanted to see, and he&apos;d never gone
so long without blowing up an alien on his computer.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bfe9f7a98cca4f323993fb7a2f557fb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1814">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ea70cc9deea9e12e59706c59d1cf37ba</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon stopped at last outside a gloomy-looking hotel on the
outskirts of a big city.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ea70cc9deea9e12e59706c59d1cf37ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1815">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5d12784e40370cd959f0ee991b25987d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley and Harry shared a room with twin beds
and damp, musty sheets.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5d12784e40370cd959f0ee991b25987d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1816">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9bb600a2730d10c6b1075699ac5c3df3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley snored but Harry stayed awake, sitting on
the windowsill, staring down at the lights of passing cars and
wondering....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9bb600a2730d10c6b1075699ac5c3df3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1817">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d4343b123fda9c0f1a851be11769bc13</data>
      <data key="v_content">They ate stale cornflakes and cold tinned tomatoes on toast for
breakfast the next day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d4343b123fda9c0f1a851be11769bc13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1818">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-086d8959df743d02f437a55b16c7e37a</data>
      <data key="v_content">They had just finished when the owner of the
hotel came over to their table.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-086d8959df743d02f437a55b16c7e37a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1819">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f42c154f10a9217bbdc373ca3be668b4</data>
      <data key="v_content">butis,&quot;&apos;Scuse me, but is one of you Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f42c154f10a9217bbdc373ca3be668b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1820">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f499e698538a98a5f9b268695e7362c7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Potter? Only I got about an &apos;undred
32
of these at the front desk.&quot;
She held up a letter so they could read the green ink address:
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f499e698538a98a5f9b268695e7362c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1821">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e049b58db4b0f2761f1ae75e8734f9f3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Potter
Room 17
Railview Hotel
Cokeworth
Harry made a grab for the letter but Uncle Vernon knocked his hand out
of the way.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e049b58db4b0f2761f1ae75e8734f9f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1822">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9d4953c2a1e0b69ffffead5f81d114ab</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;said,&quot;I&apos;ll take them,&quot; said Uncle Vernon, standing up quickly and following
her from the dining room.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9d4953c2a1e0b69ffffead5f81d114ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1823">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-03a667c6d62fd4fd21c339695cc9eb79</data>
      <data key="v_content">Wouldn&apos;t it be better just to go home, dear?&quot; Aunt Petunia suggested
timidly, hours later, but Uncle Vernon didn&apos;t seem to hear her.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-03a667c6d62fd4fd21c339695cc9eb79</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1824">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b1a422a287c9a2c5737cc218ba3b52d5</data>
      <data key="v_content">Exactly
what he was looking for, none of them knew.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b1a422a287c9a2c5737cc218ba3b52d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1825">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-df7fe218e87cda7a1e42af3514512dfe</data>
      <data key="v_content">He drove them into the
middle of a forest, got out, looked around, shook his head, got back in
the car, and off they went again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-df7fe218e87cda7a1e42af3514512dfe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1826">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1c496b5d9be050e7f97377e1087c980b</data>
      <data key="v_content">The same thing happened in the middle
of a plowed field, halfway across a suspension bridge, and at the top of
a multilevel parking garage.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1c496b5d9be050e7f97377e1087c980b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1827">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ed30255b78ad324d16d40460bf35d694</data>
      <data key="v_content">hasn&apos;t,&quot;Daddy&apos;s gone mad, hasn&apos;t he?&quot; Dudley asked Aunt Petunia dully late that
afternoon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ed30255b78ad324d16d40460bf35d694</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1828">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-327d0d475a42b79855fa294b11358312</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon had parked at the coast, locked them all inside
the car, and disappeared.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-327d0d475a42b79855fa294b11358312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1829">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-edf43cba538e2cc48784feea53d28a45</data>
      <data key="v_content">Great drops beat on the roof of the car.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-edf43cba538e2cc48784feea53d28a45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1830">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d8eb36f9db7af203f53951f2ae4089bb</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;hetold,&quot;It&apos;s Monday,&quot; he told his mother.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d8eb36f9db7af203f53951f2ae4089bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1831">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2199b1f1c3d9c52823952051c5293306</data>
      <data key="v_content">I
want to stay somewhere with a television.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2199b1f1c3d9c52823952051c5293306</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1832">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-38da7bd7b8d09205f4dcf910ca2b21d1</data>
      <data key="v_content">If it was Monday -- and you
could usually count on Dudley to know the days the week, because of
television -- then tomorrow, Tuesday, was Harry&apos;s eleventh birthday.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-38da7bd7b8d09205f4dcf910ca2b21d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1833">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bf329af09f00ac7e1e476923e9fe59df</data>
      <data key="v_content">hisbirthdays,Of
course, his birthdays were never exactly fun -- last year, the Dursleys
had given him a coat hanger and a pair of Uncle Vernon&apos;s old socks.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bf329af09f00ac7e1e476923e9fe59df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1834">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-96f043c923149b5912e67e5b1c17030f</data>
      <data key="v_content">youweren&apos;televen,Still, you weren&apos;t eleven every day.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-96f043c923149b5912e67e5b1c17030f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1835">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-896ef1546f63a6df3ec952690c30939d</data>
      <data key="v_content">33
Uncle Vernon was back and he was smiling.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-896ef1546f63a6df3ec952690c30939d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1836">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1ad40727d4dfb9e110dde9e8b7d3a40f</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was also carrying a long,
thin package and didn&apos;t answer Aunt Petunia when she asked what he&apos;d
bought.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1ad40727d4dfb9e110dde9e8b7d3a40f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1837">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f01864bdde436f733f5e4c23d0217d1f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Found the perfect place!&quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f01864bdde436f733f5e4c23d0217d1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1838">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6e46fac0d0b183c81ffa5e992ec13e2f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Come on! Everyone out!&quot;
It was very cold outside the car.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6e46fac0d0b183c81ffa5e992ec13e2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1839">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6863f6f1202307e2b3683d56bb2444d6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon was pointing at what
looked like a large rock way out at sea.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6863f6f1202307e2b3683d56bb2444d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1840">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5cae5f9c2de05f852d1b0562d723a7ea</data>
      <data key="v_content">Perched on top of the rock was
the most miserable little shack you could imagine.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5cae5f9c2de05f852d1b0562d723a7ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1841">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-911731c07cfad01dd74fe110631d63b1</data>
      <data key="v_content">,One thing was
certain, there was no television in there.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-911731c07cfad01dd74fe110631d63b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1842">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-408a5958a1d4a88ff08d110c3a3eaf4c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Storm forecast for tonight!&quot; said Uncle Vernon gleefully, clapping his
hands together.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-408a5958a1d4a88ff08d110c3a3eaf4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1843">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0568f15117e85e4b2bb4e26366b1c84f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;And this gentleman&apos;s kindly agreed to lend us his
boat!&quot;
A toothless old man came ambling up to them, pointing, with a rather
wicked grin, at an old rowboat bobbing in the iron-gray water below
them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0568f15117e85e4b2bb4e26366b1c84f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1844">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-810ccd94aadab55137f5050c3e212263</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I&apos;ve already got us some rations,&quot; said Uncle Vernon, &quot;so all aboard!&quot;
It was freezing in the boat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-810ccd94aadab55137f5050c3e212263</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1845">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f77a6f0c84cb8dd0d517cafd6e523c9d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Icy sea spray and rain crept down their
necks and a chilly wind whipped their faces.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f77a6f0c84cb8dd0d517cafd6e523c9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1846">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-255d5e55cfbf25f22b86227203b33015</data>
      <data key="v_content">After what seemed like
hours they reached the rock, where Uncle Vernon, slipping and sliding,
led the way to the broken-down house.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-255d5e55cfbf25f22b86227203b33015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1847">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-22bd161f8bdbde8b879735fbcb1edd24</data>
      <data key="v_content">The inside was horrible; it smelled strongly of seaweed, the wind
whistled through the gaps in the wooden walls, and the fireplace was
damp and empty.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-22bd161f8bdbde8b879735fbcb1edd24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1848">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d1b43c161ce85c5722934977a126e9fb</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon&apos;s rations turned out to be a bag of chips each and four
bananas.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d1b43c161ce85c5722934977a126e9fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1849">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9f064322af79eb08d9062df289aa48cd</data>
      <data key="v_content">He tried to start a fire but the empty chip bags just smoked
and shriveled up.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9f064322af79eb08d9062df289aa48cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1850">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7fb69b9fe22390783bfaa23c6d1cbd80</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Could do with some of those letters now, eh?&quot; he said cheerfully.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7fb69b9fe22390783bfaa23c6d1cbd80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1851">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d9e25f87e1e7a7cb7e4069accb990d3e</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was in a very good mood.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d9e25f87e1e7a7cb7e4069accb990d3e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1852">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c9ca1e160f60ca723c23b9c89a8c117f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Obviously he thought nobody stood a chance
of reaching them here in a storm to deliver mail.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c9ca1e160f60ca723c23b9c89a8c117f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1853">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3a1d6aae295d4509e3bcc412dc975fbc</data>
      <data key="v_content">though,Harry privately
agreed, though the thought didn&apos;t cheer him up at all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3a1d6aae295d4509e3bcc412dc975fbc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1854">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b04b4e081dd8b76cd2424555572bab0c</data>
      <data key="v_content">the,As night fell, the promised storm blew up around them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b04b4e081dd8b76cd2424555572bab0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1855">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7cee83c5064e5482d4f1e08c0929a532</data>
      <data key="v_content">Spray from the
high waves splattered the walls of the hut and a fierce wind rattled the
filthy windows.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7cee83c5064e5482d4f1e08c0929a532</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1856">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a8070b2cf331fa2f81991cea72c7999a</data>
      <data key="v_content">Aunt Petunia found a few moldy blankets in the second
34
room and made up a bed for Dudley on the moth-eaten sofa.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a8070b2cf331fa2f81991cea72c7999a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1857">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ca3eb1f80de9e428bf1ab5cbc4ae6488</data>
      <data key="v_content">She and Uncle
Vernon went off to the lumpy bed next door, and Harry was left to find
the softest bit of floor he could and to curl up under the thinnest,
most ragged blanket.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ca3eb1f80de9e428bf1ab5cbc4ae6488</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1858">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-05ed88901c9d9df756d6a3d329ce076b</data>
      <data key="v_content">The storm raged more and more ferociously as the night went on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-05ed88901c9d9df756d6a3d329ce076b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1859">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5086a131be962e61536496e06729bcaf</data>
      <data key="v_content">He shivered and turned over, trying to get comfortable,
his stomach rumbling with hunger.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5086a131be962e61536496e06729bcaf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1860">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c7955c4b5fc374192ed3a1788db95257</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley&apos;s snores were drowned by the
low rolls of thunder that started near midnight.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c7955c4b5fc374192ed3a1788db95257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1861">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eafaa5eca846f4c1575a41e5ae488773</data>
      <data key="v_content">The lighted dial of
Dudley&apos;s watch, which was dangling over the edge of the sofa on his fat
wrist, told Harry he&apos;d be eleven in ten minutes&apos; time.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eafaa5eca846f4c1575a41e5ae488773</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1862">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f6e4689561aaccbefde2c796a22a058b</data>
      <data key="v_content">He lay and
watched his birthday tick nearer, wondering if the Dursleys would
remember at all, wondering where the letter writer was now.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f6e4689561aaccbefde2c796a22a058b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1863">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2ddf97710eca333f41d4729a33108f79</data>
      <data key="v_content">He hoped the
roof wasn&apos;t going to fall in, although he might be warmer if it did.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2ddf97710eca333f41d4729a33108f79</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1864">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f096aa45020b33dce48496f7d0f3e864</data>
      <data key="v_content">Maybe the house in Privet Drive would be so full of
letters when they got back that he&apos;d be able to steal one somehow.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f096aa45020b33dce48496f7d0f3e864</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1865">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a9b90e549f74cbfe4ebadb288c537eaa</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Was that the sea, slapping hard on the rock like
that? And (two minutes to go) what was that funny crunching noise? Was
the rock crumbling into the sea?
One minute to go and he&apos;d be eleven.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a9b90e549f74cbfe4ebadb288c537eaa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1866">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6bc5ec73bf4c821eb5ff5ad567d6c2c4</data>
      <data key="v_content">nine -- maybe he&apos;d wake Dudley up, just to annoy him -- three...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6bc5ec73bf4c821eb5ff5ad567d6c2c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1867">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-34835ae780931ffd60944c0cf319c35b</data>
      <data key="v_content">The whole shack shivered and Harry sat bolt upright, staring at the
door.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-34835ae780931ffd60944c0cf319c35b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1868">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-554efefed8359e00f000b77d874112c3</data>
      <data key="v_content">knocking,Someone was outside, knocking to come in.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-554efefed8359e00f000b77d874112c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1869">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ebb6410ad4eef0a4e5866c84bb7b5903</data>
      <data key="v_content">CHAPTER FOUR
THE KEEPER OF THE KEYS
BOOM.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ebb6410ad4eef0a4e5866c84bb7b5903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1870">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2cc579320505157ce114f845eace0182</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Where&apos;s the cannon?&quot; he
said stupidly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2cc579320505157ce114f845eace0182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1871">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-09a549c48fadc913f8e5c00e9637b2b3</data>
      <data key="v_content">There was a crash behind them and Uncle Vernon came skidding into the
room.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-09a549c48fadc913f8e5c00e9637b2b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1872">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7f663cb99b112aac559765cecf145014</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was holding a rifle in his hands -- now they knew what had been
in the long, thin package he had brought with them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7f663cb99b112aac559765cecf145014</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1873">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9bea76383724f41c2df7b9ed447bec6b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I warn you -- I&apos;m armed!&quot;
There was a pause.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9bea76383724f41c2df7b9ed447bec6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1874">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-58b6dfac2f476b37830edafe4a3beb45</data>
      <data key="v_content">Then --
SMASH!
The door was hit with such force that it swung clean off its hinges and
with a deafening crash landed flat on the floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-58b6dfac2f476b37830edafe4a3beb45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1875">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0fcb73682348bd228be50dfca52ea2cc</data>
      <data key="v_content">A giant of a man was standing in the doorway.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0fcb73682348bd228be50dfca52ea2cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1876">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-636c14eced0a00dea6fd74bddee7e6a6</data>
      <data key="v_content">His face was almost
completely hidden by a long, shaggy mane of hair and a wild, tangled
beard, but you could make out his eyes, glinting like black beetles
under all the hair.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-636c14eced0a00dea6fd74bddee7e6a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1877">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ab34c3f907752ac500be1473d468d1db</data>
      <data key="v_content">The giant squeezed his way into the hut, stooping so that his head just
brushed the ceiling.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ab34c3f907752ac500be1473d468d1db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1878">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b77e76611682388bb2cb830920c8ec7f</data>
      <data key="v_content">picked,He bent down, picked up the door, and fitted it
easily back into its frame.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b77e76611682388bb2cb830920c8ec7f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1879">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b486893e7a8e63e58c4916104d61baec</data>
      <data key="v_content">The noise of the storm outside dropped a
little.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b486893e7a8e63e58c4916104d61baec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1880">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1b80178c8d06b6c8486083daeaaf1b78</data>
      <data key="v_content">He turned to look at them all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1b80178c8d06b6c8486083daeaaf1b78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1881">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ee71f153efb846a96514fd527cc1a62c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Couldn&apos;t make us a cup o&apos; tea, could yeh? It&apos;s not been an easy
journey...&quot;
He strode over to the sofa where Dudley sat frozen with fear.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ee71f153efb846a96514fd527cc1a62c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1882">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c01571dab68c3b71c2d3b63e5b79c048</data>
      <data key="v_content">yehgreat,&quot;Budge up, yeh great lump,&quot; said the stranger.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c01571dab68c3b71c2d3b63e5b79c048</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1883">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-55700408f5cfee23eb9656439661e680</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudley squeaked and ran to hide behind his mother, who was crouching,
terrified, behind Uncle Vernon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-55700408f5cfee23eb9656439661e680</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1884">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dd454350c33ab72f944f66904a3acab0</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;An&apos; here&apos;s Harry!&quot; said the giant.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dd454350c33ab72f944f66904a3acab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1885">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-19fc7ff001128d80afd2c32bd1df8be7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry looked up into the fierce, wild, shadowy face and saw that the
beetle eyes were crinkled in a smile.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-19fc7ff001128d80afd2c32bd1df8be7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1886">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-595066e8fc1ec38aeda55c8d73adb390</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Las&apos; time I saw you, you was only a baby,&quot; said the giant.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-595066e8fc1ec38aeda55c8d73adb390</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1887">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cb90a46d59936cf72a7c13b6fef62fdd</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Yeh look a
lot like yet dad, but yeh&apos;ve got yet mom&apos;s eyes.&quot;
Uncle Vernon made a funny rasping noise.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cb90a46d59936cf72a7c13b6fef62fdd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1888">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-80afabdb9f986f732e9a9979884e3430</data>
      <data key="v_content">I demand that you leave at once, sit!&quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-80afabdb9f986f732e9a9979884e3430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1889">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-db13fb4ef126ec3f24997bbd8f38f7e5</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You are breaking and
entering!&quot;
36
&quot;Ah, shut up, Dursley, yeh great prune,&quot; said the giant; he reached over
the back of the sofa, jerked the gun out of Uncle Vernon&apos;s hands, bent
it into a knot as easily as if it had been made of rubber, and threw it
into a corner of the room.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-db13fb4ef126ec3f24997bbd8f38f7e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1890">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b10c216239d6cf85bb86e56d55e87006</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon made another funny noise, like a mouse being trodden on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b10c216239d6cf85bb86e56d55e87006</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1891">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-55a8e22fb20d16fd23d77c1afa5fcff9</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;said,&quot;Anyway -- Harry,&quot; said the giant, turning his back on the Dursleys, &quot;a
very happy birthday to yeh.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-55a8e22fb20d16fd23d77c1afa5fcff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1892">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3fbf75c8aeace2dbfc4489df8fa09c92</data>
      <data key="v_content">Got summat fer yeh here -- I mighta sat on
it at some point, but it&apos;ll taste all right.&quot;
From an inside pocket of his black overcoat he pulled a slightly
squashed box.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3fbf75c8aeace2dbfc4489df8fa09c92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1893">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cd43a52cb31375b335a5cfb9dfb25fb0</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry opened it with trembling fingers.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cd43a52cb31375b335a5cfb9dfb25fb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1894">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b8d206f36229fe74449ab0cff871e7a9</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Inside was a
large, sticky chocolate cake with Happy Birthday Harry written on it in
green icing.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b8d206f36229fe74449ab0cff871e7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1895">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a3b98584d0565f030eaa57ca74fa28dd</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry looked up at the giant.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a3b98584d0565f030eaa57ca74fa28dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1896">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-aa3990d3a3e9000ea13a087e6fd85058</data>
      <data key="v_content">He meant to say thank you, but the words
got lost on the way to his mouth, and what he said instead was, &quot;Who are
you?&quot;
The giant chuckled.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-aa3990d3a3e9000ea13a087e6fd85058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1897">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3365bb90cb6f66a7eca606020763ef01</data>
      <data key="v_content">Keeperof,Rubeus Hagrid, Keeper of Keys and
Grounds at Hogwarts.&quot;
He held out an enormous hand and shook Harry&apos;s whole arm.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3365bb90cb6f66a7eca606020763ef01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1898">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c49443d55aa79e1bf7ff7c14370f9750</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;What about that tea then, eh?&quot; he said, rubbing his hands together.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c49443d55aa79e1bf7ff7c14370f9750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1899">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-139f0dc1b5b6886fb4bcc6ad6cece706</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I&apos;d not say no ter summat stronger if yeh&apos;ve got it, mind.&quot;
His eyes fell on the empty grate with the shriveled chip bags in it and
he snorted.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-139f0dc1b5b6886fb4bcc6ad6cece706</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1900">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1004a77dd2c2020cb9e377286f6d00d8</data>
      <data key="v_content">He bent down over the fireplace; they couldn&apos;t see what he
was doing but when he drew back a second later, there was a roaring fire
there.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1004a77dd2c2020cb9e377286f6d00d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1901">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-687d4e5c1f2057da5cd90b4d7e36feda</data>
      <data key="v_content">It filled the whole damp hut with flickering light and Harry felt
the warmth wash over him as though he&apos;d sunk into a hot bath.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-687d4e5c1f2057da5cd90b4d7e36feda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1902">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6c3d3b26af57673b2e465f40dc19ce48</data>
      <data key="v_content">The giant sat back down on the sofa, which sagged under his weight, and
began taking all sorts of things out of the pockets of his coat: a
copper kettle, a squashy package of sausages, a poker, a teapot, several
chipped mugs, and a bottle of some amber liquid that he took a swig from
before starting to make tea.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6c3d3b26af57673b2e465f40dc19ce48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1903">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b1ef177946f6c150a7a0a09becb7820b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Soon the hut was full of the sound and
smell of sizzling sausage.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b1ef177946f6c150a7a0a09becb7820b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1904">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0a3d7d0c660433a990da04bee0c83a34</data>
      <data key="v_content">Nobody said a thing while the giant was
working, but as he slid the first six fat, juicy, slightly burnt
37
sausages from the poker, Dudley fidgeted a little.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0a3d7d0c660433a990da04bee0c83a34</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1905">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1e17087accab0c65c5279283aaf753ac</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Uncle Vernon said
sharply, &quot;Don&apos;t touch anything he gives you, Dudley.&quot;
The giant chuckled darkly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1e17087accab0c65c5279283aaf753ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1906">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8f1373cfb27c395ca95776279fd70990</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Yet great puddin&apos; of a son don&apos; need fattenin&apos; anymore, Dursley, don&apos;
worry.&quot;
He passed the sausages to Harry, who was so hungry he had never tasted
anything so wonderful, but he still couldn&apos;t take his eyes off the
giant.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8f1373cfb27c395ca95776279fd70990</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1907">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-258be2b840c7801f510168f328792408</data>
      <data key="v_content">asnobodyseemed,Finally, as nobody seemed about to explain anything, he said,
&quot;I&apos;m sorry, but I still don&apos;t really know who you are.&quot;
The giant took a gulp of tea and wiped his mouth with the back of his
hand.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-258be2b840c7801f510168f328792408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1908">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9ad9ab58fae7725cca69aa64f1e17a0a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;he,&quot;Call me Hagrid,&quot; he said, &quot;everyone does.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9ad9ab58fae7725cca69aa64f1e17a0a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1909">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eaa9693d6bf0c47ad05f182d671ae3e0</data>
      <data key="v_content">An&apos; like I told yeh, I&apos;m
Keeper of Keys at Hogwarts -- yeh&apos;ll know all about Hogwarts, o&apos; course.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eaa9693d6bf0c47ad05f182d671ae3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1910">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1f36f1af927064b0afafdf33bc86c031</data>
      <data key="v_content">turning,&quot;Sony?&quot; barked Hagrid, turning to stare at the Dursleys, who shrank back
into the shadows.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1f36f1af927064b0afafdf33bc86c031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1911">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-81525ba541fb40370c160da5056d7923</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;It&apos; s them as should be sorry! I knew yeh weren&apos;t
gettin&apos; yer letters but I never thought yeh wouldn&apos;t even know abou&apos;
Hogwarts, fer cryin&apos; out loud! Did yeh never wonder where yet parents
learned it all?&quot;
&quot;All what?&quot; asked Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-81525ba541fb40370c160da5056d7923</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1912">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-26afee4491f5eb595695008a63a3532f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Now wait jus&apos; one second!&quot;
He had leapt to his feet.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-26afee4491f5eb595695008a63a3532f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1913">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-af0c534501364e66372bf2d1aa7d6c0d</data>
      <data key="v_content">In his anger he seemed to fill the whole hut.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-af0c534501364e66372bf2d1aa7d6c0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1914">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-32ff57d8565840a48fa9e2b3de148477</data>
      <data key="v_content">The Dursleys were cowering against the wall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-32ff57d8565840a48fa9e2b3de148477</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1915">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-749ca34794bd9af60e8d73a7589b7b62</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Do you mean ter tell me,&quot; he growled at the Dursleys, &quot;that this boy --
this boy! -- knows nothin&apos; abou&apos; -- about ANYTHING?&quot;
Harry thought this was going a bit far.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-749ca34794bd9af60e8d73a7589b7b62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1916">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-14642a8e402198f699383e3c6320c067</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had been to school, after
all, and his marks weren&apos;t bad.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-14642a8e402198f699383e3c6320c067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1917">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-74d8eb3602a16a886c56b7e780d21ca1</data>
      <data key="v_content">38
&quot;I know some things,&quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-74d8eb3602a16a886c56b7e780d21ca1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1918">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b190679b6ae6f5c6f0db49b78e094ca8</data>
      <data key="v_content">youknow,,&quot;I can, you know, do math and stuff.&quot; But
Hagrid simply waved his hand and said, &quot;About our world, I mean.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b190679b6ae6f5c6f0db49b78e094ca8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1919">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0c883a41e9ab4f570fda61ed8135d252</data>
      <data key="v_content">Yer parents&apos; world.&quot;
&quot;What world?&quot;
Hagrid looked as if he was about to explode.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0c883a41e9ab4f570fda61ed8135d252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1920">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-86ab84245e6b8833b11553c24dba25d5</data>
      <data key="v_content">whohad,Uncle Vernon, who had gone very pale, whispered something that sounded
like &quot;Mimblewimble.&quot; Hagrid stared wildly at Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-86ab84245e6b8833b11553c24dba25d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1921">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-498ef76b3fa0bac00621cee5b724e5a2</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But yeh must know about yet mom and dad,&quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-498ef76b3fa0bac00621cee5b724e5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1922">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-995f54208844d58c1822a7987fbb2111</data>
      <data key="v_content">You&apos;re famous.&quot;
&quot;What? My -- my mom and dad weren&apos;t famous, were they?&quot;
&quot;Yeh don&apos; know...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-995f54208844d58c1822a7987fbb2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1923">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bfe6ea809ac9b5e6b6434be0279313fa</data>
      <data key="v_content">yeh don&apos; know...&quot; Hagrid ran his fingers through his
hair, fixing Harry with a bewildered stare.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bfe6ea809ac9b5e6b6434be0279313fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1924">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9c4be324f48af95c852352fae2226546</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Yeh don&apos; know what yeh are?&quot; he said finally.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9c4be324f48af95c852352fae2226546</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1925">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0f0dffcf3cb1a903bc5f1accf9f75300</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon suddenly found his voice.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0f0dffcf3cb1a903bc5f1accf9f75300</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1926">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5da65f451b9b17e2991996af33caf2ec</data>
      <data key="v_content">sit!,&quot;Stop right there, sit! I forbid you to tell the
boy anything!&quot;
A braver man than Vernon Dursley would have quailed under the furious
look Hagrid now gave him; when Hagrid spoke, his every syllable trembled
with rage.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5da65f451b9b17e2991996af33caf2ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1927">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d6e1ee2ac526b504c40534269c87022a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You never told him? Never told him what was in the letter Dumbledore
left fer him? I was there! I saw Dumbledore leave it, Dursley! An&apos;
you&apos;ve kept it from him all these years?&quot;
&quot;Kept what from me?&quot; said Harry eagerly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d6e1ee2ac526b504c40534269c87022a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1928">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-701a606c075e0be9e7704209ba1f23cc</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;STOP! I FORBID YOU!&quot; yelled Uncle Vernon in panic.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-701a606c075e0be9e7704209ba1f23cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1929">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d70045a0c326c75984d8a81b80825e01</data>
      <data key="v_content">Aunt Petunia gave a gasp of horror.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d70045a0c326c75984d8a81b80825e01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1930">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3ed5b1150deb8e12db3a1f4c1693ea36</data>
      <data key="v_content">goboil,39
&quot;Ah, go boil yet heads, both of yeh,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3ed5b1150deb8e12db3a1f4c1693ea36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1931">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4f13af88dc092acbfef18d9aec5a61a2</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Harry -- yet a
wizard.&quot;
There was silence inside the hut.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4f13af88dc092acbfef18d9aec5a61a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1932">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d74c676bfba23a0647039e85929b45c4</data>
      <data key="v_content">Only the sea and the whistling wind
could be heard.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d74c676bfba23a0647039e85929b45c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1933">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c61f3d7c9d26a09e7cb5d0161d6d80f6</data>
      <data key="v_content">o&apos;course,&quot;,&quot;A wizard, o&apos; course,&quot; said Hagrid, sitting back down on the sofa, which
groaned and sank even lower, &quot;an&apos; a thumpin&apos; good&apos;un, I&apos;d say, once
yeh&apos;ve been trained up a bit.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c61f3d7c9d26a09e7cb5d0161d6d80f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1934">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0c899bc058b031a42dac0c734d3799a0</data>
      <data key="v_content">With a mum an&apos; dad like yours, what else
would yeh be? An&apos; I reckon it&apos;s abou&apos; time yeh read yer letter.&quot;
Harry stretched out his hand at last to take the yellowish envelope,
addressed in emerald green to Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0c899bc058b031a42dac0c734d3799a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1935">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-829c9c2cb9acfc894f0174be4fe18b20</data>
      <data key="v_content">TheFloor,Hut-on-the-Rock,,Potter, The Floor, Hut-on-the-Rock,
The Sea.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-829c9c2cb9acfc894f0174be4fe18b20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1936">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8283125777e817f583fc2d6f5e524182</data>
      <data key="v_content">He pulled out the letter and read:
HOGWARTS SCHOOL of WITCHCRAFT and WIZARDRY
Headmaster: ALBUS DUMBLEDORE
(Order of Merlin, First Class, Grand Sorc., Chf.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8283125777e817f583fc2d6f5e524182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1937">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-45b8decd8225e97ae9d5bef6e95a9d9d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Wearepleased,Potter,
We are pleased to inform you that you have been accepted at Hogwarts
School of Witchcraft and Wizardry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-45b8decd8225e97ae9d5bef6e95a9d9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1938">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e669601901f2570427b2db0adac96166</data>
      <data key="v_content">Please find enclosed a list of all
necessary books and equipment.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e669601901f2570427b2db0adac96166</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1939">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-977b541f0aedfe076ffbfd313b4e1920</data>
      <data key="v_content">We await your owl by no later than July 31.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-977b541f0aedfe076ffbfd313b4e1920</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1940">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a8e5beafc14126a4ac9821f6da0b8134</data>
      <data key="v_content">MinervaMcGonagall,,Yours sincerely,
Minerva McGonagall,
Deputy Headmistress
Questions exploded inside Harry&apos;s head like fireworks and he couldn&apos;t
decide which to ask first.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a8e5beafc14126a4ac9821f6da0b8134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1941">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-39eefb145f866e56bc49dc4d599671f5</data>
      <data key="v_content">After a few minutes he stammered, &quot;What does
it mean, they await my owl?&quot;
&quot;Gallopin&apos; Gorgons, that reminds me,&quot; said Hagrid, clapping a hand to
his forehead with enough force to knock over a cart horse, and from yet
40
another pocket inside his overcoat he pulled an owl -- a real, live,
rather ruffled-looking owl -- a long quill, and a roll of parchment.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-39eefb145f866e56bc49dc4d599671f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1942">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-db0aceaebb3dbd4776585273c77a943e</data>
      <data key="v_content">With his tongue between his teeth he scribbled a note that Harry could
read upside down:
Dear Professor Dumbledore,
Given Harry his letter.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-db0aceaebb3dbd4776585273c77a943e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1943">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3b6c6a225238b9f496988ef5ab00bff5</data>
      <data key="v_content">Taking him to buy his things tomorrow.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3b6c6a225238b9f496988ef5ab00bff5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1944">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-362d74cd65b8406f45a5325971a3d703</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid
Hagrid rolled up the note, gave it to the owl, which clamped it in its
beak, went to the door, and threw the owl out into the storm.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-362d74cd65b8406f45a5325971a3d703</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1945">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-df8f4f33b666ae26859b9b80c07ae079</data>
      <data key="v_content">Then he
came back and sat down as though this was as normal as talking on the
telephone.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-df8f4f33b666ae26859b9b80c07ae079</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1946">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-94918a838207ca569db5bf129f841763</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry realized his mouth was open and closed it quickly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-94918a838207ca569db5bf129f841763</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1947">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5767040f564be3f911b113356f69e8ee</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Where was I?&quot; said Hagrid, but at that moment, Uncle Vernon, still
ashen-faced but looking very angry, moved into the firelight.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5767040f564be3f911b113356f69e8ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1948">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4865da3f2dc9fe1ec0169e9c95256f38</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I&apos;d like ter see a great Muggle like you stop him,&quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4865da3f2dc9fe1ec0169e9c95256f38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1949">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bc6037bbcd679eab4b011cc1ca148747</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidHagrid,,&quot;A Muggle,&quot; said Hagrid, &quot;it&apos;s what we call nonmagic folk like thern.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bc6037bbcd679eab4b011cc1ca148747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1950">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-049ff2be8f75f035c4b440c805f239a4</data>
      <data key="v_content">An&apos; it&apos;s your bad luck you grew up in a family o&apos; the biggest Muggles I
ever laid eyes on.&quot;
&quot;We swore when we took him in we&apos;d put a stop to that rubbish,&quot; said
Uncle Vernon, &quot;swore we&apos;d stamp it out of him! Wizard indeed!&quot;
&quot;You knew?&quot; said Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-049ff2be8f75f035c4b440c805f239a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1951">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c83ece0477dc22f5407e77bd1388b248</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You knew I&apos;m a -- a wizard?&quot;
&quot;Knew!&quot; shrieked Aunt Petunia suddenly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c83ece0477dc22f5407e77bd1388b248</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1952">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d0cf85d8240170166a43460c96e1bc09</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Knew! Of course we knew! How
41
could you not be, my dratted sister being what she was? Oh, she got a
letter just like that and disappeared off to that-that school-and came
home every vacation with her pockets full of frog spawn, turning teacups
into rats.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d0cf85d8240170166a43460c96e1bc09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1953">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4831f02bbd601df459437bef8688e7c8</data>
      <data key="v_content">I was the only one who saw her for what she was -- a freak!
But for my mother and father, oh no, it was Lily this and Lily that,
they were proud of having a witch in the family!&quot;
She stopped to draw a deep breath and then went ranting on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4831f02bbd601df459437bef8688e7c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1954">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ae7127a61f4db40392832386a3076d80</data>
      <data key="v_content">It seemed
she had been wanting to say all this for years.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ae7127a61f4db40392832386a3076d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1955">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4eb32d1d8568fc26db31e54d869936af</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Then she met that Potter at school and they left and got married and
had you, and of course I knew you&apos;d be just the same, just as strange,
just as -- as -- abnormal -- and then, if you please, she went and got
herself blown up and we got landed with you!&quot;
Harry had gone very white.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4eb32d1d8568fc26db31e54d869936af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1956">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7211e9849c509152fe26116f399d8e59</data>
      <data key="v_content">As soon as he found his voice he said, &quot;Blown
up? You told me they died in a car crash!&quot;
&quot;CAR CRASH!&quot; roared Hagrid, jumping up so angrily that the Dursleys
scuttled back to their corner.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7211e9849c509152fe26116f399d8e59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1957">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a5107caaee6094ab22995be210c9afa0</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;How could a car crash kill Lily an&apos;
James Potter? It&apos;s an outrage! A scandal! Harry Potter not knowin&apos; his
own story when every kid in our world knows his name!&quot; &quot;But why? What
happened?&quot; Harry asked urgently.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a5107caaee6094ab22995be210c9afa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1958">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-40ecd2a662a1266bae7234ffd35f3a65</data>
      <data key="v_content">The anger faded from Hagrid&apos;s face.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-40ecd2a662a1266bae7234ffd35f3a65</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1959">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c01de229f24913ebb29b44af4883dfb7</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;I never expected this,&quot; he said, in a low, worried voice.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c01de229f24913ebb29b44af4883dfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1960">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-63741722b479cba0bc9e2c7f6086ac75</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;I had no
idea, when Dumbledore told me there might be trouble gettin&apos; hold of
yeh, how much yeh didn&apos;t know.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-63741722b479cba0bc9e2c7f6086ac75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1961">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6448a14d2d2caa0a152629982bdb63f6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry,Idon&apos;,Ah, Harry, I don&apos; know if I&apos;m the right
person ter tell yeh -- but someone 3 s gotta -- yeh can&apos;t go off ter
Hogwarts not knowin&apos;.&quot;
He threw a dirty look at the Dursleys.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6448a14d2d2caa0a152629982bdb63f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1962">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d5600e71a326e699cc6dd37a8b99fc2b</data>
      <data key="v_content">it&apos;sbestyeh,&quot;Well, it&apos;s best yeh know as much as I can tell yeh -- mind, I can&apos;t
tell yeh everythin&apos;, it&apos;s a great myst&apos;ry, parts of it....&quot;
He sat down, stared into the fire for a few seconds, and then said, &quot;It
begins, I suppose, with -- with a person called -- but it&apos;s incredible
yeh don&apos;t know his name, everyone in our world knows --&quot;
&quot;Who? &quot;
42
&quot;Well -- I don&apos; like sayin&apos; the name if I can help it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d5600e71a326e699cc6dd37a8b99fc2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1963">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d343b390e2f0319e569c4abede331862</data>
      <data key="v_content">No one does.&quot;
&quot;Why not?&quot;
&quot;Gulpin&apos; gargoyles, Harry, people are still scared.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d343b390e2f0319e569c4abede331862</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1964">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-aeaa051d71428b347cdf95e468a5d018</data>
      <data key="v_content">therewasthis,See, there was this wizard who went...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-aeaa051d71428b347cdf95e468a5d018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1965">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eac922d7b8554e1c6cf8f47e1dce8d0e</data>
      <data key="v_content">As bad as you
could go.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eac922d7b8554e1c6cf8f47e1dce8d0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1966">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-08af7a4947e7bbc61212faa33e9b1e36</data>
      <data key="v_content">His name was...&quot;
Hagrid gulped, but no words came out.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-08af7a4947e7bbc61212faa33e9b1e36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1967">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-427dbfcc6f45b49b0d89bf0105fca806</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Could you write it down?&quot; Harry suggested.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-427dbfcc6f45b49b0d89bf0105fca806</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1968">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1e956da623ca742ac7a2fc6323ee3e67</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Don&apos;
make me say it again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1e956da623ca742ac7a2fc6323ee3e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1969">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4a82ee1caab1c5c16951c5b6fc77887b</data>
      <data key="v_content">this--this,Anyway, this -- this wizard, about twenty years
ago now, started lookin&apos; fer followers.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4a82ee1caab1c5c16951c5b6fc77887b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1970">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c4fa83f4ca1aa4f775bb4d3f5653dded</data>
      <data key="v_content">too--,Got &apos;em, too -- some were
afraid, some just wanted a bit o&apos; his power, &apos;cause he was gettin&apos;
himself power, all right.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c4fa83f4ca1aa4f775bb4d3f5653dded</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1971">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f410c64ea142dfa6d1a5112aacc3319d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Didn&apos;t know who ter trust,
didn&apos;t dare get friendly with strange wizards or witches...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f410c64ea142dfa6d1a5112aacc3319d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1972">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e2773b8462f2313104f942a9f85cd24c</data>
      <data key="v_content">somestoodup,&apos;Course, some stood up to him --
an&apos; he killed &apos;em.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e2773b8462f2313104f942a9f85cd24c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1973">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ba709ab2a595f1f5f7fa203a37ea4152</data>
      <data key="v_content">One o&apos; the only safe places left was
Hogwarts.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ba709ab2a595f1f5f7fa203a37ea4152</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1974">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-682fe426aea42ab8ae350e21e6c6a02c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Reckon Dumbledore&apos;s the only one You-Know-Who was afraid of.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-682fe426aea42ab8ae350e21e6c6a02c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1975">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e4da4fd5de1c912d1c0435267057ddf6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Didn&apos;t dare try takin&apos; the school, not jus&apos; then, anyway.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e4da4fd5de1c912d1c0435267057ddf6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1976">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8f90a2a8b8ffb597518956864bba60ff</data>
      <data key="v_content">yermuman&apos;,&quot;Now, yer mum an&apos; dad were as good a witch an&apos; wizard as I ever knew.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8f90a2a8b8ffb597518956864bba60ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1977">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ca3c2b8fdd42d672a07df4b19d5167a2</data>
      <data key="v_content">Head boy an&apos; girl at Hogwarts in their day! Suppose the myst&apos;ry is why
You-Know-Who never tried to get &apos;em on his side before...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ca3c2b8fdd42d672a07df4b19d5167a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1978">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-90ea176a94ed4c10dacc5d1d136dc838</data>
      <data key="v_content">probably knew
they were too close ter Dumbledore ter want anythin&apos; ter do with the
Dark Side.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-90ea176a94ed4c10dacc5d1d136dc838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1979">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0dfc12f357d457c730c693d36d6d926c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Maybe he thought he could persuade &apos;em...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0dfc12f357d457c730c693d36d6d926c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1980">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dd5cd6395135f2b4fe6b92c3f334358b</data>
      <data key="v_content">maybe he just wanted &apos;em
outta the way.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dd5cd6395135f2b4fe6b92c3f334358b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1981">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f9f2bd8d0f98f44b76fdc01a49b654ae</data>
      <data key="v_content">,All anyone knows is, he turned up in the village where
you was all living, on Halloween ten years ago.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f9f2bd8d0f98f44b76fdc01a49b654ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1982">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-be906eeefca85c784734e8fca6ec0495</data>
      <data key="v_content">You was just a year old.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-be906eeefca85c784734e8fca6ec0495</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1983">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-aad92b617c32156902fe84bba453ac55</data>
      <data key="v_content">He came ter yer house an&apos; -- an&apos; --&quot;
Hagrid suddenly pulled out a very dirty, spotted handkerchief and blew
his nose with a sound like a foghorn.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-aad92b617c32156902fe84bba453ac55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1984">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f8a1dcc3d908e47622bbe7d1442ad80d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But it&apos;s that sad -- knew yer mum an&apos; dad, an&apos; nicer
people yeh couldn&apos;t find -- anyway...&quot;
&quot;You-Know-Who killed &apos;em.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f8a1dcc3d908e47622bbe7d1442ad80d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1985">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-be256a108b196ff5318435284819776d</data>
      <data key="v_content">An&apos; then -- an&apos; this is the real myst&apos;ry of
the thing -- he tried to kill you, too.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-be256a108b196ff5318435284819776d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1986">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f1d6dbb9dc35497edb194a3b99869e42</data>
      <data key="v_content">Wanted ter make a clean job of
it, I suppose, or maybe he just liked killin&apos; by then.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f1d6dbb9dc35497edb194a3b99869e42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1987">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d1c0526c5b1c7c7ed9da48ca5afe8a0f</data>
      <data key="v_content">But he couldn&apos;t
43
do it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d1c0526c5b1c7c7ed9da48ca5afe8a0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1988">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-84698f4231e62621e7c9953cd1955ac4</data>
      <data key="v_content">Never wondered how you got that mark on yer forehead? That was no
ordinary cut.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-84698f4231e62621e7c9953cd1955ac4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1989">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-470ad0fcbfa60b43901fc7072f83e02d</data>
      <data key="v_content">That&apos;s what yeh get when a Powerful, evil curse touches
yeh -- took care of yer mum an&apos; dad an&apos; yer house, even -- but it didn&apos;t
work on you, an&apos; that&apos;s why yer famous, Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-470ad0fcbfa60b43901fc7072f83e02d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1990">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c8859691d9e181267201465e3b0b13b0</data>
      <data key="v_content">No one ever lived after
he decided ter kill &apos;em, no one except you, an&apos; he&apos;d killed some o&apos; the
best witches an&apos; wizards of the age -- the McKinnons, the Bones, the
Prewetts -- an&apos; you was only a baby, an&apos; you lived.&quot;
Something very painful was going on in Harry&apos;s mind.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c8859691d9e181267201465e3b0b13b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1991">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eb7b6b8b216793d1ffe6b4e587266cb3</data>
      <data key="v_content">As Hagrid&apos;s story
came to a close, he saw again the blinding flash of green light, more
clearly than he had ever remembered it before -- and he remembered
something else, for the first time in his life: a high, cold, cruel
laugh.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eb7b6b8b216793d1ffe6b4e587266cb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1992">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-80ccfb02a30e552af32c96b4f3a81136</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Took yeh from the ruined house myself, on Dumbledore&apos;s orders.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-80ccfb02a30e552af32c96b4f3a81136</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1993">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3a0238e98ec0ce5b27a0772dc2b116bf</data>
      <data key="v_content">Brought
yeh ter this lot...&quot;
&quot;Load of old tosh,&quot; said Uncle Vernon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3a0238e98ec0ce5b27a0772dc2b116bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1994">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0a119a54e487752a7e7c74cdc4377c28</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry jumped; he had almost
forgotten that the Dursleys were there.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0a119a54e487752a7e7c74cdc4377c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1995">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cb1732855b6ca26dd25ddbea1c39b34e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon certainly seemed to
have got back his courage.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cb1732855b6ca26dd25ddbea1c39b34e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1996">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fdfd781f856ee8e31247ff1d4ce886b5</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was glaring at Hagrid and his fists were
clenched.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fdfd781f856ee8e31247ff1d4ce886b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1997">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d103c2532c4c5e2ff5fe7e4e81881241</data>
      <data key="v_content">youlistenhere,,&quot;Now, you listen here, boy,&quot; he snarled, &quot;I accept there&apos;s something
strange about you, probably nothing a good beating wouldn&apos;t have cured
-- and as for all this about your parents, well, they were weirdos, no
denying it, and the world&apos;s better off without them in my opinion --
asked for all they got, getting mixed up with these wizarding types --
just what I expected, always knew they&apos;d come to a sticky end --&quot;
But at that moment, Hagrid leapt from the sofa and drew a battered pink
umbrella from inside his coat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d103c2532c4c5e2ff5fe7e4e81881241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1998">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7289f5ad9778be22a2dd0c0f7be5d645</data>
      <data key="v_content">Pointing this at Uncle Vernon like a
sword, he said, &quot;I&apos;m warning you, Dursley -I&apos;m warning you -- one more
word...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7289f5ad9778be22a2dd0c0f7be5d645</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n1999">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c5ffd7f1b9c2831f358573068c5ed90b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;
In danger of being speared on the end of an umbrella by a bearded giant,
Uncle Vernon&apos;s courage failed again; he flattened himself against the
wall and fell silent.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c5ffd7f1b9c2831f358573068c5ed90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2000">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-234cb0077f50e34f4c071289fb7ef5c4</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidHagrid,,&quot;That&apos;s better,&quot; said Hagrid, breathing heavily and sitting back down on
the sofa, which this time sagged right down to the floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-234cb0077f50e34f4c071289fb7ef5c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2001">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7752a07726c7b674e64fd7a973ce0823</data>
      <data key="v_content">meanwhile,still,44
Harry, meanwhile, still had questions to ask, hundreds of them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7752a07726c7b674e64fd7a973ce0823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2002">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6b9dd9bed4c516ea789f8e6fe14010d6</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But what happened to Vol--, sorry -- I mean, You-Know-Who?&quot;
&quot;Good question, Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6b9dd9bed4c516ea789f8e6fe14010d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2003">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4f5991044fa411f01231e888ba846f6d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Same night he tried ter
kill you.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4f5991044fa411f01231e888ba846f6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2004">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7e5e8535496711b8f9e0e0120199debd</data>
      <data key="v_content">he was gettin&apos; more an&apos; more powerful -- why&apos;d he go?
&quot;Some say he died.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7e5e8535496711b8f9e0e0120199debd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2005">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ec191a661cbaf70b3efdd0bf2895d7f8</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dunno if he had enough
human left in him to die.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ec191a661cbaf70b3efdd0bf2895d7f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2006">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6afdaa4e0f819a03b13232e6b8ae6b62</data>
      <data key="v_content">Some say he&apos;s still out there, bidin&apos; his
time, like, but I don&apos; believe it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6afdaa4e0f819a03b13232e6b8ae6b62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2007">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-461871a8ba1dbff78dab4bd39dd24782</data>
      <data key="v_content">People who was on his side came back
ter ours.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-461871a8ba1dbff78dab4bd39dd24782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2008">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-870f24cfdb9c1d2586d46ac7ff57477d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Some of &apos;em came outta kinda trances.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-870f24cfdb9c1d2586d46ac7ff57477d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2009">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9a5d5375c1baa3fcc2a24027a118e800</data>
      <data key="v_content">Don~ reckon they
could&apos;ve done if he was comin&apos; back.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9a5d5375c1baa3fcc2a24027a118e800</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2010">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-09e44dae94ba58f7685ac69fe84ad96e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Most of us reckon he&apos;s still out there somewhere but lost his powers.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-09e44dae94ba58f7685ac69fe84ad96e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2011">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8beb8ad102fb8e25557e329192e2299b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&apos;Cause somethin&apos; about you finished him, Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8beb8ad102fb8e25557e329192e2299b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2012">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ebde483e73103dfcaaa6d0528f9b296a</data>
      <data key="v_content">There was somethin&apos; goin&apos; on that night he hadn&apos;t counted on -- I dunno
what it was, no one does -- but somethin&apos; about you stumped him, all
right.&quot;
Hagrid looked at Harry with warmth and respect blazing in his eyes, but
Harry, instead of feeling pleased and proud, felt quite sure there had
been a horrible mistake.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ebde483e73103dfcaaa6d0528f9b296a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2013">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d18c7290c8534d950d97b86927e19b22</data>
      <data key="v_content">A wizard? Him? How could he possibly be? He&apos;d
spent his life being clouted by Dudley, and bullied by Aunt Petunia and
Uncle Vernon; if he was really a wizard, why hadn&apos;t they been turned
into warty toads every time they&apos;d tried to lock him in his cupboard? If
he&apos;d once defeated the greatest sorcerer in the world, how come Dudley
had always been able to kick him around like a football?
&quot;Hagrid,&quot; he said quietly, &quot;I think you must have made a mistake.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d18c7290c8534d950d97b86927e19b22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2014">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e7a55989efc5f4d1c96da24fbe435f19</data>
      <data key="v_content">I
don&apos;t think I can be a wizard.&quot;
To his surprise, Hagrid chuckled.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e7a55989efc5f4d1c96da24fbe435f19</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2015">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b59aedcdedb079596f98fd96e727c5c1</data>
      <data key="v_content">eh?,&quot;Not a wizard, eh? Never made things happen when you was scared or
angry?&quot;
Harry looked into the fire.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b59aedcdedb079596f98fd96e727c5c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2016">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ab82ea134e1519f98cee43f889888de5</data>
      <data key="v_content">Now he came to think about it...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ab82ea134e1519f98cee43f889888de5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2017">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2c72129b15bfa76e50d4df5bddf7a8f7</data>
      <data key="v_content">every odd
thing that had ever made his aunt and uncle furious with him had
happened when he, Harry, had been upset or angry...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2c72129b15bfa76e50d4df5bddf7a8f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2018">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e4b952319994c0eb0ccb6cbbb4abf2c4</data>
      <data key="v_content">,chased by Dudley&apos;s
gang, he had somehow found himself out of their reach...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e4b952319994c0eb0ccb6cbbb4abf2c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2019">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-df29011db8d8ca6932ce638085a09e22</data>
      <data key="v_content">dreading going
to school with that ridiculous haircut, he&apos;d managed to make it grow
back...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-df29011db8d8ca6932ce638085a09e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2020">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6962ac351138c963f0d9fb8f2c35dbc8</data>
      <data key="v_content">and the very last time Dudley had hit him, hadn&apos;t he got his
45
revenge, without even realizing he was doing it? Hadn&apos;t he set a boa
constrictor on him?
Harry looked back at Hagrid, smiling, and saw that Hagrid was positively
beaming at him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6962ac351138c963f0d9fb8f2c35dbc8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2021">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a41d673bb3a9c3cd36de25d99379d638</data>
      <data key="v_content">nota,&quot;Harry Potter, not a wizard -- you wait, you&apos;ll be
right famous at Hogwarts.&quot;
But Uncle Vernon wasn&apos;t going to give in without a fight.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a41d673bb3a9c3cd36de25d99379d638</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2022">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3518be45768e9ebee960110d16894726</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Haven&apos;t I told you he&apos;s not going?&quot; he hissed.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3518be45768e9ebee960110d16894726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2023">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-49359ee3ca6d4d31dda2dfc19dfde1d1</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;He&apos;s going to Stonewall
High and he&apos;ll be grateful for it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-49359ee3ca6d4d31dda2dfc19dfde1d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2024">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4b94f4ab5e2157cf1fb1ac0eb77f5f0b</data>
      <data key="v_content">I&apos;ve read those letters and he needs
all sorts of rubbish -- spell books and wands and --&quot;
&quot;If he wants ter go, a great Muggle like you won&apos;t stop him,&quot; growled
Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4b94f4ab5e2157cf1fb1ac0eb77f5f0b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2025">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dfa40855860c3e9f92c895ee7d19c434</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Stop Lily an&apos; James Potter&apos; s son goin&apos; ter Hogwarts! Yer mad.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dfa40855860c3e9f92c895ee7d19c434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2026">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-26753294ffb8fe06a2363548729101a5</data>
      <data key="v_content">His name&apos;s been down ever since he was born.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-26753294ffb8fe06a2363548729101a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2027">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bc99cd0835e6c278445bf6cdc4164854</data>
      <data key="v_content">He&apos;s off ter the finest
school of witchcraft and wizardry in the world.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bc99cd0835e6c278445bf6cdc4164854</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2028">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-51b105b6dacad757c9b5f4ad3d012c4b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Seven years there and he
won&apos;t know himself.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-51b105b6dacad757c9b5f4ad3d012c4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2029">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0b5692fd35cb39fb633f49d35e27c8fd</data>
      <data key="v_content">He&apos;ll be with youngsters of his own sort, fer a
change, an&apos; he&apos;ll be under the greatest headmaster Hogwarts ever had
Albus Dumbled--&quot;
&quot;I AM NOT PAYING FOR SOME CRACKPOT OLD FOOL To TEACH HIM
MAGIC TRICKS!&quot;
yelled Uncle Vernon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0b5692fd35cb39fb633f49d35e27c8fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2030">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1699844d9aa86f257db75bf0806e41e8</data>
      <data key="v_content">But he had finally gone too far.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1699844d9aa86f257db75bf0806e41e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2031">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c49fd29a9cd91e158af0da29b0c0cb9b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid seized his umbrella and whirled
it over his head, &quot;NEVER,&quot; he thundered, &quot;- INSULT- ALBUS- DUMBLEDORE-
IN- FRONT- OF- ME!&quot;
He brought the umbrella swishing down through the air to point at Dudley
-- there was a flash of violet light, a sound like a firecracker, a
sharp squeal, and the next second, Dudley was dancing on the spot with
his hands clasped over his fat bottom, howling in pain.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c49fd29a9cd91e158af0da29b0c0cb9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2032">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bc16c4ef33f2ada04aaa7f839ded7bd6</data>
      <data key="v_content">When he turned
his back on them, Harry saw a curly pig&apos;s tail poking through a hole in
his trousers.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bc16c4ef33f2ada04aaa7f839ded7bd6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2033">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-29f7ba793a13b254599b3aeabe8872f8</data>
      <data key="v_content">Pulling Aunt Petunia and Dudley into the other
room, he cast one last terrified look at Hagrid and slammed the door
behind them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-29f7ba793a13b254599b3aeabe8872f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2034">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-29e1eef52a251e6099694c6926f01c67</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid looked down at his umbrella and stroked his beard.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-29e1eef52a251e6099694c6926f01c67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2035">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1c0fd47773745796f7b41af7556e758e</data>
      <data key="v_content">46
&quot;Shouldn&apos;ta lost me temper,&quot; he said ruefully, &quot;but it didn&apos;t work
anyway.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1c0fd47773745796f7b41af7556e758e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2036">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2bc07a0a2ceb08e8ce75945f16fd32e9</data>
      <data key="v_content">Meant ter turn him into a pig, but I suppose he was so much like
a pig anyway there wasn&apos;t much left ter do.&quot;
He cast a sideways look at Harry under his bushy eyebrows.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2bc07a0a2ceb08e8ce75945f16fd32e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2037">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-328e6d638958ca36fc8268f1e108ba44</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Be grateful if yeh didn&apos;t mention that ter anyone at Hogwarts,&quot; he
said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-328e6d638958ca36fc8268f1e108ba44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2038">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-683f4adf762a6333f8e6e7e2ec9979fa</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I&apos;m -- er -- not supposed ter do magic, strictly speakin&apos;.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-683f4adf762a6333f8e6e7e2ec9979fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2039">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7fa461d28dbaeed446302fd2caa4d668</data>
      <data key="v_content">I was
allowed ter do a bit ter follow yeh an&apos; get yer letters to yeh an&apos; stuff
-- one o&apos; the reasons I was so keen ter take on the job
&quot;Why aren&apos;t you supposed to do magic?&quot; asked Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7fa461d28dbaeed446302fd2caa4d668</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2040">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9ba5584a949dbad97a6fd4072a2325c9</data>
      <data key="v_content">well--I,&quot;Oh, well -- I was at Hogwarts meself but I -- er -- got expelled, ter
tell yeh the truth.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9ba5584a949dbad97a6fd4072a2325c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2041">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-019a9fb6d84703869e829d02f3b8012d</data>
      <data key="v_content">They snapped me wand in half an&apos;
everything.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-019a9fb6d84703869e829d02f3b8012d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2042">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8b1d89d494a642519bfacc17b2dff5b8</data>
      <data key="v_content">But Dumbledore let me stay on as gamekeeper.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8b1d89d494a642519bfacc17b2dff5b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2043">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-97b086dbd747ba11e5a40d8ef62d6885</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dumbledore.&quot;&quot;Why,Great man,
Dumbledore.&quot; &quot;Why were you expelled?&quot;
&quot;It&apos;s gettin&apos; late and we&apos;ve got lots ter do tomorrow,&quot; said Hagrid
loudly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-97b086dbd747ba11e5a40d8ef62d6885</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2044">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-445a36279adbd7eca76943eea1d33c5d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Gotta get up ter town, get all yer books an&apos; that.&quot;
He took off his thick black coat and threw it to Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-445a36279adbd7eca76943eea1d33c5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2045">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b84d8b2b5720c4dcdaa1a0fb4014b45a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You can kip under that,&quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b84d8b2b5720c4dcdaa1a0fb4014b45a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2046">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f3a1b047976e44a4ad2a3fcadf51ad4c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Don&apos; mind if it wriggles a bit, I
think I still got a couple o&apos; dormice in one o&apos; the pockets.&quot;
CHAPTER FIVE
DIAGON ALLEY
Harry woke early the next morning.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f3a1b047976e44a4ad2a3fcadf51ad4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2047">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e557aeb02d62de98d61d5768ede686f1</data>
      <data key="v_content">Although he could tell it was
daylight, he kept his eyes shut tight.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e557aeb02d62de98d61d5768ede686f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2048">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-766cbae7bf9fc1aaad276cd09027fddb</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;It was a dream, he told himself firmly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-766cbae7bf9fc1aaad276cd09027fddb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2049">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-82aa88477466883abcc676146d35561e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I dreamed a giant called
Hagrid came to tell me I was going to a school for wizards.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-82aa88477466883abcc676146d35561e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2050">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6fe91680806f4cd5b3f7c551bf1fcb08</data>
      <data key="v_content">When I open
my eyes I&apos;ll be at home in my cupboard.&quot;
There was suddenly a loud tapping noise.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6fe91680806f4cd5b3f7c551bf1fcb08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2051">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b1c61e01fb4fea2e2e3366f206ec003c</data>
      <data key="v_content">And there&apos;s Aunt Petunia knocking on the door, Harry thought, his heart
sinking.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b1c61e01fb4fea2e2e3366f206ec003c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2052">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-636b7ba39c6a305de41cfecd16f6c8ad</data>
      <data key="v_content">But he still didn&apos;t open his eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-636b7ba39c6a305de41cfecd16f6c8ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2053">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-35b6f1b13d2b244ef024ac883533de3d</data>
      <data key="v_content">It had been such a good
47
dream.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-35b6f1b13d2b244ef024ac883533de3d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2054">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b912d331188f7f37f6d7e901daec15da</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Harrymumbled,,&quot;All right,&quot; Harry mumbled, &quot;I&apos;m getting up.&quot;
He sat up and Hagrid&apos;s heavy coat fell off him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b912d331188f7f37f6d7e901daec15da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2055">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5854697028d0895878ab5f06935f88b9</data>
      <data key="v_content">The hut was full of
sunlight, the storm was over, Hagrid himself was asleep on the collapsed
sofa, and there was an owl rapping its claw on the window, a newspaper
held in its beak.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5854697028d0895878ab5f06935f88b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2056">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c74113762fba565e30540c5f52eb5129</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry scrambled to his feet, so happy he felt as though a large balloon
was swelling inside him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c74113762fba565e30540c5f52eb5129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2057">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8e90ad899932a2ba110fc5581cbeb4b8</data>
      <data key="v_content">He went straight to the window and jerked it
open.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8e90ad899932a2ba110fc5581cbeb4b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2058">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ae5bf98228851b9f23676dbf176fbdf5</data>
      <data key="v_content">The owl swooped in and dropped the newspaper on top of Hagrid, who
didn&apos;t wake up.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ae5bf98228851b9f23676dbf176fbdf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2059">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-61ffc2ba2242f8b6eca33fcee124117f</data>
      <data key="v_content">The owl then fluttered onto the floor and began to
attack Hagrid&apos;s coat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-61ffc2ba2242f8b6eca33fcee124117f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2060">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-665b1b7f5903af210af215cb57004c13</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Don&apos;t do that.&quot;
Harry tried to wave the owl out of the way, but it snapped its beak
fiercely at him and carried on savaging the coat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-665b1b7f5903af210af215cb57004c13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2061">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dc95b4919e5fd205f01492496b40a172</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;There&apos;s an owl
&quot;Pay him,&quot; Hagrid grunted into the sofa.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dc95b4919e5fd205f01492496b40a172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2062">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fab7adef34ac2329878ee9dfe5d75ef3</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;What?&quot;
&quot;He wants payin&apos; fer deliverin&apos; the paper.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fab7adef34ac2329878ee9dfe5d75ef3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2063">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-38d8ec69fd894cc20d9951d134124cb1</data>
      <data key="v_content">Look in the pockets.&quot;
Hagrid&apos;s coat seemed to be made of nothing but pockets -- bunches of
keys, slug pellets, balls of string, peppermint humbugs, teabags...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-38d8ec69fd894cc20d9951d134124cb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2064">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8e53ca2cdabe68b9d4a6307e4346da98</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harrypulledout,finally, Harry pulled out a handful of strange-looking coins.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8e53ca2cdabe68b9d4a6307e4346da98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2065">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0d2c2140eb1b5a4dccd992391aa72da5</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;Give him five Knuts,&quot; said Hagrid sleepily.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0d2c2140eb1b5a4dccd992391aa72da5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2066">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a0ca00d154102b741b78957d7e816ebf</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Knuts?&quot;
&quot;The little bronze ones.&quot;
Harry counted out five little bronze coins, and the owl held out his leg
so Harry could put the money into a small leather pouch tied to it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a0ca00d154102b741b78957d7e816ebf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2067">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cb1693708ade47f64a0e2ddf82b2be31</data>
      <data key="v_content">Then
he flew off through the open window.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cb1693708ade47f64a0e2ddf82b2be31</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2068">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6c52602b97cb61f0dc7fe9b00a42f675</data>
      <data key="v_content">,48
Hagrid yawned loudly, sat up, and stretched.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6c52602b97cb61f0dc7fe9b00a42f675</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2069">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c3087518d9f3d689f7d6e8efa5e02963</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry,,&quot;Best be Off, Harry, lots ter do today, gotta get up ter London an&apos; buy
all yer stuff fer school.&quot;
Harry was turning over the wizard coins and looking at them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c3087518d9f3d689f7d6e8efa5e02963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2070">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2870c5dddb94b12429d8049614498c93</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had just
thought of something that made him feel as though the happy balloon
inside him had got a puncture.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2870c5dddb94b12429d8049614498c93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2071">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a5d2201cd4ddfc637455a0a49138777b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Um -- Hagrid?&quot;
&quot;Mm?&quot; said Hagrid, who was pulling on his huge boots.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a5d2201cd4ddfc637455a0a49138777b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2072">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8c2fbe08f81cc97e41dc9b4cf6e6c34b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I haven&apos;t got any money -- and you heard Uncle Vernon last night ...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8c2fbe08f81cc97e41dc9b4cf6e6c34b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2073">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-477b75e23f1858930dca362cd578215e</data>
      <data key="v_content">he
won&apos;t pay for me to go and learn magic.&quot;
&quot;Don&apos;t worry about that,&quot; said Hagrid, standing up and scratching his
head.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-477b75e23f1858930dca362cd578215e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2074">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4642893f9d07e77d064ff8c96c441849</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;D&apos;yeh think yer parents didn&apos;t leave yeh anything?&quot;
&quot;But if their house was destroyed --&quot;
&quot;They didn&apos; keep their gold in the house, boy! Nah, first stop fer us is
Gringotts.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4642893f9d07e77d064ff8c96c441849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2075">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-63d5424cafe03a5e69adf8c3530a67ae</data>
      <data key="v_content">they&apos;re,Have a sausage, they&apos;re not bad cold -- an&apos; I
wouldn&apos; say no teh a bit o&apos; yer birthday cake, neither.&quot;
&quot;Wizards have banks?&quot;
&quot;Just the one.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-63d5424cafe03a5e69adf8c3530a67ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2076">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-83627244356066a2330d7f142c8cbe3f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Run by goblins.&quot;
Harry dropped the bit of sausage he was holding.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-83627244356066a2330d7f142c8cbe3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2077">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b3047dd398158e92e98fe6cfd465014d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Goblins?&quot;
&quot;Yeah -- so yeh&apos;d be mad ter try an&apos; rob it, I&apos;ll tell yeh that.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b3047dd398158e92e98fe6cfd465014d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2078">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-153da7d221e3615f296d77d8a6e17aff</data>
      <data key="v_content">Gringotts is the safest place in the world fer
anything yeh want ter keep safe -- &apos;cept maybe Hogwarts.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-153da7d221e3615f296d77d8a6e17aff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2079">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4789c58cb5ae928e9d87ca932b41d8f1</data>
      <data key="v_content">As a matter o&apos;
fact, I gotta visit Gringotts anyway.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4789c58cb5ae928e9d87ca932b41d8f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2080">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eba77bc9f054a5b9a7f6cc2eb1fb3505</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hogwarts
business.&quot; Hagrid drew himself up proudly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eba77bc9f054a5b9a7f6cc2eb1fb3505</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2081">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e7ba65a5c79d94f6eb783864a51bc854</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;He usually gets me ter do
important stuff fer him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e7ba65a5c79d94f6eb783864a51bc854</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2082">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-edc65131618c2eb79cfd020116d056e9</data>
      <data key="v_content">Fetchin&apos; you gettin&apos; things from Gringotts --
knows he can trust me, see.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-edc65131618c2eb79cfd020116d056e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2083">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d6e7eb40e2aa4eb37a7ee9ece1a27c61</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Got everythin&apos;? Come on, then.&quot;
49
Harry followed Hagrid out onto the rock.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d6e7eb40e2aa4eb37a7ee9ece1a27c61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2084">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dcf4c4198138941c9d726aa882798d72</data>
      <data key="v_content">The sky was quite clear now and
the sea gleamed in the sunlight.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dcf4c4198138941c9d726aa882798d72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2085">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-56d9379ac9f42f06d9c2e49658ff10f5</data>
      <data key="v_content">The boat Uncle Vernon had hired was
still there, with a lot of water in the bottom after the storm.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-56d9379ac9f42f06d9c2e49658ff10f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2086">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-06c1152545fbf38d22637f7e768b1695</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;How did you get here?&quot; Harry asked, looking around for another boat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-06c1152545fbf38d22637f7e768b1695</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2087">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c27e7de636d077015cef1b9f8aaea026</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Flew?&quot;
&quot;Yeah -- but we&apos;ll go back in this.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c27e7de636d077015cef1b9f8aaea026</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2088">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-27fbae255b83b926edee77048908e27b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Not s&apos;pposed ter use magic now I&apos;ve
got yeh.&quot;
They settled down in the boat, Harry still staring at Hagrid, trying to
imagine him flying.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-27fbae255b83b926edee77048908e27b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2089">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a0dee96001a896c688f244dc637944fd</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Seems a shame ter row, though,&quot; said Hagrid, giving Harry another of
his sideways looks.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a0dee96001a896c688f244dc637944fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2090">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-334401254d2b4eafd37e56643e58dd94</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;If I was ter -- er -- speed things up a bit, would
yeh mind not mentionin&apos; it at Hogwarts?&quot;
&quot;Of course not,&quot; said Harry, eager to see more magic.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-334401254d2b4eafd37e56643e58dd94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2091">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e3cd8f2298c21b2a6ae80a81659a85a3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid pulled out
the pink umbrella again, tapped it twice on the side of the boat, and
they sped off toward land.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e3cd8f2298c21b2a6ae80a81659a85a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2092">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d85f970861d49fcd0d5e3128e7978ec3</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Why would you be mad to try and rob Gringotts?&quot; Harry asked.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d85f970861d49fcd0d5e3128e7978ec3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2093">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eb1b6fd8bebf9488df9c79d69692db92</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;said,&quot;Spells -- enchantments,&quot; said Hagrid, unfolding his newspaper as he
spoke.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eb1b6fd8bebf9488df9c79d69692db92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2094">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-626b31c79b5629e5f5917237e22eb072</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;They say there&apos;s dragons guardin&apos; the highsecurity vaults.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-626b31c79b5629e5f5917237e22eb072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2095">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4dae36f02aa200d29996f01a49a6a51a</data>
      <data key="v_content">And
then yeh gotta find yer way -- Gringotts is hundreds of miles under
London, see.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4dae36f02aa200d29996f01a49a6a51a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2096">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5577a7d2c60155e660e4c046ace3cdba</data>
      <data key="v_content">Yeh&apos;d die of hunger tryin&apos; ter
get out, even if yeh did manage ter get yer hands on summat.&quot;
Harry sat and thought about this while Hagrid read his newspaper, the
Daily Prophet.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5577a7d2c60155e660e4c046ace3cdba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2097">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2139a4b128481552598138ee538c8608</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry had learned from Uncle Vernon that people liked to
be left alone while they did this, but it was very difficult, he&apos;d never
had so many questions in his life.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2139a4b128481552598138ee538c8608</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2098">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-529c08ad70939971999f4e2830eca6b4</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Ministry o&apos; Magic messin&apos; things up as usual,&quot; Hagrid muttered, turning
the page.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-529c08ad70939971999f4e2830eca6b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2099">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-367d69899f9016ba279253ffae4bc718</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;There&apos;s a Ministry of Magic?&quot; Harry asked, before he could stop
himself.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-367d69899f9016ba279253ffae4bc718</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2100">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3edf7f5850e5f62ec8f5fb25d27cd647</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;They wanted Dumbledore fer Minister, 0 &apos;
50
course, but he&apos;d never leave Hogwarts, so old Cornelius Fudge got the
job.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3edf7f5850e5f62ec8f5fb25d27cd647</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2101">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5a01f68edd046025b5fb87168ea4dd5e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Bungler if ever there was one.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5a01f68edd046025b5fb87168ea4dd5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2102">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1356518f5f3f7e9c63455747e39b6963</data>
      <data key="v_content">So he pelts Dumbledore with owls
every morning, askin&apos; fer advice.&quot;
&quot;But what does a Ministry of Magic do?&quot;
&quot;Well, their main job is to keep it from the Muggles that there&apos;s still
witches an&apos; wizards up an&apos; down the country.&quot;
&quot;Why?&quot;
&quot;Why? Blimey, Harry, everyone&apos;d be wantin&apos; magic solutions to their
problems.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1356518f5f3f7e9c63455747e39b6963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2103">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9410e60c18406fa797f0d2bbe5129768</data>
      <data key="v_content">we&apos;rebestleft,Nah, we&apos;re best left alone.&quot;
At this moment the boat bumped gently into the harbor wall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9410e60c18406fa797f0d2bbe5129768</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2104">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-283134b10c525016b5fe99ec88128ef6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid
folded up his newspaper, and they clambered up the stone steps onto the
street.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-283134b10c525016b5fe99ec88128ef6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2105">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c12f80d33dc73357e80943afff7a5a33</data>
      <data key="v_content">Passersby stared a lot at Hagrid as they walked through the little town
to the station.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c12f80d33dc73357e80943afff7a5a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2106">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-290ea00c9974c5b65e33bf587c41f33d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Not only was Hagrid twice as
tall as anyone else, he kept pointing at perfectly ordinary things like
parking meters and saying loudly, &quot;See that, Harry? Things these Muggles
dream up, eh?&quot;
&quot;Hagrid,&quot; said Harry, panting a bit as he ran to keep up, &quot;did you say
there are dragons at Gringotts?&quot;
&quot;Well, so they say,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-290ea00c9974c5b65e33bf587c41f33d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2107">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a31ba1e58e794404e2f84c1574cc8f9c</data>
      <data key="v_content">I&apos;dlikea,&quot;Crikey, I&apos;d like a dragon.&quot;
&quot;You&apos;d like one?&quot;
&quot;Wanted one ever since I was a kid -- here we go.&quot;
They had reached the station.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a31ba1e58e794404e2f84c1574cc8f9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2108">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-97e5e3e833610d5ab4701758752488ad</data>
      <data key="v_content">There was a train to London in five
minutes&apos; time.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-97e5e3e833610d5ab4701758752488ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2109">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1327b625d1106bbd6ec64aaf1d9de6b6</data>
      <data key="v_content">whodidn&apos;tunderstand,Hagrid, who didn&apos;t understand &quot;Muggle money,&quot; as he
called it, gave the bills to Harry so he could buy their tickets.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1327b625d1106bbd6ec64aaf1d9de6b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2110">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-08bc4f3de9ba02520007e1289435a1ca</data>
      <data key="v_content">People stared more than ever on the train.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-08bc4f3de9ba02520007e1289435a1ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2111">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-63a190cc6d957d69f5b9386ba5985d00</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid took up two seats and
sat knitting what looked like a canary-yellow circus tent.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-63a190cc6d957d69f5b9386ba5985d00</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2112">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2a5bd39d12082c3da4ce15c1eed6f59f</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Still got yer letter, Harry?&quot; he asked as he counted stitches.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2a5bd39d12082c3da4ce15c1eed6f59f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2113">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0f7c146299282bf484a7bc95f3dc14ef</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry
took the parchment envelope out of his pocket.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0f7c146299282bf484a7bc95f3dc14ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2114">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-80f070032c95417d7fc143c8f3e05dda</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;There&apos;s a list there of everything yeh need.&quot;
Harry unfolded a second piece of paper he hadn&apos;t noticed the night
before, and read:
HOGWARTS SCHOOL of WITCHCRAFT and WIZARDRY
UNIFORM
First-year students will require:
1.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-80f070032c95417d7fc143c8f3e05dda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2115">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8c2b73e8c02f980abe13469c75f750ae</data>
      <data key="v_content">Three sets of plain work robes (black)
2.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8c2b73e8c02f980abe13469c75f750ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2116">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-49451ff0ab995c2a431f079b72a9aad4</data>
      <data key="v_content">One plain pointed hat (black) for day wear
3.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-49451ff0ab995c2a431f079b72a9aad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2117">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-962f1f5fbb4f1a3f477601b1ef22cdb8</data>
      <data key="v_content">One pair of protective gloves (dragon hide or similar)
4.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-962f1f5fbb4f1a3f477601b1ef22cdb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2118">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-50678a11db27c7d4024fb717840c7b67</data>
      <data key="v_content">,One winter cloak (black, silver fastenings)
Please note that all pupils&apos; clothes should carry name tags
COURSE BOOKS
All students should have a copy of each of the following:
The Standard Book of Spells (Grade 1) by Miranda Goshawk
A History of Magic by Bathilda Bagshot
Magical Theory by Adalbert Waffling
A Beginners&apos; Guide to Transfiguration by Emetic Switch
One Thousand Magical Herbs and Fungi by Phyllida Spore
Magical Drafts and Potions by Arsenius Jigger
Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them by Newt Scamander
The Dark Forces: A Guide to Self-Protection by Quentin Trimble
OTHER EQUIPMENT
52
wand cauldron (pewter, standard size 2) set
glass or crystal phials
telescope set
brass scales
Students may also bring an owl OR a cat OR a toad
PARENTS ARE REMINDED THAT FIRST YEARS ARE NOT ALLOWED
THEIR OWN
BROOMSTICKS
&quot;Can we buy all this in London?&quot; Harry wondered aloud.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-50678a11db27c7d4024fb717840c7b67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2119">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e5e356278ada47d18108973e2eb4d5ab</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;If yeh know where to go,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e5e356278ada47d18108973e2eb4d5ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2120">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f257a0bf5c1529ff06188ba83109b1ac</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry had never been to London before.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f257a0bf5c1529ff06188ba83109b1ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2121">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d4f52b6b6fe912c72ad762373144ff54</data>
      <data key="v_content">Although Hagrid seemed to know
where he was going, he was obviously not used to getting there in an
ordinary way.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d4f52b6b6fe912c72ad762373144ff54</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2122">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1113cfbc50eea069cc917be9c86dd67c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He got stuck in the ticket barrier on the Underground, and
complained loudly that the seats were too small and the trains too slow.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1113cfbc50eea069cc917be9c86dd67c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2123">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-88352dc8e1827117b704c27ec7f2932b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I don&apos;t know how the Muggles manage without magic,&quot; he said as they
climbed a broken-down escalator that led up to a bustling road lined
with shops.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-88352dc8e1827117b704c27ec7f2932b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2124">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5d5773056ec5e427bc5bca3bddfa4137</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid was so huge that he parted the crowd easily; all Harry had to do
was keep close behind him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5d5773056ec5e427bc5bca3bddfa4137</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2125">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-10215e4110e00a724f7aaec19387e23a</data>
      <data key="v_content">They passed book shops and music stores,
hamburger restaurants and cinemas, but nowhere that looked as if it
could sell you a magic wand.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-10215e4110e00a724f7aaec19387e23a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2126">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a007dd8cf51e2ba47a459d79379ee712</data>
      <data key="v_content">This was just an ordinary street full of
ordinary people.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a007dd8cf51e2ba47a459d79379ee712</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2127">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3f592e784dcadd5e56d98f3b0583d790</data>
      <data key="v_content">Could there really be piles of wizard gold buried miles
beneath them? Were there really shops that sold spell books and
broomsticks? Might this not all be some huge joke that the Dursleys had
cooked up? If Harry hadn&apos;t known that the Dursleys had no sense of
humor, he might have thought so; yet somehow, even though everything
Hagrid had told him so far was unbelievable, Harry couldn&apos;t help
trusting him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3f592e784dcadd5e56d98f3b0583d790</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2128">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b9be4466343ec38b08a5eac149ac022f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;said,&quot;This is it,&quot; said Hagrid, coming to a halt, &quot;the Leaky Cauldron.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b9be4466343ec38b08a5eac149ac022f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2129">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a20912881a82507455ecf4136fa6b6c5</data>
      <data key="v_content">It&apos;s a
famous place.&quot;
It was a tiny, grubby-looking pub.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a20912881a82507455ecf4136fa6b6c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2130">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e9e8ec088d5f03f2f7da958a54f78e0e</data>
      <data key="v_content">If Hagrid hadn&apos;t pointed it out,
53
Harry wouldn&apos;t have noticed it was there.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e9e8ec088d5f03f2f7da958a54f78e0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2131">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5cdbe103744362a72007b313fc259c2d</data>
      <data key="v_content">The people hurrying by didn&apos;t
glance at it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5cdbe103744362a72007b313fc259c2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2132">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cb2d1517cd4465d0c25f8691490bc4e7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Their eyes slid from the big book shop on one side to the
record shop on the other as if they couldn&apos;t see the Leaky Cauldron at
all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cb2d1517cd4465d0c25f8691490bc4e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2133">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5df6fad539182e3b5d198a2b23ec2a18</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harryhad,In fact, Harry had the most peculiar feeling that only he and
Hagrid could see it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5df6fad539182e3b5d198a2b23ec2a18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2134">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7212a6d63ed5a6142dc392bf5ff638ce</data>
      <data key="v_content">Before he could mention this, Hagrid had steered
him inside.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7212a6d63ed5a6142dc392bf5ff638ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2135">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0a697fcb3967ce45c3a349882bf7eff2</data>
      <data key="v_content">,For a famous place, it was very dark and shabby.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0a697fcb3967ce45c3a349882bf7eff2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2136">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cabb1a662fb2c17b64f115d0d0bccf5b</data>
      <data key="v_content">A few old women were
sitting in a corner, drinking tiny glasses of sherry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cabb1a662fb2c17b64f115d0d0bccf5b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2137">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-23f582058394a6eeae6f603b1f390bb3</data>
      <data key="v_content">One of them was
smoking a long pipe.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-23f582058394a6eeae6f603b1f390bb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2138">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-080a17eb11aab98328c394ac91cf9ab9</data>
      <data key="v_content">A little man in a top hat was talking to the old
bartender, who was quite bald and looked like a toothless walnut.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-080a17eb11aab98328c394ac91cf9ab9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2139">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-626957fe45943732dc09fcd14a5fa51b</data>
      <data key="v_content">The
low buzz of chatter stopped when they walked in.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-626957fe45943732dc09fcd14a5fa51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2140">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-990c74b0dcd2ca498b777afa63fd057c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Everyone seemed to know
Hagrid; they waved and smiled at him, and the bartender reached for a
glass, saying, &quot;The usual, Hagrid?&quot;
&quot;Can&apos;t, Tom, I&apos;m on Hogwarts business,&quot; said Hagrid, clapping his great
hand on Harry&apos;s shoulder and making Harry&apos;s knees buckle.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-990c74b0dcd2ca498b777afa63fd057c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2141">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-224854c6c0c5e53446706927bea44294</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidthe,&quot;Good Lord,&quot; said the bartender, peering at Harry, &quot;is this -- can this
be --?&quot;
The Leaky Cauldron had suddenly gone completely still and silent.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-224854c6c0c5e53446706927bea44294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2142">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9d44d501afa0ef4f685293936c8cddfb</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;whispered,&quot;Bless my soul,&quot; whispered the old bartender, &quot;Harry Potter...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9d44d501afa0ef4f685293936c8cddfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2143">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7806421ecec48877102988b121455956</data>
      <data key="v_content">what an
honor.&quot;
He hurried out from behind the bar, rushed toward Harry and seized his
hand, tears in his eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7806421ecec48877102988b121455956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2144">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d765db66b41bc6cc8631e6216faa2b2d</data>
      <data key="v_content">welcomeback.&quot;Harry,Potter, welcome back.&quot;
Harry didn&apos;t know what to say.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d765db66b41bc6cc8631e6216faa2b2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2145">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0596d0c320a47a61ac710b545a924c4e</data>
      <data key="v_content">The old
woman with the pipe was puffing on it without realizing it had gone out.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0596d0c320a47a61ac710b545a924c4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2146">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0d28e56a09c4514b064bdffc4ed5f20c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Then there was a great scraping of chairs and the next moment, Harry
found himself shaking hands with everyone in the Leaky Cauldron.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0d28e56a09c4514b064bdffc4ed5f20c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2147">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4468e7bdffd1213dba1f771eb5ee9d1f</data>
      <data key="v_content">can&apos;tbelieveI&apos;m,Potter, can&apos;t believe I&apos;m meeting you at last.&quot;
&quot;So proud, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4468e7bdffd1213dba1f771eb5ee9d1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2148">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-185989abce400f67a3ff9af3c452e12b</data>
      <data key="v_content">I&apos;mjustso,Potter, I&apos;m just so proud.&quot;
54
&quot;Always wanted to shake your hand -- I&apos;m all of a flutter.&quot;
&quot;Delighted, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-185989abce400f67a3ff9af3c452e12b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2149">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fec19bee7ff0149def99f46954260747</data>
      <data key="v_content">justcan&apos;ttell,Potter, just can&apos;t tell you, Diggle&apos;s the name, Dedalus
Diggle.&quot;
&quot;I&apos;ve seen you before!&quot; said Harry, as Dedalus Diggle&apos;s top hat fell off
in his excitement.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fec19bee7ff0149def99f46954260747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2150">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-82d147416b080838d60e510e4e7bba48</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You bowed to me once in a shop.&quot;
&quot;He remembers!&quot; cried Dedalus Diggle, looking around at everyone.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-82d147416b080838d60e510e4e7bba48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2151">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cdd53343bf6227718532bad3a8c8e770</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Did
you hear that? He remembers me!&quot; Harry shook hands again and again --
Doris Crockford kept coming back for more.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cdd53343bf6227718532bad3a8c8e770</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2152">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-246b1c3bc825b3c6b49969d995d834b8</data>
      <data key="v_content">A pale young man made his way forward, very nervously.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-246b1c3bc825b3c6b49969d995d834b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2153">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-574425a388836c1db03f7da488e25e98</data>
      <data key="v_content">One of his eyes
was twitching.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-574425a388836c1db03f7da488e25e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2154">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-173fcff52074cba0e61344d5ddb04762</data>
      <data key="v_content">ProfessorQuirrellwill,&quot;Harry, Professor Quirrell will be
one of your teachers at Hogwarts.&quot;
&quot;P-P-Potter,&quot; stammered Professor Quirrell, grasping Harry&apos;s hand,
&quot;c-can&apos;t t-tell you how p- pleased I am to meet you.&quot;
&quot;What sort of magic do you teach, Professor Quirrell?&quot;
&quot;D-Defense Against the D-D-Dark Arts,&quot; muttered Professor Quirrell, as
though he&apos;d rather not think about it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-173fcff52074cba0e61344d5ddb04762</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2155">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f60c1d960aca58c09a50d7d67abf6a0b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;N-not that you n-need it, eh,
P-P-Potter?&quot; He laughed nervously.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f60c1d960aca58c09a50d7d67abf6a0b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2156">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6fb76d7a5193e3b65feb7782f15e289d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You&apos;ll be g-getting all your
equipment, I suppose? I&apos;ve g-got to p-pick up a new b-book on vampires,
m-myself.&quot; He looked terrified at the very thought.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6fb76d7a5193e3b65feb7782f15e289d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2157">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ade4f5ac664ed860bd346a5b2d031919</data>
      <data key="v_content">But the others wouldn&apos;t let Professor Quirrell keep Harry to himself.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ade4f5ac664ed860bd346a5b2d031919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2158">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6423d26181a17dbba45842bf043dc58a</data>
      <data key="v_content">It
took almost ten minutes to get away from them all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6423d26181a17dbba45842bf043dc58a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2159">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d7db909975b65501d4b82a3410d8908b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagridmanaged,At last, Hagrid
managed to make himself heard over the babble.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d7db909975b65501d4b82a3410d8908b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2160">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-812904ffb7253dfbfd4f7ab218f9cac5</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Must get on -- lots ter buy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-812904ffb7253dfbfd4f7ab218f9cac5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2161">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c19acc2713090a76fba5e5ef1f410e20</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry.&quot;Doris,Come on, Harry.&quot;
Doris Crockford shook Harry&apos;s hand one last time, and Hagrid led them
through the bar and out into a small, walled courtyard, where there was
nothing but a trash can and a few weeds.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c19acc2713090a76fba5e5ef1f410e20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2162">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2d762871f7d4e6b9d636afba14e5a45d</data>
      <data key="v_content">didn&apos;tI?,&quot;Told yeh, didn&apos;t I? Told yeh you was famous.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2d762871f7d4e6b9d636afba14e5a45d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2163">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a6bb88db1182dc92a727094857949d0b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Even Professor Quirrell
55
was tremblin&apos; ter meet yeh -- mind you, he&apos;s usually tremblin&apos;.&quot;
&quot;Is he always that nervous?&quot;
&quot;Oh, yeah.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a6bb88db1182dc92a727094857949d0b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2164">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bab2fc3f03e5edee24d8536299a61411</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was fine while he was
studyin&apos; outta books but then he took a year off ter get some firsthand
experience....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bab2fc3f03e5edee24d8536299a61411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2165">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ae5b84d01968d0bd1a919475ccb31279</data>
      <data key="v_content">They say he met vampires in the Black Forest, and there
was a nasty bit o&apos; trouble with a hag -- never been the same since.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ae5b84d01968d0bd1a919475ccb31279</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2166">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0b737b3a46644be0c0f15349c9599e8c</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Scared of the students, scared of his own subject now, where&apos;s me
umbrella?&quot;
Vampires? Hags? Harry&apos;s head was swimming.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0b737b3a46644be0c0f15349c9599e8c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2167">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-62b316b3a30d5c00045b4502aef5fd15</data>
      <data key="v_content">meanwhile,wascounting,Hagrid, meanwhile, was
counting bricks in the wall above the trash can.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-62b316b3a30d5c00045b4502aef5fd15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2168">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-875055ee413a5243f81cc0c7106c1547</data>
      <data key="v_content">standback,Harry.&quot;,&quot;Right, stand back, Harry.&quot;
He tapped the wall three times with the point of his umbrella.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-875055ee413a5243f81cc0c7106c1547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2169">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d4dbacfd2be8030c65d84c1b06910e48</data>
      <data key="v_content">The brick he had touched quivered -- it wriggled -- in the middle, a
small hole appeared -- it grew wider and wider -- a second later they
were facing an archway large enough even for Hagrid, an archway onto a
cobbled street that twisted and turned out of sight.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d4dbacfd2be8030c65d84c1b06910e48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2170">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-29cad7ad14fa87effd7dbf4d9ff97823</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidHagrid,&quot;to,&quot;Welcome,&quot; said Hagrid, &quot;to Diagon Alley.&quot;
He grinned at Harry&apos;s amazement.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-29cad7ad14fa87effd7dbf4d9ff97823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2171">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1a59729c96e195212ae31c1da46b882e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry
looked quickly over his shoulder and saw the archway shrink instantly
back into solid wall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1a59729c96e195212ae31c1da46b882e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2172">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7711ff3ba51de21883088f3e43d909cb</data>
      <data key="v_content">The sun shone brightly on a stack of cauldrons outside the nearest shop.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7711ff3ba51de21883088f3e43d909cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2173">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-28c98a7321ac9750cb65e17eeb2061f4</data>
      <data key="v_content">Cauldrons -- All Sizes - Copper, Brass, Pewter, Silver -- Self-Stirring
-- Collapsible, said a sign hanging over them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-28c98a7321ac9750cb65e17eeb2061f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2174">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-738529d03edcbdc43b73745972a58b83</data>
      <data key="v_content">you&apos;llbeneedin&apos;,&quot;Yeah, you&apos;ll be needin&apos; one,&quot; said Hagrid, &quot;but we gotta get yer money
first.&quot;
Harry wished he had about eight more eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-738529d03edcbdc43b73745972a58b83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2175">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8debe9e2f4f17f7f55ee960edc24b17c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He turned his head in every
direction as they walked up the street, trying to look at everything at
once: the shops, the things outside them, the people doing their
shopping.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8debe9e2f4f17f7f55ee960edc24b17c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2176">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b76277c2528daf40cf38b98e82b427e3</data>
      <data key="v_content">A plump woman outside an Apothecary was shaking her head as
they passed, saying, &quot;Dragon liver, seventeen Sickles an ounce, they&apos;re
mad....&quot;
56
A low, soft hooting came from a dark shop with a sign saying Eeylops Owl
Emporium -- Tawny, Screech, Barn, Brown, and Snowy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b76277c2528daf40cf38b98e82b427e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2177">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d76e2ecace43fd4ca14dcb21fcd3464f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Several boys of
about Harry&apos;s age had their noses pressed against a window with
broomsticks in it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d76e2ecace43fd4ca14dcb21fcd3464f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2178">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3ae6619f3f180cea33921e8a345c841b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Harryheardone,&quot;Look,&quot; Harry heard one of them say, &quot;the new Nimbus
Two Thousand -- fastest ever --&quot; There were shops selling robes, shops
selling telescopes and strange silver instruments Harry had never seen
before, windows stacked with barrels of bat spleens and eels&apos; eyes,
tottering piles of spell books, quills, and rolls of parchment, potion
bottles, globes of the moon....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3ae6619f3f180cea33921e8a345c841b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2179">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f3e68855f19562645e016eb4c8dddeb7</data>
      <data key="v_content">They had reached a snowy white building that towered over the other
little shops.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f3e68855f19562645e016eb4c8dddeb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2180">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a0ff3881ba2a861ccd833ed285875c76</data>
      <data key="v_content">Standing beside its burnished bronze doors, wearing a
uniform of scarlet and gold, was -
&quot;Yeah, that&apos;s a goblin,&quot; said Hagrid quietly as they walked up the white
stone steps toward him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a0ff3881ba2a861ccd833ed285875c76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2181">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0db69af0ca29c0f24961cc8f34a14658</data>
      <data key="v_content">The goblin was about a head shorter than Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0db69af0ca29c0f24961cc8f34a14658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2182">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8132538e596056613cc0f81be50da490</data>
      <data key="v_content">,He had a swarthy, clever face, a pointed beard and, Harry noticed, very
long fingers and feet.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8132538e596056613cc0f81be50da490</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2183">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b19e5119d06285d11db0223189d210c6</data>
      <data key="v_content">He bowed as they walked inside.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b19e5119d06285d11db0223189d210c6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2184">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8ff22d68f16b2f18dda2c4e148e2df1f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Now they were
facing a second pair of doors, silver this time, with words engraved
upon them:
Enter, stranger, but take heed
Of what awaits the sin of greed,
For those who take, but do not earn,
Must pay most dearly in their turn.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8ff22d68f16b2f18dda2c4e148e2df1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2185">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dcd2df7e4b2730c9fb796fc76d0873f9</data>
      <data key="v_content">So if you seek beneath our floors
A treasure that was never yours,
Thief, you have been warned, beware
Of finding more than treasure there.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dcd2df7e4b2730c9fb796fc76d0873f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2186">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ed071f7d51fdd9c0ada3349a72fce72d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Yeh&apos;d,&quot;Like I said, Yeh&apos;d be mad ter try an&apos; rob it,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ed071f7d51fdd9c0ada3349a72fce72d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2187">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-87d91be285f3ab12d7fa0fdad9bd6aea</data>
      <data key="v_content">A pair of goblins bowed them through the silver doors and they were in a
57
vast marble hall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-87d91be285f3ab12d7fa0fdad9bd6aea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2188">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b64a464fe8fd031ee4ec19c98a158808</data>
      <data key="v_content">About a hundred more goblins were sitting on high
stools behind a long counter, scribbling in large ledgers, weighing
coins in brass scales, examining precious stones through eyeglasses.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b64a464fe8fd031ee4ec19c98a158808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2189">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d198265faf38f53f7f9042946de81283</data>
      <data key="v_content">There were too many doors to count leading off the hall, and yet more
goblins were showing people in and out of these.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d198265faf38f53f7f9042946de81283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2190">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-300d938f2fc9ebd5eac7409bc73182e3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid and Harry made
for the counter.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-300d938f2fc9ebd5eac7409bc73182e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2191">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ece4ffa3aace28cb27cc85c047ac3d6b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidHagridto,&quot;Morning,&quot; said Hagrid to a free goblin.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ece4ffa3aace28cb27cc85c047ac3d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2192">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-09b3d100e4f2ddc94a11e292ebe3636b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;We&apos;ve come ter take some money
outta Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-09b3d100e4f2ddc94a11e292ebe3636b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2193">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a50f2817aec310afe3d68771734291ed</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry Potter&apos;s safe.&quot;
&quot;You have his key, Sir?&quot;
&quot;Got it here somewhere,&quot; said Hagrid, and he started emptying his
pockets onto the counter, scattering a handful of moldy dog biscuits
over the goblin&apos;s book of numbers.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a50f2817aec310afe3d68771734291ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2194">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7f534ad2d0f7587995f62a4b6f80a00f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry
watched the goblin on their right weighing a pile of rubies as big as
glowing coals.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7f534ad2d0f7587995f62a4b6f80a00f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2195">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bc62fa67ee5ab1051739924fc079d191</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidHagrid,&quot;Got it,&quot; said Hagrid at last, holding up a tiny golden key.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bc62fa67ee5ab1051739924fc079d191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2196">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1e70e141904c13f4f0d67feeebcbd232</data>
      <data key="v_content">The goblin looked at it closely.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1e70e141904c13f4f0d67feeebcbd232</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2197">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7f6f28b6b6bc44b5c468e90228e2f55c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;That seems to be in order.&quot;
&quot;An&apos; I&apos;ve also got a letter here from Professor Dumbledore,&quot; said Hagrid
importantly, throwing out his chest.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7f6f28b6b6bc44b5c468e90228e2f55c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2198">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-61ccefb5f8d5ad9cae556723cce94908</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;It&apos;s about the YouKnow-What in
vault seven hundred and thirteen.&quot;
The goblin read the letter carefully.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-61ccefb5f8d5ad9cae556723cce94908</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2199">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-daa10961f5688addd41f5e49eaaaa671</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;hesaid,,&quot;Very well,&quot; he said, handing it back to Hagrid, &quot;I will have Someone
take you down to both vaults.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-daa10961f5688addd41f5e49eaaaa671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2200">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ac6ca9e7e0cbc7ac3bbc7becd8ae5717</data>
      <data key="v_content">Griphook!&quot;
Griphook was yet another goblin.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ac6ca9e7e0cbc7ac3bbc7becd8ae5717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2201">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-764211e300d6e8e3f0cad6b55818495f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Once Hagrid had crammed all the dog
biscuits back inside his pockets, he and Harry followed Griphook toward
one of the doors leading off the hall.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-764211e300d6e8e3f0cad6b55818495f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2202">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-85e9d879cac1226a5f66563376fac2fb</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;What&apos;s the You-Know-What in vault seven hundred and thirteen?&quot; Harry
asked.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-85e9d879cac1226a5f66563376fac2fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2203">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-07a89671dc05a2255350b5daf3bf90da</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;Can&apos;t tell yeh that,&quot; said Hagrid mysteriously.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-07a89671dc05a2255350b5daf3bf90da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2204">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b6caa10e0ce0d5536e1213defa84ad25</data>
      <data key="v_content">More&apos;n my job&apos;s worth ter tell yeh
that.&quot;
58
Griphook held the door open for them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b6caa10e0ce0d5536e1213defa84ad25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2205">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-43bc2a413d318e3e0dfcfa054d367ab0</data>
      <data key="v_content">whohadexpected,Harry, who had expected more
marble, was surprised.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-43bc2a413d318e3e0dfcfa054d367ab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2206">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9018d93cb46957de566a3d88a43c3a76</data>
      <data key="v_content">They were in a narrow stone passageway lit with
flaming torches.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9018d93cb46957de566a3d88a43c3a76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2207">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f3ec52cda2a4c01aa0f6ed8d323c1c9a</data>
      <data key="v_content">It sloped steeply downward and there were little
railway tracks on the floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f3ec52cda2a4c01aa0f6ed8d323c1c9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2208">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7bc35dc8b9551f36cecb4f9183a4add2</data>
      <data key="v_content">Griphook whistled and a small cart came
hurtling up the tracks toward them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7bc35dc8b9551f36cecb4f9183a4add2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2209">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-934a1744a549b68513afa75b9d08609d</data>
      <data key="v_content">They climbed in -- Hagrid with some
difficulty -- and were off.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-934a1744a549b68513afa75b9d08609d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2210">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0111902c8d11f8cafaab99658bd4bd00</data>
      <data key="v_content">At first they just hurtled through a maze of twisting passages.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0111902c8d11f8cafaab99658bd4bd00</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2211">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-678e5234bf472b7fd07056411d8b3afb</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Harry
tried to remember, left, right, right, left, middle fork, right, left,
but it was impossible.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-678e5234bf472b7fd07056411d8b3afb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2212">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b1405d69bc4c6382317e948813c6b0c8</data>
      <data key="v_content">The rattling cart seemed to know its own way,
because Griphook wasn&apos;t steering.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b1405d69bc4c6382317e948813c6b0c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2213">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bf40bf4dd00cd718ea1185e74d2ce101</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry&apos;s eyes stung as the cold air rushed past them, but he kept them
wide open.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bf40bf4dd00cd718ea1185e74d2ce101</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2214">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-46daed826a6483c93fb683e9416db875</data>
      <data key="v_content">hethoughthe,Once, he thought he saw a burst of fire at the end of a
passage and twisted around to see if it was a dragon, but too late - -
they plunged even deeper, passing an underground lake where huge
stalactites and stalagmites grew from the ceiling and floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-46daed826a6483c93fb683e9416db875</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2215">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-620f8a3e512f510cec8958b2f2f0c564</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Harry,I never know,&quot; Harry called to Hagrid over the noise of the cart,
&quot;what&apos;s the difference between a stalagmite and a stalactite?&quot;
&quot;Stalagmite&apos;s got an &apos;m&apos; in it,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-620f8a3e512f510cec8958b2f2f0c564</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2216">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7cf4367db4accbe88297c9c7518183b3</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;An&apos; don&apos; ask me questions
just now, I think I&apos;m gonna be sick.&quot;
He did look very green, and when the cart stopped at last beside a small
door in the passage wall, Hagrid got out and had to lean against the
wall to stop his knees from trembling.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7cf4367db4accbe88297c9c7518183b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2217">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b17a46b2aa5acc8d4f607f74acf27fd1</data>
      <data key="v_content">A lot of green smoke came billowing out, and
as it cleared, Harry gasped.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b17a46b2aa5acc8d4f607f74acf27fd1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2218">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-86310ab6df69831251e25f90eb5eaa56</data>
      <data key="v_content">Inside were mounds of gold coins.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-86310ab6df69831251e25f90eb5eaa56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2219">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0525b4f847c9c7da81b107c4327bd5e8</data>
      <data key="v_content">All Harry&apos;s -- it was incredible.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0525b4f847c9c7da81b107c4327bd5e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2220">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9eaaefe139fc2457c1a633d269f4d420</data>
      <data key="v_content">The Dursleys couldn&apos;t have known about
this or they&apos;d have had it from him faster than blinking.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9eaaefe139fc2457c1a633d269f4d420</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2221">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-13c68cd985eb8c35a95ef3be2fb5012e</data>
      <data key="v_content">How often had
they complained how much Harry cost them to keep? And all the time there
had been a small fortune belonging to him, buried deep under London.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-13c68cd985eb8c35a95ef3be2fb5012e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2222">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7b99d20529778acc9be53eb972e41027</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid helped Harry pile some of it into a bag.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7b99d20529778acc9be53eb972e41027</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2223">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9be666dcd2a423572fafe9a61c86f8c4</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;The gold ones are Galleons,&quot; he explained.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9be666dcd2a423572fafe9a61c86f8c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2224">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-70c3a7b705d1c07042ba88f5202fce2b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Seventeen silver Sickles to
59
a Galleon and twenty-nine Knuts to a Sickle, it&apos;s easy enough.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-70c3a7b705d1c07042ba88f5202fce2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2225">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-56804b33f3b4b2cdf741cd6d3d496699</data>
      <data key="v_content">thatshouldbe,Right,
that should be enough fer a couple o&apos; terms, we&apos;ll keep the rest safe
for yeh.&quot; He turned to Griphook.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-56804b33f3b4b2cdf741cd6d3d496699</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2226">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0d7a1dd4a698c7e959a1f540d17bc2ab</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Vault seven hundred and thirteen now,
please, and can we go more slowly?&quot;
&quot;One speed only,&quot; said Griphook.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0d7a1dd4a698c7e959a1f540d17bc2ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2227">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-54bdf4550a3eb401aa86effba533f1af</data>
      <data key="v_content">They were going even deeper now and gathering speed.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-54bdf4550a3eb401aa86effba533f1af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2228">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8b6696f1a4ce8221ac54781cfc071221</data>
      <data key="v_content">The air became
colder and colder as they hurtled round tight corners.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8b6696f1a4ce8221ac54781cfc071221</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2229">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fa03f3a7fcf068f085f1fc2d7ebdca11</data>
      <data key="v_content">They went
rattling over an underground ravine, and Harry leaned over the side to
try to see what was down at the dark bottom, but Hagrid groaned and
pulled him back by the scruff of his neck.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fa03f3a7fcf068f085f1fc2d7ebdca11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2230">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-13a0afc8d31f3598b1676d050abc41ef</data>
      <data key="v_content">Vault seven hundred and thirteen had no keyhole.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-13a0afc8d31f3598b1676d050abc41ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2231">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-10b426fb72780129655b94f03b8d6ee8</data>
      <data key="v_content">He stroked the door gently with
one of his long fingers and it simply melted away.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-10b426fb72780129655b94f03b8d6ee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2232">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a99e9378a17f2cfe92140aa60438d976</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;If anyone but a Gringotts goblin tried that, they&apos;d be sucked through
the door and trapped in there,&quot; said Griphook.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a99e9378a17f2cfe92140aa60438d976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2233">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8f5448016127a86a0ab3a6b3b36b05ce</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;How often do you check to see if anyone&apos;s inside?&quot; Harry asked.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8f5448016127a86a0ab3a6b3b36b05ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2234">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b796a9a86b5c9319d1128efdec72a847</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;About once every ten years,&quot; said Griphook with a rather nasty grin.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b796a9a86b5c9319d1128efdec72a847</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2235">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8c4fd8e6e6359ed3b8146372c177900f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Something really extraordinary had to be inside this top security vault,
Harry was sure, and he leaned forward eagerly, expecting to see fabulous
jewels at the very least -- but at first he thought it was empty.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8c4fd8e6e6359ed3b8146372c177900f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2236">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-94cbdb3d1af9426596158dd016045d12</data>
      <data key="v_content">Then
he noticed a grubby little package wrapped up in brown paper lying on
the floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-94cbdb3d1af9426596158dd016045d12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2237">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b465a61bf65196264863f7dd3a77e3fb</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid picked it up and tucked it deep inside his coat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b465a61bf65196264863f7dd3a77e3fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2238">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-04d2f3d53039935fa767f5b261562580</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry
longed to know what it was, but knew better than to ask.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-04d2f3d53039935fa767f5b261562580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2239">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fea7624081a18b2f4e1309e89b24f928</data>
      <data key="v_content">backin,&quot;Come on, back in this infernal cart, and don&apos;t talk to me on the way
back, it&apos;s best if I keep me mouth shut,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fea7624081a18b2f4e1309e89b24f928</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2240">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-74d8ef634236adf708298f547c8d38fc</data>
      <data key="v_content">One wild cart ride later they stood blinking in the sunlight outside
Gringotts.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-74d8ef634236adf708298f547c8d38fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2241">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-54bb51eb4153127224231847cd4eda31</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry didn&apos;t know where to run first now that he had a bag
full of money.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-54bb51eb4153127224231847cd4eda31</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2242">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-54c875c43f1cf2338eff61380c791422</data>
      <data key="v_content">He didn&apos;t have to know how many Galleons there were to a
pound to know that he was holding more money than he&apos;d had in his whole
life -- more money than even Dudley had ever had.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-54c875c43f1cf2338eff61380c791422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2243">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-065f2582e602ffe94cc76d59722dbf39</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Might as well get yer uniform,&quot; said Hagrid, nodding toward Madam
Malkin&apos;s Robes for All Occasions.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-065f2582e602ffe94cc76d59722dbf39</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2244">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bdb186be5447152ae6096948797c1bcd</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry,wouldyeh,&quot;Listen, Harry, would yeh mind if I
60
slipped off fer a pick-me-up in the Leaky Cauldron? I hate them
Gringotts carts.&quot; He did still look a bit sick, so Harry entered Madam
Malkin&apos;s shop alone, feeling nervous.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bdb186be5447152ae6096948797c1bcd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2245">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0d29f8df8a5c985891d27b5eca13a202</data>
      <data key="v_content">Madam Malkin was a squat, smiling witch dressed all in mauve.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0d29f8df8a5c985891d27b5eca13a202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2246">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2526774dfd2acd44972229a2c38a8c0a</data>
      <data key="v_content">clear?&quot;shesaid,,&quot;Hogwarts, clear?&quot; she said, when Harry started to speak.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2526774dfd2acd44972229a2c38a8c0a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2247">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0e70e3be5067614e6ec633ec05c2d452</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Got the lot
here -- another young man being fitted up just now, in fact.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0e70e3be5067614e6ec633ec05c2d452</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2248">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0dd78e422b658b319370fa017c62c851</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;
In the back of the shop, a boy with a pale, pointed face was standing on
a footstool while a second witch pinned up his long black robes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0dd78e422b658b319370fa017c62c851</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2249">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-40cf554c9f3b6f007e7108046d84521d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Madam
Malkin stood Harry on a stool next to him) slipped a long robe over his
head, and began to pin it to the right length.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-40cf554c9f3b6f007e7108046d84521d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2250">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-36d3448239496e92dc0b460dd50b9d27</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidtheboy,,&quot;Hello,&quot; said the boy, &quot;Hogwarts, too?&quot;
&quot;Yes,&quot; said Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-36d3448239496e92dc0b460dd50b9d27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2251">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f6d0eb37f3e9de0609f75a2de0713ed2</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;My father&apos;s next door buying my books and mother&apos;s up the street
looking at wands,&quot; said the boy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f6d0eb37f3e9de0609f75a2de0713ed2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2252">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cbc554c9b6c5ec07e59d1faaafd80cb4</data>
      <data key="v_content">,He had a bored, drawling voice.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cbc554c9b6c5ec07e59d1faaafd80cb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2253">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d27b00c846f3b42edfd2e23ebb8de779</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Then
I&apos;m going to drag them off to took at racing brooms.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d27b00c846f3b42edfd2e23ebb8de779</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2254">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b72baefe42fc98b69e58a32941b39525</data>
      <data key="v_content">I don&apos;t see why
first years can&apos;t have their own.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b72baefe42fc98b69e58a32941b39525</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2255">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-15e0097d438637cecacc7b793e2cdb04</data>
      <data key="v_content">I think I&apos;ll bully father into getting
me one and I&apos;ll smuggle it in somehow.&quot;
Harry was strongly reminded of Dudley.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-15e0097d438637cecacc7b793e2cdb04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2256">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-49385e6234c0712699dba363f0f14e5c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Have you got your own broom?&quot; the boy went on.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-49385e6234c0712699dba363f0f14e5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2257">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-89b9470cabaad36d423c6e6bd9402f6f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Play Quidditch at all?&quot;
&quot;No,&quot; Harry said again, wondering what on earth Quidditch could be.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-89b9470cabaad36d423c6e6bd9402f6f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2258">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-06434bc7544d7025ec436a7f05b855f4</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I do -- Father says it&apos;s a crime if I&apos;m not picked to play for my
house, and I must say, I agree.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-06434bc7544d7025ec436a7f05b855f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2259">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f61142d94a22be59fee24f7f744b8aa6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Know what house you&apos;ll be in yet?&quot;
&quot;No,&quot; said Harry, feeling more stupid by the minute.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f61142d94a22be59fee24f7f744b8aa6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2260">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9b1ee410b6c31b88b461cc5c979bf8de</data>
      <data key="v_content">noonereally,&quot;Well, no one really knows until they get there, do they, but I know
I&apos;ll be in Slytherin, all our family have been -- imagine being in
Hufflepuff, I think I&apos;d leave, wouldn&apos;t you?&quot; &quot;Mmm,&quot; said Harry, wishing
he could say something a bit more interesting.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9b1ee410b6c31b88b461cc5c979bf8de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2261">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ff585dd6a918aaca3b701ff45b7e6f56</data>
      <data key="v_content">look,61
&quot;I say, look at that man!&quot; said the boy suddenly, nodding toward the
front window.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ff585dd6a918aaca3b701ff45b7e6f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2262">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-90c8cfaed3d2d7f580efabd3f1a175e8</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Hagrid was standing there, grinning at Harry and pointing
at two large ice creams to show he couldn&apos;t come in.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-90c8cfaed3d2d7f580efabd3f1a175e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2263">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-47d3b3b0006534879d81d5a0ce0277ba</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidHarry,,&quot;That&apos;s Hagrid,&quot; said Harry, pleased to know something the boy didn&apos;t.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-47d3b3b0006534879d81d5a0ce0277ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2264">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e49fcc20bc0644dd7bf7bae70acf1090</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;He works at Hogwarts.&quot;
&quot;Oh,&quot; said the boy, &quot;I&apos;ve heard of him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e49fcc20bc0644dd7bf7bae70acf1090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2265">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-da3feed7eab2230677dc245120b9cb2a</data>
      <data key="v_content">He&apos;s a sort of servant, isn&apos;t
he?&quot;
&quot;He&apos;s the gamekeeper,&quot; said Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-da3feed7eab2230677dc245120b9cb2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2266">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ef236b8bd49eca5b889b0e09bb468f1c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was liking the boy less and less
every second.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ef236b8bd49eca5b889b0e09bb468f1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2267">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-83da90f9e6bbb350a72caa144522c81f</data>
      <data key="v_content">I heard he&apos;s a sort of savage -- lives in a hut on the
school grounds and every now and then he gets drunk, tries to do magic,
and ends up setting fire to his bed.&quot;
&quot;I think he&apos;s brilliant,&quot; said Harry coldly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-83da90f9e6bbb350a72caa144522c81f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2268">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ad15979c5179d1e1f7e19a7047cf4a69</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Do you?&quot; said the boy, with a slight sneer.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ad15979c5179d1e1f7e19a7047cf4a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2269">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0efca14885989d463c28275fbf7a66ea</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Why is he with you? Where
are your parents?&quot;
&quot;They&apos;re dead,&quot; said Harry shortly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0efca14885989d463c28275fbf7a66ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2270">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fa6cca9111544dce8c3d6d97dcadaecd</data>
      <data key="v_content">He didn&apos;t feel much like going into
the matter with this boy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fa6cca9111544dce8c3d6d97dcadaecd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2271">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-78ab114e71f09281f2ec0ef7f5d21510</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But they were
our kind, weren&apos;t they?&quot;
&quot;They were a witch and wizard, if that&apos;s what you mean.&quot;
&quot;I really don&apos;t think they should let the other sort in, do you? They&apos;re
just not the same, they&apos;ve never been brought up to know our ways.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-78ab114e71f09281f2ec0ef7f5d21510</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2272">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ba1f068687d81eee0c57ff4ff2a73c08</data>
      <data key="v_content">Some
of them have never even heard of Hogwarts until they get the letter,
imagine.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ba1f068687d81eee0c57ff4ff2a73c08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2273">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a59af84f8252e30702988dbd22ed60f7</data>
      <data key="v_content">I think they should keep it in the old wizarding families.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a59af84f8252e30702988dbd22ed60f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2274">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-96c4a6e5ca49001aa5fef84ba2ebe3a4</data>
      <data key="v_content">anyway?&quot;,What&apos;s your surname, anyway?&quot;
But before Harry could answer, Madam Malkin said, &quot;That&apos;s you done, my
dear,&quot; and Harry, not sorry for an excuse to stop talking to the boy,
hopped down from the footstool.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-96c4a6e5ca49001aa5fef84ba2ebe3a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2275">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bc8a69e4fbc972f67935f6f2f557390d</data>
      <data key="v_content">I&apos;llseeyou,&quot;Well, I&apos;ll see you at Hogwarts, I suppose,&quot; said the drawling boy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bc8a69e4fbc972f67935f6f2f557390d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2276">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-068e7e26a446ccee8178592ad19e1cf2</data>
      <data key="v_content">62
Harry was rather quiet as he ate the ice cream Hagrid had bought him
(chocolate and raspberry with chopped nuts).</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-068e7e26a446ccee8178592ad19e1cf2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2277">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8bf0a0842eac0e5883da0498ae97c505</data>
      <data key="v_content">They stopped to buy parchment and quills.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8bf0a0842eac0e5883da0498ae97c505</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2278">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d9c131fc1975f15929e317dfb13d353c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry
cheered up a bit when he found a bottle of ink that changed color as you
wrote.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d9c131fc1975f15929e317dfb13d353c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2279">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-986b212cf506353a2f571dbcfb6f21a0</data>
      <data key="v_content">When they had left the shop, he said, &quot;Hagrid, what&apos;s Quidditch?&quot;
&quot;Blimey, Harry, I keep forgettin&apos; how little yeh know -- not knowin&apos;
about Quidditch!&quot;
&quot;Don&apos;t make me feel worse,&quot; said Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-986b212cf506353a2f571dbcfb6f21a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2280">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-581b157e4081690a0a1281af049b44d9</data>
      <data key="v_content">He told Hagrid about the pate
boy in Madam Malkin&apos;s.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-581b157e4081690a0a1281af049b44d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2281">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3dce05db2548e42578cc4fe5cd67af43</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;--and he said people from Muggle families shouldn&apos;t even be allowed
in.&quot;
&quot;Yer not from a Muggle family.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3dce05db2548e42578cc4fe5cd67af43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2282">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0d56ea7b03edd476961e86600062356f</data>
      <data key="v_content">If he&apos;d known who yeh were -- he&apos;s grown
up knowin&apos; yer name if his parents are wizardin&apos; folk.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0d56ea7b03edd476961e86600062356f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2283">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3e86c01775a4d566d4c2937ffc34b30d</data>
      <data key="v_content">You saw what
everyone in the Leaky Cauldron was like when they saw yeh.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3e86c01775a4d566d4c2937ffc34b30d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2284">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-512d167ec16f840c5ae2430422ecbb70</data>
      <data key="v_content">whatdoeshe,Anyway, what
does he know about it, some o&apos; the best I ever saw were the only ones
with magic in &apos;em in a long line 0&apos; Muggles -- look at yer mum! Look
what she had fer a sister!&quot;
&quot;So what is Quidditch?&quot;
&quot;It&apos;s our sport.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-512d167ec16f840c5ae2430422ecbb70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2285">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b65eddf2c215675184ad26d53885aeec</data>
      <data key="v_content">It&apos;s like -- like soccer in the Muggle
world -- everyone follows Quidditch -- played up in the air on
broomsticks and there&apos;s four balls -- sorta hard ter explain the rules.&quot;
&quot;And what are Slytherin and Hufflepuff?&quot;
&quot;School houses.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b65eddf2c215675184ad26d53885aeec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2286">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ab8dea392adcdee7804c28f76dd1fdac</data>
      <data key="v_content">Everyone says Hufflepuff are a lot o&apos;
duffers, but --&quot;
&quot;I bet I&apos;m in Hufflepuff&quot; said Harry gloomily.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ab8dea392adcdee7804c28f76dd1fdac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2287">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-def3a4db8a1929928fea98bfbde057b3</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;Better Hufflepuff than Slytherin,&quot; said Hagrid darkly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-def3a4db8a1929928fea98bfbde057b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2288">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-68a1faeea147f03245d21973eaa18dc7</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;There&apos;s not a
single witch or wizard who went bad who wasn&apos;t in Slytherin.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-68a1faeea147f03245d21973eaa18dc7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2289">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-70d8ea7ecfc7f88e42b630d1ad5a4ca2</data>
      <data key="v_content">,You-Know-Who was one.&quot;
&quot;Vol-, sorry - You-Know-Who was at Hogwarts?&quot;
63
&quot;Years an&apos; years ago,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-70d8ea7ecfc7f88e42b630d1ad5a4ca2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2290">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8f49428e8ec225f9421791a312436a13</data>
      <data key="v_content">They bought Harry&apos;s school books in a shop called Flourish and Blotts
where the shelves were stacked to the ceiling with books as large as
paving stones bound in leather; books the size of postage stamps in
covers of silk; books full of peculiar symbols and a few books with
nothing in them at all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8f49428e8ec225f9421791a312436a13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2291">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f0683fb2ee46f34a4ba6b1c71b28e3d2</data>
      <data key="v_content">whonever,Even Dudley, who never read anything, would have
been wild to get his hands on some of these.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f0683fb2ee46f34a4ba6b1c71b28e3d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2292">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c36af22ce39a1b01ae143f486baa46d4</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid almost had to drag
Harry away from Curses and Countercurses (Bewitch Your Friends and
Befuddle Your Enemies with the Latest Revenges: Hair Loss, Jelly-Legs,
Tongue- Tying and Much, Much More) by Professor Vindictus Viridian.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c36af22ce39a1b01ae143f486baa46d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2293">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e87c4ce614522bbf0789eaf1e2468695</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I was trying to find out how to curse Dudley.&quot;
&quot;I&apos;m not sayin&apos; that&apos;s not a good idea, but yer not ter use magic in the
Muggle world except in very special circumstances,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e87c4ce614522bbf0789eaf1e2468695</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2294">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-63da1a3a2e129ca69ab800d5a5dd097a</data>
      <data key="v_content">yehcouldn&apos;,&quot;An&apos;
anyway, yeh couldn&apos; work any of them curses yet, yeh&apos;ll need a lot more
study before yeh get ter that level.&quot;
Hagrid wouldn&apos;t let Harry buy a solid gold cauldron, either (&quot;It says
pewter on yer list&quot;), but they got a nice set of scales for weighing
potion ingredients and a collapsible brass telescope.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-63da1a3a2e129ca69ab800d5a5dd097a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2295">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f6d9bd2ef316b232bdf877963d1a3edb</data>
      <data key="v_content">Then they visited
the Apothecary, which was fascinating enough to make up for its horrible
smell, a mixture of bad eggs and rotted cabbages.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f6d9bd2ef316b232bdf877963d1a3edb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2296">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5c44cefed73e41de3a6a1dff4d4c7b9e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Barrels of slimy stuff
stood on the floor; jars of herbs, dried roots, and bright powders lined
the walls; bundles of feathers, strings of fangs, and snarled claws hung
from the ceiling.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5c44cefed73e41de3a6a1dff4d4c7b9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2297">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7f627bcbc79362cabb65761e85866466</data>
      <data key="v_content">While Hagrid asked the man behind the counter for a
supply of some basic potion ingredients for Harry, Harry himself
examined silver unicorn horns at twenty-one Galleons each and minuscule,
glittery-black beetle eyes (five Knuts a scoop).</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7f627bcbc79362cabb65761e85866466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2298">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cceba2a8d5b3408c1c8a646478bbde99</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid,Outside the Apothecary, Hagrid checked Harry&apos;s list again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cceba2a8d5b3408c1c8a646478bbde99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2299">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7260350bdfaabae906c65ce6e2c31a70</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Just yer wand left - A yeah, an&apos; I still haven&apos;t got yeh a birthday
present.&quot;
Harry felt himself go red.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7260350bdfaabae906c65ce6e2c31a70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2300">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ca2584463383ad64f0aca06b92d0a8ea</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You don&apos;t have to --&quot;
&quot;I know I don&apos;t have to.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ca2584463383ad64f0aca06b92d0a8ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2301">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fbe6c4fcf429ff55e3e54ba15f3f4c02</data>
      <data key="v_content">I&apos;ll,Tell yeh what, I&apos;ll get yer animal.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fbe6c4fcf429ff55e3e54ba15f3f4c02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2302">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fc991aef536a647e14a9256742a03716</data>
      <data key="v_content">toads,Not a toad,
toads went outta fashion years ago, yeh&apos;d be laughed at - an&apos; I don&apos;
like cats, they make me sneeze.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fc991aef536a647e14a9256742a03716</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2303">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f5dffaac0e82c15e7cabe24045ba33b6</data>
      <data key="v_content">All the kids want
64
owls, they&apos;re dead useful, carry yer mail an&apos; everythin&apos;.&quot;
Twenty minutes later, they left Eeylops Owl Emporium, which had been
dark and full of rustling and flickering, jewel-bright eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f5dffaac0e82c15e7cabe24045ba33b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2304">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-55027ad74829db777ba3bfb76e4d97f7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry now
carried a large cage that held a beautiful snowy owl, fast asleep with
her head under her wing.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-55027ad74829db777ba3bfb76e4d97f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2305">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-48c0dbb3dd675910ba15a84045957ee8</data>
      <data key="v_content">He couldn&apos;t stop stammering his thanks,
sounding just like Professor Quirrell.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-48c0dbb3dd675910ba15a84045957ee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2306">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6fffec263d04f8f8a650bf780b77a1e7</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;said,&quot;Don&apos; mention it,&quot; said Hagrid gruffly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6fffec263d04f8f8a650bf780b77a1e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2307">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-efccbc5ff60c48a14e58c36fa280a068</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Don&apos; expect you&apos;ve had a lotta
presents from them Dursleys.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-efccbc5ff60c48a14e58c36fa280a068</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2308">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-88ee4c22605d76861c00633af3a0d239</data>
      <data key="v_content">Just Ollivanders left now - only place fer
wands, Ollivanders, and yeh gotta have the best wand.&quot;
A magic wand...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-88ee4c22605d76861c00633af3a0d239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2309">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5009bf7131265e017a52822726a8d314</data>
      <data key="v_content">this was what Harry had been really looking forward to.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5009bf7131265e017a52822726a8d314</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2310">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-053edc4d139ec37a434a62631f34fb30</data>
      <data key="v_content">The last shop was narrow and shabby.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-053edc4d139ec37a434a62631f34fb30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2311">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bc8d18303e7d1d035b7f2dbafe71938d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Peeling gold letters over the door
read Ollivanders: Makers of Fine Wands since 382 B.C.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bc8d18303e7d1d035b7f2dbafe71938d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2312">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-157485e4c53c705bcf16f8044f784d7a</data>
      <data key="v_content">A single wand lay
on a faded purple cushion in the dusty window.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-157485e4c53c705bcf16f8044f784d7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2313">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e662a083764f95df343eb53201c9661e</data>
      <data key="v_content">A tinkling bell rang somewhere in the depths of the shop as they stepped
inside.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e662a083764f95df343eb53201c9661e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2314">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f8dcb473946ffc941124edb5454302e3</data>
      <data key="v_content">It was a tiny place, empty except for a single, spindly chair
that Hagrid sat on to wait.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f8dcb473946ffc941124edb5454302e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2315">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ca712210751fdec5705bba89e255179f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry felt strangely as though he had
entered a very strict library; he swallowed a lot of new questions that
had just occurred to him and looked instead at the thousands of narrow
boxes piled neatly right up to the ceiling.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ca712210751fdec5705bba89e255179f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2316">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e787e14102a7c0a50d51ac8bda0f9fe5</data>
      <data key="v_content">the,For some reason, the back of
his neck prickled.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e787e14102a7c0a50d51ac8bda0f9fe5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2317">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-26c3541f80d59a9b6fa74d95d605ea12</data>
      <data key="v_content">The very dust and silence in here seemed to tingle
with some secret magic.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-26c3541f80d59a9b6fa74d95d605ea12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2318">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b01bee448e0f20a93830a7a7324895be</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saida,&quot;Good afternoon,&quot; said a soft voice.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b01bee448e0f20a93830a7a7324895be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2319">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a63d545498834dd7a5014a51839e3223</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Hagrid must have
jumped, too, because there was a loud crunching noise and he got quickly
off the spindly chair.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a63d545498834dd7a5014a51839e3223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2320">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4ca3c056639bf4e0c5e2f9df69abc6bc</data>
      <data key="v_content">An old man was standing before them, his wide, pale eyes shining like
moons through the gloom of the shop.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4ca3c056639bf4e0c5e2f9df69abc6bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2321">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bbd666a4cf2a4e5255e6c40b21681806</data>
      <data key="v_content">I thought I&apos;d be seeing you soon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bbd666a4cf2a4e5255e6c40b21681806</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2322">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-11eac1ceb2c6caee300485fdb22acf10</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry Potter.&quot; It wasn&apos;t a question.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-11eac1ceb2c6caee300485fdb22acf10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2323">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6ebab80cf9b9e4f29a003f17ca5d6aa7</data>
      <data key="v_content">It
seems only yesterday she was in here herself, buying her first wand.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6ebab80cf9b9e4f29a003f17ca5d6aa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2324">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7eac9eebf46413aecf0c7a7408931ea3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ten
and a quarter inches long, swishy, made of willow.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7eac9eebf46413aecf0c7a7408931ea3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2325">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-de298e736618310a1615dcee8f88ca42</data>
      <data key="v_content">Nice wand for charm
work.&quot;
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-de298e736618310a1615dcee8f88ca42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2326">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b0c210eb5d13ef44bbcaadc8fd9d1e22</data>
      <data key="v_content">Those
65
silvery eyes were a bit creepy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b0c210eb5d13ef44bbcaadc8fd9d1e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2327">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d3c774901352033f9a9bee6f2ffb9e97</data>
      <data key="v_content">onthe,&quot;Your father, on the other hand, favored a mahogany wand.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d3c774901352033f9a9bee6f2ffb9e97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2328">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-03cd172169819cd52978885692812e14</data>
      <data key="v_content">A little more power and excellent for transfiguration.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-03cd172169819cd52978885692812e14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2329">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e22884a047d6b81d00c485f05e78f6fb</data>
      <data key="v_content">Isayyour,Well, I
say your father favored it -- it&apos;s really the wand that chooses the
wizard, of course.&quot;
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e22884a047d6b81d00c485f05e78f6fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2330">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-747b3ffdf9b8728cccaec65cbcb69545</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ollivander had come so close that he and Harry were almost nose to
nose.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-747b3ffdf9b8728cccaec65cbcb69545</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2331">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-57334fd3a40fd0cd35ace3e920f52d42</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry could see himself reflected in those misty eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-57334fd3a40fd0cd35ace3e920f52d42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2332">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-eb5fc0725788ebf21b0cdc008b6e29f3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ollivander touched the lightning scar on Harry&apos;s forehead with a
long, white finger.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-eb5fc0725788ebf21b0cdc008b6e29f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2333">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a3b5a44033f5164a2a4089a48afa1a35</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I&apos;m sorry to say I sold the wand that did it,&quot; he said softly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a3b5a44033f5164a2a4089a48afa1a35</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2334">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8d34aa7a3d283a1aa74caa4185d0c9e5</data>
      <data key="v_content">verypowerful,,Powerful wand, very powerful, and in
the wrong hands...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8d34aa7a3d283a1aa74caa4185d0c9e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2335">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-78d48866c5c156f1657976899125b87d</data>
      <data key="v_content">ifI&apos;dknown,well, if I&apos;d known what that wand was going out into
the world to do....&quot;
He shook his head and then, to Harry&apos;s relief, spotted Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-78d48866c5c156f1657976899125b87d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2336">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-203c36811b2f2f56fd4e9c8c91455049</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Rubeus! Rubeus Hagrid! How nice to see you again....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-203c36811b2f2f56fd4e9c8c91455049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2337">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cc7c667fd709c3aabf7b8a466b4d1cd1</data>
      <data key="v_content">sixteeninches,rather,Oak, sixteen
inches, rather bendy, wasn&apos;t it?&quot;
&quot;It was, sir, yes,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cc7c667fd709c3aabf7b8a466b4d1cd1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2338">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d5e4780affc3490a18de37d1b15645ae</data>
      <data key="v_content">But I suppose they snapped it in half when you got
expelled?&quot; said Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d5e4780affc3490a18de37d1b15645ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2339">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-78bfa1093055c3e97e1e85c64c75144b</data>
      <data key="v_content">they,&quot;Er -- yes, they did, yes,&quot; said Hagrid, shuffling his feet.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-78bfa1093055c3e97e1e85c64c75144b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2340">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c824ff14c210d0b6a050639278c1cc6b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I&apos;ve still
got the pieces, though,&quot; he added brightly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c824ff14c210d0b6a050639278c1cc6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2341">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9e233d6ac68f8685336d28db57df5810</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;But you don&apos;t use them?&quot; said Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9e233d6ac68f8685336d28db57df5810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2342">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-329ffafc7f6f7a55e2ef5ad155c1e8a4</data>
      <data key="v_content">no,sit,&quot;said,&quot;Oh, no, sit,&quot; said Hagrid quickly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-329ffafc7f6f7a55e2ef5ad155c1e8a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2343">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5dc1f9b40b85a8862fe870a5398942bd</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry noticed he gripped his pink
umbrella very tightly as he spoke.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5dc1f9b40b85a8862fe870a5398942bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2344">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-39f7ad70a0773ca2cbcc46b5088580ca</data>
      <data key="v_content">givingHagrida,Ollivander, giving Hagrid a piercing look.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-39f7ad70a0773ca2cbcc46b5088580ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2345">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fe839fc16b006708ac771018ffbff321</data>
      <data key="v_content">Let me see.&quot; He pulled a long tape measure with silver
markings out of his pocket.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fe839fc16b006708ac771018ffbff321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2346">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1efb4cea584a699c0499ce7000bb8fd1</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Which is your wand arm?&quot;
&quot;Er -- well, I&apos;m right-handed,&quot; said Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1efb4cea584a699c0499ce7000bb8fd1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2347">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0c33ee98c6078248c262a5dcb3ea04df</data>
      <data key="v_content">That&apos;s it.&quot; He measured Harry from shoulder to
finger, then wrist to elbow, shoulder to floor, knee to armpit and round
his head.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0c33ee98c6078248c262a5dcb3ea04df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2348">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5fc408f783bc3db5c9be62b99193d307</data>
      <data key="v_content">he,As he measured, he said, &quot;Every Ollivander wand has a core of
a powerful magical substance, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5fc408f783bc3db5c9be62b99193d307</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2349">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8d465e7f4864c0c44ec48a9e585d0025</data>
      <data key="v_content">,We use unicorn hairs, phoenix
tail feathers, and the heartstrings of dragons.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8d465e7f4864c0c44ec48a9e585d0025</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2350">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-646c478b9fdb3c631efce9e0065d05f5</data>
      <data key="v_content">No two Ollivander wands
are the same, just as no two unicorns, dragons, or phoenixes are quite
the same.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-646c478b9fdb3c631efce9e0065d05f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2351">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-364a931586dd98b7228802da61441147</data>
      <data key="v_content">you,And of course, you will never get such good results with
another wizard&apos;s wand.&quot;
Harry suddenly realized that the tape measure, which was measuring
between his nostrils, was doing this on its own.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-364a931586dd98b7228802da61441147</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2352">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c58284657fa8eb7df72d11265877ac8a</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ollivander was
flitting around the shelves, taking down boxes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c58284657fa8eb7df72d11265877ac8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2353">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b5655d4960ae8870aecd2557e52cdb48</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;he,&quot;That will do,&quot; he said, and the tape measure crumpled into a heap on
the floor.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b5655d4960ae8870aecd2557e52cdb48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2354">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-47d491eade8390d3496a9668aef33839</data>
      <data key="v_content">just take it and give it a
wave.&quot;
Harry took the wand and (feeling foolish) waved it around a bit, but Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-47d491eade8390d3496a9668aef33839</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2355">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1cf7f5eba2dcf2abe0ea49be45d9c170</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ollivander snatched it out of his hand almost at once.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1cf7f5eba2dcf2abe0ea49be45d9c170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2356">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d4905ca84eb979616a80cfe993dc2106</data>
      <data key="v_content">Try --&quot;
Harry tried -- but he had hardly raised the wand when it, too, was
snatched back by Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d4905ca84eb979616a80cfe993dc2106</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2357">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c9b8d0eb9747e456eb1ae2888d1860e3</data>
      <data key="v_content">no-here,ebony,&quot;No, no -here, ebony and unicorn hair, eight and a half inches, springy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c9b8d0eb9747e456eb1ae2888d1860e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2358">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-97cb4c398f1ac8be1b7a815d33ea1e83</data>
      <data key="v_content">goon,,Go on, go on, try it out.&quot;
Harry tried.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-97cb4c398f1ac8be1b7a815d33ea1e83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2359">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-42d0d107b17d952cda05d8c90ea4a3a7</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had no idea what Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-42d0d107b17d952cda05d8c90ea4a3a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2360">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1650a06dc494e498567ee6c00eac8f0b</data>
      <data key="v_content">The pile of tried wands was mounting higher and higher on the
spindly chair, but the more wands Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1650a06dc494e498567ee6c00eac8f0b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2361">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f4b08dfd01b2e193c61d73ecfa672068</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ollivander pulled from the
shelves, the happier he seemed to become.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f4b08dfd01b2e193c61d73ecfa672068</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2362">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-197098e2b66f5cce62aec82239161739</data>
      <data key="v_content">eh?Not,&quot;Tricky customer, eh? Not to worry, we&apos;ll find the perfect match here
somewhere -- I wonder, now - - yes, why not -- unusual combination --
holly and phoenix feather, eleven inches, nice and supple.&quot;
Harry took the wand.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-197098e2b66f5cce62aec82239161739</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2363">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a371ddbadbdf68bdd80e3d15cae0fe89</data>
      <data key="v_content">He felt a sudden warmth in his fingers.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a371ddbadbdf68bdd80e3d15cae0fe89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2364">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-87d5dfdb46b2b38cde4c0f64f820c3d6</data>
      <data key="v_content">He raised
the wand above his head, brought it swishing down through the dusty air
and a stream of red and gold sparks shot from the end like a firework,
throwing dancing spots of light on to the walls.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-87d5dfdb46b2b38cde4c0f64f820c3d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2365">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-62362b850f594278193c7ef304a29ad9</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid whooped and
67
clapped and Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-62362b850f594278193c7ef304a29ad9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2366">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-565bb3af3d6c0772005e80413245410b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Oh,bravo!,Ollivander cried, &quot;Oh, bravo! Yes, indeed, oh, very
good.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-565bb3af3d6c0772005e80413245410b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2367">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-27d1d42bea22513762aa0b1b6ef920c9</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;
He put Harry&apos;s wand back into its box and wrapped it in brown paper,
still muttering, &quot;Curious...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-27d1d42bea22513762aa0b1b6ef920c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2368">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3a0a15b0c04b7c1e4d24e18f310bf10b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidHarry,&quot;but,&quot;Sorry,&quot; said Harry, &quot;but what&apos;s curious?&quot;
Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3a0a15b0c04b7c1e4d24e18f310bf10b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2369">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-43369be9f4bc16f02f55b100b23f5afc</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ollivander fixed Harry with his pale stare.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-43369be9f4bc16f02f55b100b23f5afc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2370">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1de7e955406d2ca19baebfb265c82f44</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I remember every wand I&apos;ve ever sold, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1de7e955406d2ca19baebfb265c82f44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2371">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7ac0f409dc59464267a0c5ff17ca3a12</data>
      <data key="v_content">It
so happens that the phoenix whose tail feather is in your wand, gave
another feather -- just one other.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7ac0f409dc59464267a0c5ff17ca3a12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2372">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ed925c486ec0f4ca65e2aad37b9ae806</data>
      <data key="v_content">It is very curious indeed that you
should be destined for this wand when its brother why, its brother gave
you that scar.&quot;
Harry swallowed.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ed925c486ec0f4ca65e2aad37b9ae806</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2373">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-011b21c2bd2edc66d2a5726af87769b7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Curious indeed how these things
happen.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-011b21c2bd2edc66d2a5726af87769b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2374">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-63b59d430d4ba6d085ded98d8c091f08</data>
      <data key="v_content">The wand chooses the wizard, remember....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-63b59d430d4ba6d085ded98d8c091f08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2375">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-22050fc5944b6c31bdedaceea149f057</data>
      <data key="v_content">I think we must expect
great things from you, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-22050fc5944b6c31bdedaceea149f057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2376">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-143b5be68c942b2246115b22332e4f46</data>
      <data key="v_content">He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named,After all, He-
Who-Must-Not-Be-Named did great things -- terrible, yes, but great.&quot;
Harry shivered.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-143b5be68c942b2246115b22332e4f46</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2377">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8ea4455a7e3495413170f14e5a4e23cb</data>
      <data key="v_content">He wasn&apos;t sure he liked Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8ea4455a7e3495413170f14e5a4e23cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2378">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6dae0b1ac8ecb4dc3798952e122a14d5</data>
      <data key="v_content">He paid
seven gold Galleons for his wand, and Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6dae0b1ac8ecb4dc3798952e122a14d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2379">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fd0ffd1d8f9fbd907351bd839d2fd03e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ollivander bowed them from his
shop.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fd0ffd1d8f9fbd907351bd839d2fd03e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2380">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e2588081400cf08efd030ce0ff340843</data>
      <data key="v_content">The late afternoon sun hung low in the sky as Harry and Hagrid made
their way back down Diagon Alley, back through the wall, back through
the Leaky Cauldron, now empty.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e2588081400cf08efd030ce0ff340843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2381">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d6da79e854ff1be732dce3acb13ee64c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry didn&apos;t speak at all as they walked
down the road; he didn&apos;t even notice how much people were gawking at
them on the Underground, laden as they were with all their funny-shaped
packages, with the snowy owl asleep in its cage on Harry&apos;s lap.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d6da79e854ff1be732dce3acb13ee64c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2382">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8cbb0eafd137ceb740bfedf7f6a4eb86</data>
      <data key="v_content">out,Up
another escalator, out into Paddington station; Harry only realized
where they were when Hagrid tapped him on the shoulder.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8cbb0eafd137ceb740bfedf7f6a4eb86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2383">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f25cfd178be0974baf1509ae8cd8bb9a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Got time fer a bite to eat before yer train leaves,&quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f25cfd178be0974baf1509ae8cd8bb9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2384">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ff53109dfdec211b5df94bfc169cd32a</data>
      <data key="v_content">He bought Harry a hamburger and they sat down on plastic seats to eat
them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ff53109dfdec211b5df94bfc169cd32a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2385">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c24546c6c741593c051454c201d4c9eb</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry?,&quot;You all right, Harry? Yer very quiet,&quot; said Hagrid.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c24546c6c741593c051454c201d4c9eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2386">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0c4f43893e88844bdd27b2b2f2729f34</data>
      <data key="v_content">68
Harry wasn&apos;t sure he could explain.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0c4f43893e88844bdd27b2b2f2729f34</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2387">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1c57f69b6ebd4b2a27f3cae68aa494f5</data>
      <data key="v_content">He&apos;d just had the best birthday of
his life -- and yet -- he chewed his hamburger, trying to find the
words.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1c57f69b6ebd4b2a27f3cae68aa494f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2388">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cc7bd7aab61c7995a632845d67a26532</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;Everyone thinks I&apos;m special,&quot; he said at last.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cc7bd7aab61c7995a632845d67a26532</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2389">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a043a47dee6ac508e1944f60e8e3f0a0</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;All those people in the
Leaky Cauldron, Professor Quirrell, Mr.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a043a47dee6ac508e1944f60e8e3f0a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2390">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0619b9800d33bbb2914681bbe9ea95ca</data>
      <data key="v_content">but I don&apos;t know
anything about magic at all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0619b9800d33bbb2914681bbe9ea95ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2391">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-058cff61e679c549d89df0d9a12276f6</data>
      <data key="v_content">How can they expect great things? I&apos;m
famous and I can&apos;t even remember what I&apos;m famous for.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-058cff61e679c549d89df0d9a12276f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2392">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3bbb55749930c10722fbfe7a83af8a29</data>
      <data key="v_content">I don&apos;t know what
happened when Vol-, sorry -- I mean, the night my parents died.&quot;
Hagrid leaned across the table.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3bbb55749930c10722fbfe7a83af8a29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2393">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6321ffe665c0cea96ec31bde6072def2</data>
      <data key="v_content">Behind the wild beard and eyebrows he
wore a very kind smile.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6321ffe665c0cea96ec31bde6072def2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2394">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3b5fdee133044da3a186243e52efbfb9</data>
      <data key="v_content">Everyone starts at the
beginning at Hogwarts, you&apos;ll be just fine.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3b5fdee133044da3a186243e52efbfb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2395">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c4b0c20f1eabc247875dc898844a5741</data>
      <data key="v_content">,Yeh&apos;ve been singled out, an&apos; that&apos;s always hard.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c4b0c20f1eabc247875dc898844a5741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2396">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-746fab34e41c552c488d4df5e597b0e1</data>
      <data key="v_content">But yeh&apos;ll have a
great time at Hogwarts -- I did -- still do, &apos;smatter of fact.&quot;
Hagrid helped Harry on to the train that would take him back to the
Dursleys, then handed him an envelope.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-746fab34e41c552c488d4df5e597b0e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2397">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b5e1570d8d86704474b65820cab169fc</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Yer ticket fer Hogwarts, &quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b5e1570d8d86704474b65820cab169fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2398">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0917cf5483c888caec47b1fbf2e50258</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;First o&apos; September -- King&apos;s Cross
-- it&apos;s all on yer ticket.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0917cf5483c888caec47b1fbf2e50258</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2399">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d675c86c196b4b391a31523311509c30</data>
      <data key="v_content">Any problems with the Dursleys, send me a
letter with yer owl, she&apos;ll know where to find me....</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d675c86c196b4b391a31523311509c30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2400">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-badf6a3a45a7a4687bc811d7c564d401</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry.&quot;,See yeh soon,
Harry.&quot;
The train pulled out of the station.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-badf6a3a45a7a4687bc811d7c564d401</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2401">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-81a89c18e85006a106a6d3176fe3218f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry wanted to watch Hagrid until
he was out of sight; he rose in his seat and pressed his nose against
the window, but he blinked and Hagrid had gone.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-81a89c18e85006a106a6d3176fe3218f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2402">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-28ddd3e10b281616297bfa81868ad540</data>
      <data key="v_content">CHAPTER SIX
THE JOURNEY FROM PLATFORM NINE AND THREE-QUARTERS
Harry&apos;s last month with the Dursleys wasn&apos;t fun.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-28ddd3e10b281616297bfa81868ad540</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2403">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2b54c088454248b930e130193e1ae1d1</data>
      <data key="v_content">Dudleywasnow,True, Dudley was now so
scared of Harry he wouldn&apos;t stay in the same room, while Aunt Petunia
and Uncle Vernon didn&apos;t shut Harry in his cupboard, force him to do
anything, or shout at him -- in fact, they didn&apos;t speak to him at all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2b54c088454248b930e130193e1ae1d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2404">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-71a0a19f3543b55246c38a6c9df17ced</data>
      <data key="v_content">halffurious,,Half terrified, half furious, they acted as though any chair with Harry
in it were empty.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-71a0a19f3543b55246c38a6c9df17ced</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2405">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-05d6fbf18870b8101b6516562eeae05b</data>
      <data key="v_content">Although this was an improvement in many ways, it did
become a bit depressing after a while.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-05d6fbf18870b8101b6516562eeae05b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2406">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-da29897d08b25fa7ce5ceb7b4f33c1f9</data>
      <data key="v_content">69
Harry kept to his room, with his new owl for company.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-da29897d08b25fa7ce5ceb7b4f33c1f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2407">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f876c02ed063f52a5ed2d1144c2acb55</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had decided to
call her Hedwig, a name he had found in A History of Magic.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f876c02ed063f52a5ed2d1144c2acb55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2408">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a2fa9ba1be66270921a743f21be241af</data>
      <data key="v_content">His school
books were very interesting.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a2fa9ba1be66270921a743f21be241af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2409">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3a9dcb4665a9cdb394c320d6dcce7068</data>
      <data key="v_content">He lay on his bed reading late into the
night, Hedwig swooping in and out of the open window as she pleased.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3a9dcb4665a9cdb394c320d6dcce7068</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2410">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-94a10d877104e3f558d9319cb81d9479</data>
      <data key="v_content">It
was lucky that Aunt Petunia didn&apos;t come in to vacuum anymore, because
Hedwig kept bringing back dead mice.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-94a10d877104e3f558d9319cb81d9479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2411">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d6d4dda70b5a7783eced67310d516ee3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Every night before he went to
sleep, Harry ticked off another day on the piece of paper he had pinned
to the wall, counting down to September the first.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d6d4dda70b5a7783eced67310d516ee3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2412">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cd91bb5506670dd1a2ed84b108a30ef7</data>
      <data key="v_content">On the last day of August he thought he&apos;d better speak to his aunt and
uncle about getting to King&apos;s Cross station the next day, so he went
down to the living room where they were watching a quiz show on
television.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cd91bb5506670dd1a2ed84b108a30ef7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2413">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b6d0a46a59b043cdcdd256350cbeaa4a</data>
      <data key="v_content">He cleared his throat to let them know he was there, and
Dudley screamed and ran from the room.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b6d0a46a59b043cdcdd256350cbeaa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2414">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-256740b1c33cf31964f0d9579ff23922</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Er -- Uncle Vernon?&quot;
Uncle Vernon grunted to show he was listening.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-256740b1c33cf31964f0d9579ff23922</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2415">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-777d4671723960a7da5ac0d71d1093f0</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Er -- I need to be at King&apos;s Cross tomorrow to -- to go to Hogwarts.&quot;
Uncle Vernon grunted again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-777d4671723960a7da5ac0d71d1093f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2416">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bad77528f3e7a9de9ac94e5e301cbe50</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Would it be all right if you gave me a lift?&quot;
Grunt.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bad77528f3e7a9de9ac94e5e301cbe50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2417">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bcefb7d376055b5761f4638882d8ccc0</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Thank you.&quot;
He was about to go back upstairs when Uncle Vernon actually spoke.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bcefb7d376055b5761f4638882d8ccc0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2418">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-36efb9c80d7b24ffb00d809f04f08d7c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Funny way to get to a wizards&apos; school, the train.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-36efb9c80d7b24ffb00d809f04f08d7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2419">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7bcf4e13703240ca233992d3de87938e</data>
      <data key="v_content">Magic carpets all got
punctures, have they?&quot;
Harry didn&apos;t say anything.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7bcf4e13703240ca233992d3de87938e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2420">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-aaab366db144e01f7a445a48e5c09a14</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Where is this school, anyway?&quot;
&quot;I don&apos;t know,&quot; said Harry, realizing this for the first time.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-aaab366db144e01f7a445a48e5c09a14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2421">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e38233ad39928a535ac1480f92c5104b</data>
      <data key="v_content">He pulled
the ticket Hagrid had given him out of his pocket.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e38233ad39928a535ac1480f92c5104b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2422">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c16fbdbb52c383b79df42c3d14a9e026</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I just take the train from platform nine and three-quarters at eleven
o&apos;clock,&quot; he read.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c16fbdbb52c383b79df42c3d14a9e026</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2423">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b92d59f8a899ab92a56aba0b52b3b4b9</data>
      <data key="v_content">70
His aunt and uncle stared.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b92d59f8a899ab92a56aba0b52b3b4b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2424">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4cce1a3ac2dc8374a020be51678eb338</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Platform what?&quot;
&quot;Nine and three-quarters.&quot;
&quot;Don&apos;t talk rubbish,&quot; said Uncle Vernon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4cce1a3ac2dc8374a020be51678eb338</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2425">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9d6eb94a03cb8239df5d86bafec30b23</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;There is no platform nine and
three-quarters.&quot;
&quot;It&apos;s on my ticket.&quot;
&quot;Barking,&quot; said Uncle Vernon, &quot;howling mad, the lot of them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9d6eb94a03cb8239df5d86bafec30b23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2426">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-14526572932369a65eca55a7301cc694</data>
      <data key="v_content">we&apos;lltake,All right, we&apos;ll take you to King&apos;s Cross.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-14526572932369a65eca55a7301cc694</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2427">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f16a7208de32ff7c27431b4960054915</data>
      <data key="v_content">We&apos;re going up
to London tomorrow anyway, or I wouldn&apos;t bother.&quot;
&quot;Why are you going to London?&quot; Harry asked, trying to keep things
friendly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f16a7208de32ff7c27431b4960054915</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2428">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-312def0f9876c80f30680e3bfbdddb8a</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Taking Dudley to the hospital,&quot; growled Uncle Vernon.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-312def0f9876c80f30680e3bfbdddb8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2429">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5b8e8f0395585aadd03a17e26f24d5fc</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Got to have that
ruddy tail removed before he goes to Smeltings.&quot;
Harry woke at five o&apos;clock the next morning and was too excited and
nervous to go back to sleep.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5b8e8f0395585aadd03a17e26f24d5fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2430">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fd673af13cf0d28529f166b56d9b3a9a</data>
      <data key="v_content">He got up and pulled on his jeans because
he didn&apos;t want to walk into the station in his wizard&apos;s robes -- he&apos;d
change on the train.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fd673af13cf0d28529f166b56d9b3a9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2431">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dd4fa466b37bd517ee5bd54a858ead7c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He checked his Hogwarts list yet again to make sure
he had everything he needed, saw that Hedwig was shut safely in her
cage, and then paced the room, waiting for the Dursleys to get up.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dd4fa466b37bd517ee5bd54a858ead7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2432">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-99803e936a8f28fe8cbd274eb4587adf</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry&apos;s,Two
hours later, Harry&apos;s huge, heavy trunk had been loaded into the
Dursleys&apos; car, Aunt Petunia had talked Dudley into sitting next to
Harry, and they had set off.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-99803e936a8f28fe8cbd274eb4587adf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2433">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-bd29d0bbb2ad1e6a8e5b8445cd9aff8a</data>
      <data key="v_content">They reached King&apos;s Cross at half past ten.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-bd29d0bbb2ad1e6a8e5b8445cd9aff8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2434">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-31f3e5032fc7fa84d6520703856e8823</data>
      <data key="v_content">Uncle Vernon dumped Harry&apos;s
trunk onto a cart and wheeled it into the station for him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-31f3e5032fc7fa84d6520703856e8823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2435">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d0bca8a4508f2a3e8255f5133223d007</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry thought
this was strangely kind until Uncle Vernon stopped dead, facing the
platforms with a nasty grin on his face.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d0bca8a4508f2a3e8255f5133223d007</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2436">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ca3d1e20e4c7e5b5cfe441f390df0b4f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Your platform
should be somewhere in the middle, but they don&apos;t seem to have built it
yet, do they?&quot;
He was quite right, of course.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ca3d1e20e4c7e5b5cfe441f390df0b4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2437">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b7d34290d311e3e00fedf9dfaa2fc93f</data>
      <data key="v_content">There was a big plastic number nine over
one platform and a big plastic number ten over the one next to it, and
71
in the middle, nothing at all.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b7d34290d311e3e00fedf9dfaa2fc93f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2438">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2ea5f1db03cb78682c7ad35b6109a28e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;Have a good term,&quot; said Uncle Vernon with an even nastier smile.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2ea5f1db03cb78682c7ad35b6109a28e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2439">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-96839d4b06ad226af2e124afab8841bd</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry turned and saw the Dursleys drive away.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-96839d4b06ad226af2e124afab8841bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2440">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ce54962620f213a568ed8f34c60a53d4</data>
      <data key="v_content">All three of them were laughing.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ce54962620f213a568ed8f34c60a53d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2441">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2cbee5639305657c298d6c18d4e1301c</data>
      <data key="v_content">What on
earth was he going to do? He was starting to attract a lot of funny
looks, because of Hedwig.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2cbee5639305657c298d6c18d4e1301c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2442">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b006d4f8e4ed6c955f8d30fa4beb5ff2</data>
      <data key="v_content">He stopped a passing guard, but didn&apos;t dare mention platform nine and
three-quarters.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b006d4f8e4ed6c955f8d30fa4beb5ff2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2443">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8be4d55304e63e7f4a1c0101c057266c</data>
      <data key="v_content">The guard had never heard of Hogwarts and when Harry
couldn&apos;t even tell him what part of the country it was in, he started to
get annoyed, as though Harry was being stupid on purpose.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8be4d55304e63e7f4a1c0101c057266c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2444">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-65ed5b853b9baadf1df937a994824bd0</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harryasked,Getting
desperate, Harry asked for the train that left at eleven o&apos;clock, but
the guard said there wasn&apos;t one.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-65ed5b853b9baadf1df937a994824bd0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2445">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-5616abdbb3bbca4de09a364ceac278bf</data>
      <data key="v_content">In the end the guard strode away,
muttering about time wasters.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-5616abdbb3bbca4de09a364ceac278bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2446">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0a930062d64849b241f2608d2277cfbc</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry was now trying hard not to panic.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0a930062d64849b241f2608d2277cfbc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2447">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-7a5acd93e5e302d4cb30e5bbff51f23d</data>
      <data key="v_content">According to the large clock over the arrivals board, he had ten minutes
left to get on the train to Hogwarts and he had no idea how to do it; he
was stranded in the middle of a station with a trunk he could hardly
lift, a pocket full of wizard money, and a large owl.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-7a5acd93e5e302d4cb30e5bbff51f23d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2448">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2081c2f829dddbe43bf3c41e77800030</data>
      <data key="v_content">Hagrid must have forgotten to tell him something you had to do, like
tapping the third brick on the left to get into Diagon Alley.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2081c2f829dddbe43bf3c41e77800030</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2449">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1312f8fc3d53eef27aae58939b1c0f78</data>
      <data key="v_content">He
wondered if he should get out his wand and start tapping the ticket
inspector&apos;s stand between platforms nine and ten.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1312f8fc3d53eef27aae58939b1c0f78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2450">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-367463b220e47677a5056f661868843e</data>
      <data key="v_content">At that moment a group of people passed just behind him and he caught a
few words of what they were saying.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-367463b220e47677a5056f661868843e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2451">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cf256f248b5ad6e76e66933ad97e69b4</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;-- packed with Muggles, of course --&quot;
Harry swung round.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cf256f248b5ad6e76e66933ad97e69b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2452">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-126a5ab988637443d3073287e4cd932e</data>
      <data key="v_content">The speaker was a plump woman who was talking to four
boys, all with flaming red hair.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-126a5ab988637443d3073287e4cd932e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2453">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-37881411fd75322afae2bc1cdbbae900</data>
      <data key="v_content">Each of them was pushing a trunk like
Harry&apos;s in front of him -- and they had an owl.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-37881411fd75322afae2bc1cdbbae900</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2454">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d76c87cae460750b16688691c56d632c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harrypushed,Heart hammering, Harry pushed his cart after them.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d76c87cae460750b16688691c56d632c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2455">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e597929a76c4bcd89af045dc0a1369d9</data>
      <data key="v_content">They stopped and so
did he, just near enough to hear what they were saying.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e597929a76c4bcd89af045dc0a1369d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2456">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d7f080cfd0bd35d6799d071b07939dcd</data>
      <data key="v_content">what&apos;stheplatform,&quot;Now, what&apos;s the platform number?&quot; said the boys&apos; mother.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d7f080cfd0bd35d6799d071b07939dcd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2457">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d9d2c30fbd970528695faa40f974f738</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Nine and three-quarters!&quot; piped a small girl, also red-headed, who was
holding her hand, &quot;Mom, can&apos;t I go...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d9d2c30fbd970528695faa40f974f738</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2458">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cf0e1e6ca284b1aa7161a8a2f26ddcdf</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;
&quot;You&apos;re not old enough, Ginny, now be quiet.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cf0e1e6ca284b1aa7161a8a2f26ddcdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2459">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6875d0200d35953ac51208febe9cdf80</data>
      <data key="v_content">Percy,you,All right, Percy, you go
72
first.&quot;
What looked like the oldest boy marched toward platforms nine and ten.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6875d0200d35953ac51208febe9cdf80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2460">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-42371fcb1e61166e1c48ba3c2aeece9d</data>
      <data key="v_content">carefulnot,Harry watched, careful not to blink in case he missed it -- but just as
the boy reached the dividing barrier between the two platforms, a large
crowd of tourists came swarming in front of him and by the time the last
backpack had cleared away, the boy had vanished.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-42371fcb1e61166e1c48ba3c2aeece9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2461">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f540719b24891072257e4ec99cccf8d1</data>
      <data key="v_content">younext,&quot;the,&quot;Fred, you next,&quot; the plump woman said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f540719b24891072257e4ec99cccf8d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2462">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d34637d2bf56c552f96ef95000b14744</data>
      <data key="v_content">I&apos;m,&quot;I&apos;m not Fred, I&apos;m George,&quot; said the boy.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d34637d2bf56c552f96ef95000b14744</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2463">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6f7cc8aa3964b90c4ed508237fc8d3ce</data>
      <data key="v_content">woman,youcall,&quot;Honestly, woman, you call
yourself our mother? CarA you tell I&apos;m George?&quot;
&quot;Sorry, George, dear.&quot;
&quot;Only joking, I am Fred,&quot; said the boy, and off he went.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6f7cc8aa3964b90c4ed508237fc8d3ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2464">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f9db1e650e62704998aac3d91265776d</data>
      <data key="v_content">His twin called
after him to hurry up, and he must have done so, because a second later,
he had gone -- but how had he done it?
Now the third brother was walking briskly toward the barrier he was
almost there -- and then, quite suddenly, he wasn&apos;t anywhere.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f9db1e650e62704998aac3d91265776d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2465">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ecf0d97b6ce4c4586c08e68a77a01bb9</data>
      <data key="v_content">There was nothing else for it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ecf0d97b6ce4c4586c08e68a77a01bb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2466">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-a4c30340ab46abbd530499ef54f4da10</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Harrysaid,&quot;Excuse me,&quot; Harry said to the plump woman.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-a4c30340ab46abbd530499ef54f4da10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2467">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6efa67efeb700d12c4222657157de057</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;First time at Hogwarts? Ron&apos;s new, too.&quot;
She pointed at the last and youngest of her sons.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6efa67efeb700d12c4222657157de057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2468">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-62eae94493e1462deae99958aacc1bae</data>
      <data key="v_content">thin,,He was tall, thin, and
gangling, with freckles, big hands and feet, and a long nose.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-62eae94493e1462deae99958aacc1bae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2469">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4a4bbd80cbe0b73702bcf098d7b104b7</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;The thing is -- the thing is, I don&apos;t know how to
--&quot;
&quot;How to get onto the platform?&quot; she said kindly, and Harry nodded.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4a4bbd80cbe0b73702bcf098d7b104b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2470">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ff36e926be18191fdf2850e99513808c</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;All you have to do is walk straight at the
barrier between platforms nine and ten.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ff36e926be18191fdf2850e99513808c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2471">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2b0b1e11dc486b95c3ac39cbee2aa9dc</data>
      <data key="v_content">Don&apos;t stop and don&apos;t be scared
you&apos;ll crash into it, that&apos;s very important.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2b0b1e11dc486b95c3ac39cbee2aa9dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2472">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-10912816b267f504a72ab397ad07fea7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Best do it at a bit of a
run if you&apos;re nervous.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-10912816b267f504a72ab397ad07fea7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2473">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ae46f53a2cd3e92b5b3fff03c8010d61</data>
      <data key="v_content">gonow,Go on, go now before Ron.&quot;
&quot;Er -- okay,&quot; said Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ae46f53a2cd3e92b5b3fff03c8010d61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2474">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e14233e4893c59628c5867a7caea4024</data>
      <data key="v_content">73
He pushed his trolley around and stared at the barrier.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e14233e4893c59628c5867a7caea4024</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2475">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1e6920993d58ebd5cf8b45f510d516d1</data>
      <data key="v_content">He started to walk toward it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1e6920993d58ebd5cf8b45f510d516d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2476">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c2719485545a0da50bf4ef874780949f</data>
      <data key="v_content">People jostled him on their way to
platforms nine and ten.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c2719485545a0da50bf4ef874780949f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2477">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0c3bc0bf455b5f129888117ab742aa77</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was going to smash
right into that barrier and then he&apos;d be in trouble -- leaning forward
on his cart, he broke into a heavy run -- the barrier was coming nearer
and nearer -- he wouldn&apos;t be able to stop -- the cart was out of control
-- he was a foot away -- he closed his eyes ready for the crash --
It didn&apos;t come...</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0c3bc0bf455b5f129888117ab742aa77</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2478">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8cdee50d23acaf065d27a0e64d34f067</data>
      <data key="v_content">A scarlet
steam engine was waiting next to a platform packed with people.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8cdee50d23acaf065d27a0e64d34f067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2479">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3823c724178413ce78ff80c837fcd1e8</data>
      <data key="v_content">A sign
overhead said Hogwarts Express, eleven O&apos;clock.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3823c724178413ce78ff80c837fcd1e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2480">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1624f3617285a36517dbba65a33b40a7</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry looked behind him
and saw a wrought-iron archway where the barrier had been, with the
words Platform Nine and Three-Quarters on it, He had done it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1624f3617285a36517dbba65a33b40a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2481">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0247bd4fc4b808cb4605962c3b4ee3d6</data>
      <data key="v_content">Smoke from the engine drifted over the heads of the chattering crowd,
while cats of every color wound here and there between their legs.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0247bd4fc4b808cb4605962c3b4ee3d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2482">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f2103d7400700828993feeb40391202d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Owls
hooted to one another in a disgruntled sort of way over the babble and
the scraping of heavy trunks.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f2103d7400700828993feeb40391202d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2483">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0918e36ad569834ed6b980bc9d9f274a</data>
      <data key="v_content">The first few carriages were already packed with students, some hanging
out of the window to talk to their families, some fighting over seats.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0918e36ad569834ed6b980bc9d9f274a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2484">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2e0b9a4d65105da56a8200120e7b396c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry pushed his cart off down the platform in search of an empty seat.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2e0b9a4d65105da56a8200120e7b396c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2485">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c9b0ec474607cc772e76890e57efeb87</data>
      <data key="v_content">He passed a round-faced boy who was saying, &quot;Gran, I&apos;ve lost my toad
again.&quot;
&quot;Oh, Neville,&quot; he heard the old woman sigh.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c9b0ec474607cc772e76890e57efeb87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2486">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f82ccacdfae72a2e82d27c627a43c874</data>
      <data key="v_content">A boy with dreadlocks was surrounded by a small crowd.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f82ccacdfae72a2e82d27c627a43c874</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2487">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0ebfbbc8df8accfd4a882bf5659f1d9e</data>
      <data key="v_content">,&quot;Give us a look, Lee, go on.&quot;
The boy lifted the lid of a box in his arms, and the people around him
shrieked and yelled as something inside poked out a long, hairy leg.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0ebfbbc8df8accfd4a882bf5659f1d9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2488">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f1996577ce6eaee4f4b5f50f65b45e99</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry pressed on through the crowd until he found an empty compartment
near the end of the train.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f1996577ce6eaee4f4b5f50f65b45e99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2489">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0f391f00cc24ef4c0d7fa3d550456539</data>
      <data key="v_content">He put Hedwig inside first and then started
to shove and heave his trunk toward the train door.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0f391f00cc24ef4c0d7fa3d550456539</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2490">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-55108093a419c1678aeb938c90d67e30</data>
      <data key="v_content">He tried to lift it
up the steps but could hardly raise one end and twice he dropped it
painfully on his foot.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-55108093a419c1678aeb938c90d67e30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2491">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-54866a209fea282fc9671abb645bf9d5</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Want a hand?&quot; It was one of the red-haired twins he&apos;d followed through
74
the barrier.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-54866a209fea282fc9671abb645bf9d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2492">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6ad1bf4b0a55a762e4fb949964182fb3</data>
      <data key="v_content">Fred!C&apos;mereand,&quot;Oy, Fred! C&apos;mere and help!&quot;
With the twins&apos; help, Harry&apos;s trunk was at last tucked away in a corner
of the compartment.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6ad1bf4b0a55a762e4fb949964182fb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2493">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-1cddf7c05763144bd6e790e5e121fb0e</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;saidHarry,pushing,&quot;Thanks,&quot; said Harry, pushing his sweaty hair out of his eyes.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-1cddf7c05763144bd6e790e5e121fb0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2494">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ea3e91b4c6f8e5b7c1b85827c5333d29</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;What&apos;s that?&quot; said one of the twins suddenly, pointing at Harry&apos;s
lightning scar.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ea3e91b4c6f8e5b7c1b85827c5333d29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2495">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2156ceeecea2f948453c66a154a0bd80</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;Are you
&quot;He is,&quot; said the first twin.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2156ceeecea2f948453c66a154a0bd80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2496">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-dadf8dc21fc2d1f937af5b4fdbb4b3ab</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Aren&apos;t you?&quot; he added to Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-dadf8dc21fc2d1f937af5b4fdbb4b3ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2497">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-d53f3885bec0aea03dd8f71b291a1f72</data>
      <data key="v_content">yes,I,&quot;I mean, yes, I am.&quot;
The two boys gawked at him, and Harry felt himself turning red.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-d53f3885bec0aea03dd8f71b291a1f72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2498">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-98fc2a12fc56f4db8f9be1afe5430163</data>
      <data key="v_content">tohisrelief,,Then, to
his relief, a voice came floating in through the train&apos;s open door.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-98fc2a12fc56f4db8f9be1afe5430163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2499">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e7f899f86f094d75c3081c27d8931beb</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Fred? George? Are you there?&quot;
&quot;Coming, Mom.&quot;
With a last look at Harry, the twins hopped off the train.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e7f899f86f094d75c3081c27d8931beb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2500">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ee44d070ef09794e1c6427982ec3a9ca</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry sat down next to the window where, half hidden, he could watch the
red-haired family on the platform and hear what they were saying.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ee44d070ef09794e1c6427982ec3a9ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2501">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-872155c2352dd1529099fc0d8fce8cda</data>
      <data key="v_content">Their
mother had just taken out her handkerchief.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-872155c2352dd1529099fc0d8fce8cda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2502">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3cadf69a217c609dbda12e7477ff031f</data>
      <data key="v_content">you&apos;vegotsomething,&quot;Ron, you&apos;ve got something on your nose.&quot;
The youngest boy tried to jerk out of the way, but she grabbed him and
began rubbing the end of his nose.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3cadf69a217c609dbda12e7477ff031f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2503">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0ee60fd5fe890eb949a1aca4def5bf01</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Mom -- geroff&quot; He wriggled free.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0ee60fd5fe890eb949a1aca4def5bf01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2504">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ddef0630dadc281b559b42bfac0da608</data>
      <data key="v_content">hasickle,75
&quot;Aaah, has ickle Ronnie got somefink on his nosie?&quot; said one of the
twins.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ddef0630dadc281b559b42bfac0da608</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2505">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-3a5f9458710b9e4b1395006c1e2de000</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;He&apos;s coming now.&quot;
The oldest boy came striding into sight.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-3a5f9458710b9e4b1395006c1e2de000</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2506">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f88d3d6bba7cd8c6e2cb02826c5c3023</data>
      <data key="v_content">He had already changed into his
billowing black Hogwarts robes, and Harry noticed a shiny silver badge
on his chest with the letter P on it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f88d3d6bba7cd8c6e2cb02826c5c3023</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2507">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4f3e84f4ab02467b3cf782ea2dbaea32</data>
      <data key="v_content">Mother,&quot;,&quot;Can&apos;t stay long, Mother,&quot; he said.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4f3e84f4ab02467b3cf782ea2dbaea32</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2508">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-e81214814e782bf6a6d54c9e3ed0aa25</data>
      <data key="v_content">the,&quot;I&apos;m up front, the prefects have got
two compartments to themselves --&quot;
&quot;Oh, are you a prefect, Percy?&quot; said one of the twins, with an air of
great surprise.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-e81214814e782bf6a6d54c9e3ed0aa25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2509">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-4c9c9a43ede1b4c40faf52b3c1ff734d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You should have said something, we had no idea.&quot;
&quot;Hang on, I think I remember him saying something about it,&quot; said the
other twin.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-4c9c9a43ede1b4c40faf52b3c1ff734d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2510">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-47a9d2160ea739c8f6edf990def0ab6d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Once --&quot;
&quot;Or twice --&quot;
&quot;A minute --&quot;
&quot;All summer --&quot;
&quot;Oh, shut up,&quot; said Percy the Prefect.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-47a9d2160ea739c8f6edf990def0ab6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2511">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-8fea8b2c31511d8599f851a35d75b200</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;How come Percy gets new robes, anyway?&quot; said one of the twins.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-8fea8b2c31511d8599f851a35d75b200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2512">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-db993fbb297dd0ab22298a9795b3b99b</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;,&quot;Because he&apos;s a prefect,&quot; said their mother fondly.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-db993fbb297dd0ab22298a9795b3b99b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2513">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9f5691dc32286f467b2529736a98f8d6</data>
      <data key="v_content">dear,well,,&quot;All right, dear,
well, have a good term -- send me an owl when you get there.&quot;
She kissed Percy on the cheek and he left.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9f5691dc32286f467b2529736a98f8d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2514">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6b129b5b14ee3c47447fb5419b2876d4</data>
      <data key="v_content">Then she turned to the twins.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6b129b5b14ee3c47447fb5419b2876d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2515">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2455f5bd701ce5a625d02f594ead21a1</data>
      <data key="v_content">youtwo--,&quot;Now, you two -- this year, you behave yourselves.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2455f5bd701ce5a625d02f594ead21a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2516">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-55355379c7e2a8fea16e6fa26edf463d</data>
      <data key="v_content">If I get one more owl
telling me you&apos;ve -- you&apos;ve blown up a toilet or --&quot;
&quot;Blown up a toilet? We&apos;ve never blown up a toilet.&quot;
76
&quot;Great idea though, thanks, Mom.&quot;
&quot;It&apos;s not funny.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-55355379c7e2a8fea16e6fa26edf463d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2517">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-29e94cea772ee010012547fa4071667c</data>
      <data key="v_content">And look after Ron.&quot;
&quot;Don&apos;t worry, ickle Ronniekins is safe with us.&quot;
&quot;Shut up,&quot; said Ron again.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-29e94cea772ee010012547fa4071667c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2518">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-11f5f7a5f9341398759179f85a2c2c21</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was almost as tall as the twins already
and his nose was still pink where his mother had rubbed it.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-11f5f7a5f9341398759179f85a2c2c21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2519">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c3c31ae71d319131c30c929eb93b0f6c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Mom,guesswhat?,&quot;Hey, Mom, guess what? Guess who we just met on the train?&quot;
Harry leaned back quickly so they couldn&apos;t see him looking.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c3c31ae71d319131c30c929eb93b0f6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2520">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c09fa78c3e9c95ceb8a504a3e96ba242</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;You know that black-haired boy who was near us in the station? Know who
he is?&quot;
&quot;Who?&quot;
&quot;Harry Potter!&quot;
Harry heard the little girl&apos;s voice.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c09fa78c3e9c95ceb8a504a3e96ba242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2521">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-27f5073c9005b8f35412d13d21c25275</data>
      <data key="v_content">Mom,canI,&quot;Oh, Mom, can I go on the train and see him, Mom, eh please....&quot;
&quot;You&apos;ve already seen him, Ginny, and the poor boy isn&apos;t something you
goggle at in a zoo.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-27f5073c9005b8f35412d13d21c25275</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2522">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-701ecc8dca85365baae5ef7987f58700</data>
      <data key="v_content">Fred?,Is he really, Fred? How do you know?&quot;
&quot;Asked him.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-701ecc8dca85365baae5ef7987f58700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2523">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-b4d60d9177d73e148c0579f4cd07899f</data>
      <data key="v_content">It&apos;s really there - like lightning.&quot;
&quot;Poor dear - no wonder he was alone, I wondered.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-b4d60d9177d73e148c0579f4cd07899f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2524">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-ec287726661f8405bd287944676d6c9c</data>
      <data key="v_content">He was ever so polite
when he asked how to get onto the platform.&quot;
&quot;Never mind that, do you think he remembers what You-Know-Who looks
like?&quot;
Their mother suddenly became very stern.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-ec287726661f8405bd287944676d6c9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2525">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fb8b3562f32674711df9fe34c64aff9d</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;I forbid you to ask him, Fred.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fb8b3562f32674711df9fe34c64aff9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2526">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-24a025002ea6228110f149b6c6a15ddc</data>
      <data key="v_content">As though he needs
reminding of that on his first day at school.&quot;
&quot;All right, keep your hair on.&quot;
A whistle sounded.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-24a025002ea6228110f149b6c6a15ddc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2527">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-fa58f148099a5486c02441464230063a</data>
      <data key="v_content">77
&quot;Hurry up!&quot; their mother said, and the three boys clambered onto the
train.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-fa58f148099a5486c02441464230063a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2528">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-f0f7c27923ea018ee4fad8d5999a2c13</data>
      <data key="v_content">They leaned out of the window for her to kiss them good-bye, and
their younger sister began to cry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-f0f7c27923ea018ee4fad8d5999a2c13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2529">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-778f15d38c6326ddbd030faae6a7223c</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ginny,we&apos;llsend,&quot;Don&apos;t, Ginny, we&apos;ll send you loads of owls.&quot;
&quot;We&apos;ll send you a Hogwarts toilet seat.&quot;
&quot;George!&quot;
&quot;Only joking, Mom.&quot;
The train began to move.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-778f15d38c6326ddbd030faae6a7223c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2530">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-aaa8ad9cd756bafda2be9c7e0dcfa086</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry saw the boys&apos; mother waving and their
sister, half laughing, half crying, running to keep up with the train
until it gathered too much speed, then she fell back and waved.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-aaa8ad9cd756bafda2be9c7e0dcfa086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2531">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-cd06585033a355a0bd4aa337c24813de</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry watched the girl and her mother disappear as the train rounded the
corner.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-cd06585033a355a0bd4aa337c24813de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2532">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-2bc0e9207f276d6bc68a82b80c55de49</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry felt a great leap of
excitement.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-2bc0e9207f276d6bc68a82b80c55de49</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2533">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-c47072c7b95aaa0128fd229eb1cbddbd</data>
      <data key="v_content">He didn&apos;t know what he was going to but it had to be better
than what he was leaving behind.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-c47072c7b95aaa0128fd229eb1cbddbd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2534">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-0e53ece13d1c32d0cf4b9d327e5aea66</data>
      <data key="v_content">The door of the compartment slid open and the youngest redheaded boy
came in.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-0e53ece13d1c32d0cf4b9d327e5aea66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2535">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-9f9fef24b9b223ef2da0545e42d82c93</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Anyone sitting there?&quot; he asked, pointing at the seat opposite Harry.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-9f9fef24b9b223ef2da0545e42d82c93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2536">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6d53440a8d863cd8e4b5ddfc1830788f</data>
      <data key="v_content">&quot;Everywhere else is full.&quot;
Harry shook his head and the boy sat down.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6d53440a8d863cd8e4b5ddfc1830788f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2537">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-381729124a3f43e567426457fb3ccb08</data>
      <data key="v_content">He glanced at Harry and then
looked quickly out of the window, pretending he hadn&apos;t looked.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-381729124a3f43e567426457fb3ccb08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2538">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-6b067ac680354ffcdb57cdcaadff649f</data>
      <data key="v_content">Harry saw
he still had a black mark on his nose.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-6b067ac680354ffcdb57cdcaadff649f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2539">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-acdbd6697e7043cbf6d88b21eab2fc6d</data>
      <data key="v_content">Ron.&quot;Thetwins,&quot;Hey, Ron.&quot;
The twins were back.</data>
      <data key="v_name">chunk-acdbd6697e7043cbf6d88b21eab2fc6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n2540">
      <data key="v_hash_id">chunk-385b048a5d34bcd606b1ae8d7d996395</data>
